(Battambang): The Royal Government of Cambodia has expressed growing concern about the spread of drugs in Cambodia after criminals used Cambodia as a place to process and produce drugs and export them abroad.
Concerns arose after Cambodian police cracked down on a large drug trafficking site in Kampong Speu province's Oral district on December 12, 2021. During the crackdown on the large drug processing plant, the police confiscated more than 2 tons of processed drugs and intended to export them abroad.
In response to the new development of drug criminals by using Cambodia as a place to process drugs under the image of a fertilizer processing plant or other agricultural products, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that in a recent cabinet meeting, Samdech Request the ministries and institutions that have the right to issue the license to cooperate or be the chairman when cracking down on suspected drug-related sites.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized, "This synthetic drug is difficult to control because it is composed of chemicals and criminals import the ingredients little by little under the guise of processing into agricultural fertilizers, etc. When imported in all kinds. Instead of producing fertilizer, they produce drugs. "Obviously, like the crackdown in Oral district, Kampong Speu province, more than 80 tons of ingredients were found."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, who is also the chairman of the anti-drug campaign, stressed that if there is no support, cooperation or unity to fight drug crimes, it will be a big problem for the nation other than Defamation on the international stage is affecting Cambodia's human resources as drugs become more prevalent.
According to Prince Sar Kheng, of course, Cambodia does not want the drug problem to spread until it is too late, as in some countries that lead to the killing of drug criminals. He considers the killing of drug criminals to be a last resort, but does not mean that he supports the killings, which he does not mean that Cambodia should not be allowed to fall into such a situation.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also claimed that there are currently about 38,000 inmates in correctional centers across the country, of which 51% are drug inmates.
Please be reminded that on December 12, 2021, recently, the specialized police force of the General Commission of the National Police dismantled a large-scale drug processing case, in which the reserve criminals successfully exported and reached To seize more than 2 tons of ketamine (powder K) while the chemical composition up to 80 tons.
Unprecedented large-scale crackdown on drug offenses in Cambodia Police have arrested a group of four ringleaders, one of whom died in a gun battle during a crackdown last night. Midnight on December 12, 2021 along National Road 4, Kampong Seila District (Sre Ambel Intersection), Preah Sihanouk Province.
Tycoon Ung Bun Hov Organizes Khmer Traditional Ambulance Competition at Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): The traditional Khmer dong ambok competition was held on December 18-19, 2021 in Damnak Koh village, Po commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, organized by Mr. Oknha Ing Bunhov and his family. The tycoon and his team consisted of candidates from the arts group of the Ministry of Culture and teachers in the province, authorities and about 500 local people.
On the afternoon of December 19, 2021, Mr. Oknha Ung Bunhov, the host of the Khmer traditional ambok pun contest, stated that he had purchased 112 hectares of land in Damnak Kak village from the villagers and he would continue to buy more. To get a total of 120 hectares of land. For his vision and to prepare this area to become a center of Vipassana Dhurak, to build a pavilion, to build a school, to build a Buddhist school to promote the field of Buddhism, which is the national religion.
At the same time, he will organize this area to become a natural tourism area because this area is a golden mountain area with beautiful natural forests that can attract many tourists to visit to improve the lives of people. In Po and Chronok communes of Kampong Leng district, there is a prosperous life.
When the head of the Royal Government builds a bridge across the river through Kampong Leng district in the future, this area will be able to become a historical tourist site because this area also has many ancient temples that are the work of our Khmer ancestors, such as Prasat Pon. Listed in Chronok commune and so on.
Mr. Oknha continued that in order to disseminate the above plan, he also initiated the Khmer traditional dong ambok competition program in order to help preserve the cultural heritage of our ancestors so that the next generation of Cambodian children can understand about rice harvesting. Come and wash the rice to get good rice to eat.
According to the Organizing Committee of Dal Ambok Competition, the examination program lasts for 2 days and is divided into 3 sessions. The first part is on the 18th. Kantranh, Taing Krasaing commune, Teuk Phos district.
