(Islamabad): Most Muslim countries have pledged to establish a humanitarian fund for Afghanistan, where millions of people are facing famine and severe hardship during the winter. This was released by Reuters on Monday, December 20, 2021.
According to the Pakistani foreign minister, the humanitarian fund will be set up with the support of the Islamic Development Bank, but did not specify the amount, while the meeting also did not recognize the Taliban government in Afghanistan. A warning that the humanitarian situation in Afghanistan will worsen if humanitarian or emergency assistance is not addressed.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thai Rithy, Deputy Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, on December 20, 2021, confirmed to the Cambodian Freight Forwarders Association that the deep-sea port will facilitate lower shipping costs.
Mr. Thai Rithy stated this on the occasion of the representative of Mr. Lou Kimchhon, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, welcomed Mr. Chea Chandara, President of the Cambodian Freight Traders Association, who led the association's delegation through Mr. Hong Kim Hong, Chairman of the Working Group and Senior Advisor of the Association to visit and explore the economic potential of Sihanoukville International Port.
Welcoming the visit of the association's delegation, Deputy Director General Thai Rithy said that although Cambodia has been affected by 19 cases of rabies, the Royal Government's efforts to fight the disease have made Cambodia can reopen its economy and continue to grow. The revenue of Sihanoukville International Port will continue to increase in 2020 and 2021, with other countries in the region continuing to decline.
He also mentioned the deep-sea port development project, which could be a large port to facilitate transportation and reduce transportation costs to be low in the future.
Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Terminal in the first phase, with a length of 350 meters and a water depth of 14.5 meters, with a loan of more than 200 million dollars from Japan, will begin construction in 2022 and complete construction in early 2025. This has already achieved the design and is in the process of bidding.
When the deep-sea port is completed by 2025, it will be able to allow ships with a capacity of more than 4,000 containers to dock, at which time about 93% of ships in Asia will dock in Cambodia. Provide a lower shipping cost, which is estimated to be less than $ 200 per container.
Currently, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port can only accommodate only 18% of ships in the Asia-Pacific region, meaning that out of 100 ships, only 18 or 19 ships can dock and only 1,500 container vessels are allowed. .
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Chandara expressed his pleasure and pride to see the development of many port projects under the shadow of peace of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
After the presentation, the port team brought 15 delegates to visit the port. The Freight Forwarders Association is also very grateful for the warm welcome from Mr. Thai Rithy, Mr. Lou Kimchhon.
Please be informed that in the first nine months of 2021, Sihanoukville Autonomous Port received more than 254 billion riels or about 62 million dollars, compared to the same period in 2020, only more than 227 billion riels. Prey Veng Provincial Authority Holds Workshop on Dissemination of Gender Perspectives in Rural Development
