(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of December 20, 2021, continued to declare the fight against Kovid 19 as a priority issue that must go hand in hand with the reopening of the country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's announcement was made through a special voicemail, along with the announcement of the end of the "February 20 Community" event, an unprecedented large-scale 19 communicable disease event in the Cambodian community.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Today, I, Your Majesty, declare the closing of the February 20 community event, not by declaring the end of the fight against Kovid 19. "We have just announced the end of the February 20 event, but the fight against Kovid 19 is still a work in progress."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who has worked tirelessly in the fight against Kovid, stressed that the fight against Kovid 19 is a task that cannot be ignored and that no other events should occur.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on all people together with the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Health to participate in the prevention of Kovid 19 disease and call for a reduction in the number of deaths and a zero death rate. To continue through the efforts of each person, each family, each community to implement health measures.
The announcement of the end of the "February 20 community event" by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia after no more deaths due to Kovid 19, while only 7 new cases on December 19, 2021 yesterday Yesterday.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that this is a great success of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19. Samdech Techo emphasized, "It can be considered as a success or a reduction of failure due to Kovid 19, which I, Your Majesty, I always say no, the word success is just that the word damage is not great." "We have not been successful in this disease, but it can be said that it was a success in preventing us from falling into the abyss of death."
