Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum Receives Lao Ambassador
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Amphai Khin Davong expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the rapid progress of Cambodia, despite the recent crisis in Cambodia - Kovid-19. In addition, Cambodia is also a country rich in cultural treasures and heritage, especially Angkor Wat and Preah Vihear.
The ambassador stressed that the bilateral relations between the two countries have demonstrated close ties and cooperation through video conferencing meetings.
In particular, the exchange of visits of the leaders of the two countries, in which Dr. Phorn Kham Viphavan, Prime Minister of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, led a delegation to pay an official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia with remarkable results.
The Ambassador expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia for their support to Laos in the past, especially the financial support, vaccines and medical equipment.
The Ambassador noted that the two countries' parliaments have good relations and cooperation with each other, especially between the Cambodian Senate Friendship Group and the Lao National Assembly Friendship Group.
The Ambassador expressed his deep gratitude to the leaders of ministries, institutions at both the national and sub-national levels who have always provided good cooperation for the success of his diplomatic mission in the Kingdom of Cambodia. He hopes that the Senate, National Assembly, Royal Government and all national institutions of the Kingdom of Cambodia will continue to support the new Ambassador and the Embassy of Laos in Cambodia.
On behalf of the Cambodian Senate, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the Ambassador's successful diplomatic mission in Cambodia to strengthen friendship, solidarity and cooperation for the benefit of the people. Of both countries that have existed for a long time.
The President of the Senate noted that the Ambassador and the Embassy of Laos in Cambodia have good cooperation and relations with leaders, officials at all levels, ministries, institutions, provincial authorities, especially with the Cambodian people.
The President of the Senate thanked the Ambassador and the Embassy of Laos for their contribution to the Cambodian Senate's good relations and cooperation with the Lao National Assembly. The Cambodian Senate Friendship Group and the Lao National Assembly Friendship Group have maintained good relations and cooperation with each other over many activities, such as cultural exchanges, cultural exchanges and congratulatory messages on the occasion of the two countries' national holidays.
On behalf of the Senate and on his own behalf, the President of the Senate expressed his readiness to establish good cooperation with the new Ambassador of Laos and the Embassy of the Lao People's Democratic Republic in Cambodia.
Through the Ambassador, Samdech extended his deepest greetings and greetings to the top leaders of the Lao People's Democratic Republic.
The President of the Senate wished the friendship, solidarity and cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Lao People's Democratic Republic to last forever.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, confirmed that the Ministry will not relax the high school diploma exam (Bakdup) this year, both the level of discipline and discipline, despite the expansion. Outbreak of Kovid 19, which caused the school to close for a while.
He stressed that the organization of the exam according to the standard of the high school diploma exam is to make the high school diploma in Cambodia still valuable and quality, no matter when the exam.
He said this in a press conference on the process of preparing for the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination and Completion Exam Session: December 27, 2021 on December 20, 2021 at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
He acknowledged that students' education during the 19-year epidemic was not complete, but that the ministry had given students enough time to study when the school reopened.
He said that since the temporary closure of the school, the Ministry has encouraged teachers to focus on ninth and twelfth grade students by preparing brief lessons for students on the main subjects for the exam. At the same time, when the school is opened, the Ministry also requires the school management to assess the ability of students and to focus on where students are weak.
After the reopening of public and private schools in September, the ministry has given students four months to study more to prepare for the exam, which will be held at the end of the year, on December 27, 2021.
Education officials who misbehave, such as collecting money from students and giving answers to students, will be punished according to the Ministry's regulations, and if they make a serious mistake, they will be fired.
