(Phnom Penh): As of the night of December 19, 2021, the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of National Defense vaccinated 19,225,712 Kovid 19 vaccines to civil servants, citizens and the armed forces throughout the country. Including:
Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, together with Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia, Ms. Forfer Yuzat, UNICEF Representative in Cambodia, and Dr. Ly Ilan, WHO Representative in Cambodia, received the vaccine. At Phnom Penh International Airport.
This is the third time that Japan has provided Kovid-19 vaccine assistance through bilateral cooperation with the Kovak Center, including the first dose of 332,000 doses in the bilateral framework and the second dose of 668,000 doses within the framework. Kovak.
More than 300,000 doses of 19 million doses of Kovid vaccine have been delivered to Cambodia
The government and people of Japan have already provided about 1 million doses of the 19-strain Kovid 19 vaccine to Cambodia in July 2021. Vaccination assistance from the Government and the people of Japan, which arrived in Cambodia for the first time, was received directly by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
On the evening of December 19, the second visit will be received by Prof. Dr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, and Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, will represent Cambodia.
Mikami Masahiro expressed hope that the aid would further contribute to the steps towards social and economic recovery, as well as alleviate some of the concerns of the Cambodian people.
In the face of the spread of new infections that the world is facing, vaccination and strengthening the health system are a top priority for the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia. The Government of Japan is one of the countries that has actively contributed to the fight against the Kovid 19 epidemic with the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The Japanese ambassador said that so far the Japanese government has provided a total of more than 60 million US dollars in assistance to Cambodia, including the provision of medical equipment, hospital improvements, and support through international organizations for measures to prevent transmission. Border diseases, as well as the provision of facilities for the proper transportation and storage of vaccines.
The Japanese government has also provided about $ 227 million in loans to provide financial support to people affected by the 19 Koreas and to strengthen the health system.
Mr. Mikami expressed the Japanese government's commitment to continue to work with the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against the Kovid 19 epidemic. "In the fight against our 19 Kovid, Japan will continue to cooperate and work with Cambodia, our key friend," he said.
The Ambassador hopes that the global situation, including Cambodia, will improve in the near future and that the changing relations between Cambodia and Japan, as well as in the world, can resume.
Providing Kovid 19 vaccine to the people is the main strategy that the Royal Government of Cambodia has put forward to fight the Kovid 19 pandemic as well as protect the lives of the people from this pandemic.
Under a clear strategy and plan, Cambodia has become a country that can quickly find a vaccine for its people. So far, with the purchase of aid from friendly countries and the Kovak Center, Cambodia has received a total of nearly 41 million doses of the vaccine.
At the same time, the first and second doses were given to more than 14 million people, almost completed, and the third dose was given to more than 3 million people. Currently, Cambodia has more than 6.2 million doses of vaccine in stock.
So far, many countries are not getting vaccinated as planned. In particular, Cambodia is almost ready to supply the people with a lot of vaccines in stock, a testament to Cambodia's great success in vaccination policy.
Cambodia's success in finding vaccines and vaccinating people almost 100 percent faster than planned has led the World Health Organization, development partners and many countries to express their admiration and admiration for Led by the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on the fight against Kovid 19 and finding vaccines for the people.
The power of the vaccine, which the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, strives to deliver to the people, has freed Cambodia from the risk and epidemic of Kovid 19 and is reopening social activities.
