Three armed robbers shot and robbed two young men, but the police arrested two
(Phnom Penh): Two young men were chased by a group of three armed thieves armed with pistols on a motorcycle to shoot and rob a motorcycle, but failed.
In this case, the residents and the tricycle rider, in cooperation with the police force of the Po Sen Chey District Inspectorate, arrested two suspects, while another accomplice escaped. Police also confiscated a pistol and a motorcycle.
The above incident happened at midnight on December 18, 2021, along Russian Federation Blvd., Prey Chisak Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to Mr. Morn Vuthy, District Police Inspector, the suspects are: * 1: Name: Long Sotha, 19 years old, Occupation: Construction worker, living in a rented house in Thmor Koul 1 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh. * 2: Name: Soeung Samnang, 25 years old. Occupation: Phone repairman, living in Thmor Koul 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The victims are Moeung Villa, a 25-year-old male construction worker living in a rented room in Prey Tea 1 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, and Sim Sihong, a 25-year-old male construction worker living in Trapeang Chrey Village, Sangkat Kakap Ty 2 Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Mon Vuthy said that the story before the incident on December 18, 2021 at 1:30 am, the two victims rode out of a dance club. Khan Sen Sok to return to the rented room.
When they arrived at the scene, three suspects were riding a Honda motorcycle near the victim, and the suspects shouted to stop the motorcycle, with one of the suspects sitting in the back holding a belt and Another, sitting in the middle, pulled out a pistol, threatened the victim and fired two shots.
Fortunately, residents and tricycle riders came out to help in time and arrested two suspects along with exhibits at the scene. Another suspect escaped.
Authorities then intervened at the scene and brought the two suspects to the Po Sen Chey District Inspectorate for questioning and processing. As for the remaining factions, the specialized police force is continuing to search for them. More than 21,000 people evacuated as floods continue to hit Malaysia
