(Phnom Penh): Before stealing millions of dollars and jewelry from the house of the famous lotter, An Sieu Mey, four armed thieves disguised themselves as authorities and lied as enforcing the verdict Fake to get into the victim's house.
The robbery happened at 10:50 AM on December 19, 2021 at Villa V01 in Kork Chambok Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, with diamond jewelry worth about a million. Dollars.
Police said that the suspect, armed with one long weapon (MC) and three short weapons, loaded the victim with bullets, handcuffed and shocked the victim, and the victim, An Sivmoy, was taken to the first floor. Put the jewelry in the locker room and put all the jewelry in the black backpack that the suspect brought with him.
Police added that the total assets taken by the suspects were worth about $ 9 million (nine million dollars). They got into a car with their accomplices inside and fled, leaving behind only four handcuffs and a warrant.
After the incident, the joint police force, including the Po Sen Chey District Police Force, cooperated with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Force and the relevant specialized police force of the Ministry of Interior under the direct command of General Sant Dr. Bandith Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and Lt. Gen. Thet. The Phnom Penh Municipal Police, in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, is conducting a hot search operation to arrest the suspects.
So far, the cause of the crash has not been confirmed, while an investigation is underway.
According to the inspector, the robbery happened at V1, Borey Moon Town, Kork Chambok Village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, with four unidentified armed thieves.
At this time, the relevant authorities are conducting research and search operations for other information, and the details will be published by Fresh News later. Bailiffs, authorities and authorities implement a court order ordering an investigation into the current situation of Mr. Sam Rainsy's building in Chak Angre Leu commune
(Phnom Penh): Bailiffs, authorities and relevant authorities this morning, December 20, 2021, implemented the order of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, which ordered to investigate the current condition of Mr. Sam Rainsy's property in Chak Angre Leu commune. Former headquarters of the former CNRP.
Implementation of the Order to Investigate the Current Condition of Mr. Sam Rainsy Real Estate at 576, National Road 2, Prek Ta Kong Village, Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. Mony, Meanchey district governor, including Khan police force, Khan military police and village and sangkat authorities.
It should be noted that the Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on November 4, 2021, decided to forcefully sell the house of Mr. Sam Rainsy, the former headquarters of the former National Rescue Party to comply with the power of the final judgment. Civil compensation and legal penalties.
The decision to forcibly sell the house of Mr. Sam Rainsy in Sangkat Changre, Khan Meanchey was made after the request for the direct enforcement of the four Civil Parties and the four cases of the Phnom Penh Prosecutor's Office. After the losing party did not fulfill its obligation to pay compensation according to the final verdict three years ago and the final verdict.
The Civil Parties include: Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior, and a lawyer representing the Royal Government of Cambodia.
In the defamation case filed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen's lawyer, the court ordered Mr. Sam Rainsy to pay 4 billion riels in compensation. The final verdict in this case was issued by the Supreme Court on December 19, 2018.
In the case filed by the lawyer representing Samdech Heng Samrin, the court ordered Mr. Sam Rainsy to pay 4 billion riels in compensation. The final verdict in this case was issued by the Supreme Court on November 1, 2017. In addition, in the case filed by the lawyer representing Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, the court ordered Mr. Sam Rainsy to pay 2 billion riels in compensation. The final verdict in this case was issued by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on December 30, 2020.
Separately, in a case filed by a lawyer representing the Royal Government of Cambodia, the court ordered Mr. Sam Rainsy to pay 1,800 million riels in compensation. The final verdict in this case was issued by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on March 1, 2021.
The four "orders to start selling by force" issued by Mr. Im Vannak, Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court stated that: Creditors' application for compliance with Article 350.2 of the Code of Civil Procedure. Therefore decide:
1: Initiation of forced sale procedure, 2: Confiscation of immovable property with title deed, property No. 09725, dated 15 August 2007, issued by the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh, located in Sangkat Chak Angre Leu, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, which belongs to the debtor of the implementation, Sam Rainsy and his wife, Chulong Somura, to bring the money to pay the debt to the creditors of the implementation up to the full amount.
