Malaysia's worst floods force more than 30,000 people to flee their homes
Malaysia is hit by monsoons at the end of each year, and floods often force large-scale evacuations. Bad weather, combined with heavy rains since last Friday, has caused the river to overflow, flooding towns, cutting off many roads and causing severe traffic congestion.
In addition to the death toll, 239 others were injured and 52 were missing. Typhoon Rai hit the central and southern Philippine archipelago last Thursday, killing 208 people and making it the deadliest typhoon. In the year 2021.
Typhoon Rai also forced more than 300,000 people to flee their homes. Looking at the actual situation in the area that was hit by the typhoon, it reminds the Filipino people of the worst typhoon Haiyan in history in 2013, which caused more than seven Filipinos. 300 dead and missing.
Vietnamese President to pay two-day state visit to Cambodia from December 21-22
(VOVworld) - The new President of Vietnam Nguyen Xuan Phuc will pay a two-day state visit to Cambodia from December 21-22, 2021.
The President of Vietnam will arrive in Cambodia on Tuesday morning, December 21, 2021 at the invitation of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
During his state visit, Mr. Nguyen Suon Fuc will pay homage to the King of Cambodia, as well as meet with Cambodia's top leaders, including: Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Samdech Heng Samrin. President of the National Assembly. He will also bow to the two patriarchs.
In addition, the President of Vietnam and Samdech Heng Samrin will jointly preside over the groundbreaking ceremony for a new administrative building at the National Assembly building with the assistance of the Vietnamese government at a cost of about $ 25 million.
The Vietnamese President will also lay a wreath at the Independence Monument to pay tribute to the late King Norodom Sihanouk, former King of Cambodia, and to pay his respects at the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Palace.
