Ministry of Labor calls on NagaWorld workers to suspend strikes to maintain security, public order and prevent the spread of Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on December 18, 2021 issued a notice to workers of NagaWorld to suspend strikes and demonstrations to maintain security, public order and prevent the spread of disease. Kovid-19 disease.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor, in the past, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has made efforts to try to resolve labor disputes of NagaWorld in accordance with the legal procedures in force, starting with the conciliation mechanism by the Labor Inspector. Up to the Arbitration Council mechanism.
The Ministry claimed that the dispute was also resolved with the participation of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, but unfortunately due to some points agreed by the parties and some points are still not agreed. Therefore, during the prevention of the spread of Kovid-19, especially the new Kovid-19 virus, the Ministry calls on the workers who went on strike as follows:
1. To continue to discuss and resolve peacefully and maintain silence in accordance with legal procedures under the coordination of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the administration of Phnom Penh.
2. Suspend strikes and demonstrations to participate in maintaining security and public order and to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
3. The relevant ministries and authorities, especially the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, will continue to work in accordance with the legal procedures in force and based on equality to ensure that the workers who are protesting receive a solution that is appropriate and acceptable to all. .
