Thai authorities have been inspecting the damage on Saturday after about 400 inmates at the upper prison in southern Thailand have been rioting since Thursday night, demanding the release of inmates. Remove COVID-19. The prison has more than 2,100 inmates and about 300 have tested positive for the disease.
Thailand's prisons are overcrowded, making it difficult to control the spread of COVID-19, according to the Thai Department of Corrections, which holds more than 87,000 inmates. The disease has already infected 185 people, while almost 93 percent of Thailand's 281,535 inmates have been fully vaccinated.
Ministry of Public Works Prepares to Install Electric Charging Stations in Battambang and Siem Reap
(Battambang): In order to contribute to reducing carbon emissions into the environment, which is harmful to the environment and support for electric vehicles (EVs), the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is preparing a policy to support Cambodia. These electric powered vehicles (EVs).
In fact, officials from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, led by Mr. Chhuon Vorn, Director General of the General Department of Land Transport of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in three days from November 15 to 17, 2021 Professional officers, with the participation of representatives of the Department of Information Technology and Public Relations: Visited the feasibility of installing two electric car charging stations in Battambang and Siem Reap.
This inspection was made in accordance with the remarks of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, in a discussion on November 4, 2021 under the theme: "Electricity of vehicles for a green future for Cambodia ”with the participation of Mr. Pablo Kang, Ambassador of Australia to Cambodia and Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge.
The Senior Minister emphasized that the Ministry is developing policies and support for electric vehicles (EVs) and ensuring the overall infrastructure for EVs in Cambodia, including: charging stations, service centers, spare parts, staff. Train and dispose of batteries and ensure that EVs imported into Cambodia are of good quality.
According to the Lao Ministry of Culture and Tourism, the reopening of the country will be carried out in three stages. The first phase will run from January 1 to March 30, 2022, the second phase from April 1 to June 30, 2022, and the third phase from July 1, 2022. Continue.
Countries that can travel to Laos in the first phase include China, Vietnam, Cambodia, Thailand, Malaysia, Singapore, South Korea, Japan, France, the United Kingdom, Germany, the Netherlands, Spain, Italy, the United States, Canada and Australia.
As a first step, tourism will be restricted to group travel organized by tour operators licensed by the Lao authorities. Under the reopening plan, all tourists will be allowed to travel only to areas designated as green areas in Laos.
