Refugees from Myanmar to Thailand increase to more than 2,500 amid clashes between Myanmar military and ethnic forces
The KNU is one of the largest ethnic forces in Myanmar. They are based in the southeastern state of Karen and borders Thailand with a total population of 1.6 million. However, there have been no official reports on the number of casualties or damage caused by the fighting, according to local media reports. At least 18 people were killed.
Myanmar has plunged into chaos after Aung San Suu Kyi's civilian government was overthrown in a coup on February 1, 2021. Since then, a series of fierce protests and crackdowns have taken place in major cities, and it has become an opportunity for some ethnic militias to stand up against the Myanmar military.
