China remains Russia's largest trading partner for 12 consecutive years, with bilateral trade reaching a new level in the near future, Commerce Ministry spokesman Shu Jueting said at a news conference. The first 11 months of this year were $ 130.43 billion, up 33.6 percent from the same period last year and 2.3 percentage points higher than China's average trade growth.
Shu noted that the Sino-Russian trade structure has improved and new business forms are emerging.
"China-Russia cross-border e-commerce cooperation has developed rapidly, with the construction of warehousing and e-commerce platforms in Russia progressing steadily to contribute to growth," the spokesman said. "Bilateral trade is sustainable."
From January to November, China imported 298.72 billion yuan worth of energy products from Russia, up 44.2 percent, and imported 26.57 billion yuan, up 21.7 percent.
