The first Japanese standard medical safe vegetable shop opens in Cambodia
Since vegetables are an essential part of the human body in daily life, this shop not only supplies safe vegetables but also supplies safe vegetables in accordance with Japanese standards. Pregnancy, diabetics and people who are losing weight.
Having his own farm in Battambang, which covers 1.5 hectares and Mondulkiri, which covers 3.5 hectares, the CEO of this Japanese company intends to expand the cultivation of Japanese standard vegetables in line with the goal of supplying vegetables to make the connection. Between vegetable producers who ensure real safety.
In addition, the company also trains Cambodians to grow cultivation techniques according to Japanese standards, which in the future, when there is more branch expansion, the company will collect from farmers to meet local demand and for export to international markets. Well.
Hean Vannhorn, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that now the Cambodian population is growing steadily from year to year and has a better life, so eating habits and habits have changed with their attention. Focus on the quality and safety of food, especially vegetables and fruits.
He said that The Fresh's initiative to prepare safe vegetables in accordance with Japanese standards is to process the use of vegetables with the highest efficiency, especially to guide customers to use vegetables for nutrition and to facilitate. You have a health problem that heals quickly and reduces the number of treatments.
