Commentary: China-Russia relations withstand all kinds of challenges and show new strength and vitality from day to day.
BEIJING, Dec. 15 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping met with Russian President Vladimir Putin on the afternoon of December 15, 2021 to exchange views on issues such as bilateral relations, practical cooperation, coordination and cooperation. International strategy and so on.
The "Winter Olympics" meeting between the two sides not only shows the deep ties between the two heads of state, but also testifies to the high level of political trust between the two countries. Both countries as well.
This is the second video meeting between the two heads of state in 2021 and the 37th meeting between the two sides since 2013. Under the guidance of top-level diplomats, Sino-Russian relations are at an all-time high in unprecedented history, and practical cooperation in all fields has yielded fruitful results.
(Siem Reap): The Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association's local relief mission extended to Banteay Srei district as two new-style fish tanks were handed over to two families in Trapeang Thmor village, Khun Ream commune, Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province in the afternoon. December 17, 2021 with the help of the Cambodian-Chinese Progress Researchers Association and other philanthropists.
Mr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, highlighted the two-year mission from the beginning of 2018 to the end of 2019 of the Peaceland Foundation of China, in collaboration with the Cambodian authorities to manage mine action and rescue people with disabilities. Mines to contribute to demining in Trapeang Thmor village.
He emphasized that with the support and attention of the Banteay Srei District Administration, the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association has cooperated with the Peaceland Foundation of China to provide two new aquariums to the people. Two families live in this village to improve the lives of people who have been affected by landmines and unexploded ordnance left over from the war.
He encouraged people in the community to continue to understand new methods of fish and animal husbandry to contribute to improving family life and meeting real needs in the community under the development of Banteay Srei district administration.
Sanh Tha, a representative of the family who directly benefited from the project to improve the family's livelihood, said he was very excited that he would apply the wisdom of the fish farming training at home and continue to share. With the villagers to contribute to the district administration in reducing poverty of the local people.
In addition, he continued to support and encourage Chinese civil society through the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association to continue the activities of this community development project in line with the policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
It should be noted that in addition to the mission of research, publishing and training, the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association has been mobilizing Chinese investors and civil society to contribute to the development and improvement of local people's livelihoods through the project. Improving libraries, small business projects, animal husbandry and family farming projects, and scholarship programs to study in China.
The Ministry of Justice has decided to establish the ASEAN Senior Officials in Law and Justice Group, chaired by Mr. Chin Malin.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice on Friday issued a resolution establishing a working group of ASEAN Senior Officials on Law and Justice to coordinate ASEAN affairs related to the field of law and justice.
The decision issued by Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on December 17, 2021, stated that the ASEAN Senior Officials in Law and Justice of the Ministry of Justice is composed of 13 members, with Mr. Chin Malin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice As chairman, accompanied by two vice presidents.
This team has the following tasks:
Coordinate ASEAN affairs related to law and justice
Coordinate and cooperate with the ASEAN-Cambodia Secretariat and the ASEAN Secretariat in the field of law and justice
Coordinate and cooperate with the specialized units of the Ministry of Justice on the preparation of legal documents and documents related to the ASEAN Law and Justice Cooperation Program.
Participate in and organize the ASEAN Legal Senior Officials Meeting, the ASEAN Legal Ministers' Meeting and other related meetings.
Prepare documents and coordinate the delegation of the Ministry of Justice to participate in various expert working group meetings and meetings related to ASEAN law and justice.
Study, research and document necessary for the development of legal and judicial development plans with ASEAN member countries and ASEAN partner countries.
- Coordinate work with relevant government ministries and institutions, development partners and civil society organizations related to ASEAN law and justice.
- Prepare annual budget and action plan related to the ASEAN Legal Senior Officials Meeting, the ASEAN Legal Ministers' Meeting and other related meetings.
- Monitor and evaluate and report on the progress related to ASEAN law and justice to the Minister of Justice
Perform other duties as determined by the Minister of Justice.
