Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works calls on vehicle owners to abide by the law on processing and transportation
(Preah Vihear): Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, Mr. Samleang Try, called on the owners of all types of vehicles that process and transport to comply with the law, that is, do not process incorrectly and do not overweight while one vehicle The team that complied with the technical specifications was followed by the team by cutting the cage on the spot and fined according to the law as well as making a contract.
Speaking to Fresh News Agency on the afternoon of December 17, 2021, Mr. Samleang Try confirmed that on December 16, 2021, the team of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province stopped a Samsung car that was working. Driving illegally while driving on National Road 62 in O Por village, Romney commune, Rovieng district, the team cut the cage on the spot with a fine and made a contract to stop the illegal processing.
Mr. Samleang Try stressed that from today, he will abide by the law, with the exception of cars that are not technically correct to drive on the road, will be immediately banned from traffic.
As for the overweight trucks, the fines will be enforced from December 21, 2021, because since the beginning of December, the O'Po-Preah Vihear overweight truck team has been working. Disseminate the announcement of the Ministry of Public Works so that truck drivers can understand and participate in the implementation.
He said that from December 21, 2021 onwards, the team at O'Po truck weighing station will start fining overweight trucks because the team did not fine in the past, despite knowing that That is overweight, but from December 21 to follow the law.
Dr. Sok Touch: Seoul needs to expand the "pillars of peace" of its new South-South policy beyond regional security issues
Dr. Sok Touch made the remarks at the closing ceremony of the International Conference on "New Context of ASEAN-ROK Relations" this morning, December 17, 2021, at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, ASEAN welcomes Korea's new South-South policy, which aims to deepen its relations in line with the three pillars of the ASEAN Community.
"Seoul needs to expand the" pillars of peace "of its new South-South policy beyond non-traditional security issues and take a more balanced and proactive stance in its participation," said the president of the Royal Academy of Cambodia. "It's in strategic and regional security issues."
In this regard, he said, Seoul has been striving to diversify its external economic relations, re-orient its diplomacy to Southeast Asia and beyond, and promote regional cooperation. Actively. However, Seoul's central power ambitions have been severely hampered by external geopolitical constraints as well as internal new policy-oriented internal settings.
(Battambang): The National Outstanding Working Group and Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross in Battambang Province on December 17, 2021 organized a get-together with 152 people living with HIV to participate in the World AIDS Day. December 1, 2021 under the theme "End inequality, end AIDS, end global epidemics."
The ceremony took place at Wat Roka in Roka village, Roka commune, Sangke district, Battambang province, presided over by Mr. Sok Lou, Chairman of Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, Dr. Teng Kunthy, Deputy Chairman of the National Outstanding Working Group and Dr. But Kim Sean. Permanent Vice Chairman of the Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and Chairman of the National Outstanding Working Group of Battambang Branch.
At the same time, he spoke about the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, who has a clear strategy and a long-term vision to irrigate 19 Kovid vaccine to people across the country. People living with HIV who are at risk of developing opportunistic infections should be vaccinated against Kovid 19 in all doses and doses as prescribed by the Ministry of Health.
At the same time, he called on all citizens to join the Cambodian Red Cross, national authorities, public-private institutions, philanthropists and partners from all walks of life so that we can all achieve the goal of the Royal Government of Cambodia to end the AIDS problem in 2025.
Dr. But Kim Sean also thanked Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for setting out a series of work strategies to successfully improve the health of people living with HIV, especially to reduce the transmission of HIV from Mothers to fetuses to contribute to the Royal Government to achieve zero goals by 2025.
