Return of Kayaka Volunteers to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia has been sending Korean volunteers to Cambodia since 2003 to share their knowledge, skills and experience to improve The lives and livelihoods of the people and to strengthen ties between the two countries.
People all over the world have been affected by the Kovid-19 virus. KOICA made a difficult decision to send 63 of its volunteers back to Korea in March 2020, and all volunteer activities were delayed due to the spread of the virus. .
The KOICA office in Cambodia believes in the Royal Government of Cambodia in managing the spread of the virus well, which is why KOICA decided to send eight Korean volunteers back to Cambodia.
KOICA's Cambodia office is a WFK Volunteer Program Implementation Agency, a program that sends Korean volunteers worldwide. As of December 2021, KOICA has sent 777 volunteers and consultants to Cambodia. So far, the volunteers have worked with at least 25 ministries and sub-national institutions in Cambodia in various fields.
