Please read the announcement below: The outgoing Lao Ambassador to Cambodia is amazed at Cambodia's progress and thank you very much for your help in combating Kovid 19
Mr. Kin Davong said this while he said goodbye to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the Peace Palace on Friday morning, December 17, 2021.
During the farewell meeting, Mr. Kin Davong thanked Samdech Techo Cambodian leaders as well as the Cambodian people for their good cooperation in successfully completing the diplomatic mission in Cambodia for the past three years.
Mr. Kin Davong also informed Samdech Techo that for more than three years, he has seen Cambodia develop steadily. I would like to congratulate the Cambodian people, the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially Samdech Techo, who has led Cambodia to rapid development.
The outgoing Lao Ambassador also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia for providing assistance to the people and the Government of Laos in the form of medical equipment, vaccines, vehicles and funds to fight the spread of disease. Kovid 19 in Laos.
Mr. Kin Davong emphasized that the Lao people, the Lao government is very happy and grateful for the sympathy of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia.
During the farewell meeting, Mr. Kin Davong wished Samdech Techo Hun Sen success in his chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Mr. Kin Davong's diplomatic mission in Cambodia, having done a lot of work to contribute to the expansion of friendship and cooperation between the two countries.
Regarding the assistance that Cambodia has provided to the people and government of Laos, Samdech Techo said that this is assistance to help the government and people of Laos who are in need.
