Cambodia is one of the largest countries in the world to vaccinate its 19 people against measles with the help of friendly countries and development partners, especially China. Cambodia has made an unexpected difference as Cambodia has higher vaccination rates than some of the richer countries, including the United States and the United Kingdom.
It is because of this feature that Cambodia's social and economic activities can be resumed in a new form of normalcy in the context of Kovid 19.
The National Assembly President warmly welcomed the newly appointed Ambassador to Cambodia, Mr. Zac Pele, and emphasized that the National Assembly of Cambodia was ready to facilitate cooperation for his diplomatic mission. Success.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin said that Cambodia and France have built relations and cooperation between them for a long time. This good relationship and cooperation has been continuously strengthened and expanded to date.
On that occasion, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei hoped that during his diplomatic mission, he would continue to contribute to strengthening, expanding and promoting the existing good cooperation to another level.
Mr. Zac Pele thanked the President for allowing him to pay a courtesy call at this time.
