(Banteay Meanchey): Police in Banteay Meanchey province on December 17, 2021 sent two brokers to the provincial court to take legal action for bringing illegal migrant workers to Thailand at Prasat Tbeng village, Banteay Chhmar commune. Thmor Puok District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Lieutenant Colonel Ros Dara, Deputy Commander of the 807th Border Guard Regiment, said that on the night of December 16, he led the police force in cooperation with the 1st Battalion military force to patrol the Cambodian-Thai border at that time. Two brokers and six workers, including three young children, were found trying to cross the border, and the force detained them and sent them to the police station for questioning.
Lt. Col. Ros Dara confirmed that the workers who cheated the recruiters said that their group consisted of three people, including three young children, who were taken to Thailand by the brokers to find work. One person, 1,000 baht, and was detained by the authorities.
After taking notes, the six workers, including children, were sent back to their homes at the Tbeng temple checkpoint, O Bei Choan checkpoint, while the two brokers were sent to court for further action.
