WASHINGTON (Reuters) - An engineer who worked for decades on a US defense contractor has been arrested for trying to pass on confidential information to a person he thought was a Russian agent but in fact an employee of an intelligence agency. The FBI. This was released by the AP on Friday, December 17, 2021.
The investigation into Rovi lasted eight months, beginning in March 2020. During that time, Rovi met and responded to several messages with FBI agents posing as Russian agents. Rovi provided information on US military fighter jets and expressed his intention to move to Russia.
