Samdech Techo Hun Sen Tells Thai Foreign Minister to Strengthen ASEAN Cooperation During Cambodia's ASEAN Chairmanship
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen told Thai Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Don Pramat Vinay that when Cambodia takes over the ASEAN chairmanship in 2022, Cambodia will work to strengthen friendship, solidarity and promote Better cooperation between ASEAN countries.
The emphasis of Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia to the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Thailand was made during a courtesy call and discussion at the Peace Palace on Friday morning, December 17, 2021. Don Pramat Vinay is visiting Cambodia as well as attending the 11th Cambodia-Thailand Joint Commission Meeting.
On the morning of December 17, the Thai Foreign Minister also paid a courtesy call and discussed with Samdech Techo Hun Sen. According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant to the Prime Minister, during this meeting, the Minister of Foreign Affairs greeted Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the priority work that Cambodia will fulfill during its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022.
In response to the Thai Foreign Minister's curiosity, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, emphasized that the priority work that Cambodia will strive to address includes: the fight against Kovid 19 to open the economy, society and connect people and People of ASEAN. In addition, as the chair of ASEAN, Cambodia will also strive to strengthen friendship, solidarity and promote cooperation between ASEAN countries.
In addition to ASEAN issues, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reaffirmed Cambodia's position on resolving maritime issues between China and ASEAN member countries. Regarding this maritime dispute, Samdech Techo made it clear that Cambodia will promote the implementation of the Declaration on the Resolution of the South China Sea Dispute (DOC) issued when Cambodia hosted ASEAN in 2002.
In addition, Cambodia will urge all parties to negotiate and will work to achieve a code of conduct in the disputed sea, known as the COC.
During the inauguration ceremony of Chip Mong's "Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh" Hotel on December 15, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that one of the priority tasks when Cambodia hosts ASEAN is to bring the country Myanmar returns to ASEAN forum
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his position on efforts to resolve maritime disputes between China and ASEAN member countries. However, Samdech Techo warned in advance not to blame Cambodia in case it could not be resolved. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that he did not want to throw "hot stones" on this maritime issue to Cambodia, but Cambodia can accept "hot potatoes".
It should be noted that in this morning's meeting, the Thai Minister of Foreign Affairs brought a message of congratulations and congratulations on the ASEAN chairmanship to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and also wished Samdech Techo success in leading ASEAN. .
The Thai Foreign Minister also congratulated Samdech Techo on successfully preventing the spread of Kovid 19. In particular, about 90 percent of the population was vaccinated against Kovid 19.
Mr. Don Pramat Vinay also expressed his congratulations to Samdech Techo for the rapid development of Cambodia. More than 500 light poles have been installed in Svay Rieng to light the road to reduce traffic accidents.
