National Bank of Cambodia and Central Bank of Laos agree on development of payment system with cross-border payment system connection
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has held a bilateral meeting with the Central Bank of Laos (BNC). With the connection of cross-border payment systems, strengthening cooperation in monitoring and continuing to share the experience of the National Bank of Cambodia on the development, printing of national currency and so on.
The bilateral meeting was co-chaired by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and Mr. Sonexay Sitphaxay, Governor of the Central Bank of Laos. The bilateral meeting is held annually to strengthen and expand cooperation and friendly relations between the two central banks.
The meeting praised the achievements of the close cooperation between the two central banks, which has contributed to the development of the banking system and support trade, investment and tourism in both countries.
The two central bank delegations exchanged views in an atmosphere of friendship and solidarity, and set tasks to increase cooperation next year, including the development of payment systems and innovation with payment system connectivity. Cross-border strengthening cooperation in monitoring and continuing to share the experience of the National Bank of Cambodia on the development of national currency printing.
Mr. Chea Chanto thanked the Governor of the Central Bank of Laos for attending the bilateral meeting in person and always supported the bilateral cooperation between the two central banks.
Mr. Chea Chanto said, "The presence of Cambodian banking institutions operating in Laos has really contributed to strengthening investment between the two countries. Currently, two Cambodian commercial banks are operating in Laos and one Lao commercial bank is present in Cambodia.
Please be informed that in 2021, the National Bank of Cambodia will share its experience and knowledge to the Central Bank of Laos on many topics, including: International Reserve Management, Liquidity Management, Banking System Development, Risk Management Banking. And account management system.
