(Phnom Penh): Cambodian-American citizen living in Washington, DC, Mr. Nav Vichea expressed his full support for the announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister of Cambodia to nominate Mr. Hun Manet as Prime Minister. Follow-up from the Cambodian People's Party. This Cambodian-American citizen sees Mr. Hun Manet as an unassuming, highly educated person who is most worthy to be the next leader of Cambodia.
On December 2, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen made a public announcement in support of Hun Manet, the eldest son of Samdech, the Cambodian People's Party's candidate for the next Prime Minister. Samdech Techo Hun Sen reaffirmed on December 9, 2021 that the candidacy of the Prime Minister will be officially decided at the meeting of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party on December 24, 2021. .
Not only is he a graduate of an internationally renowned school, Mr. Hun Manet is an intellectual who has been involved in practical work for many years in both the Party, the military and the humanitarian framework. In particular, Mr. Hun Manet is an intellectual trained and experienced by another strong professor, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, his father.
All these points led to the announcement of Mr. Hun Manet as the candidate for Prime Minister from the Cambodian People's Party received strong support from the leadership and members of the Cambodian People's Party. Not only the leaders, party members, Cambodian people, civil servants, the armed forces have all expressed support for the presence of Mr. Hun Manet as the next Prime Minister.
In addition to the people in the country, Cambodians living in the United States have also expressed their satisfaction with Hun Manet's candidacy for the next prime minister.
Mr. Nav Vichea, a Cambodian-American living in Washington, D.C., noted that Mr. Hun Manet is the perfect candidate for Prime Minister because he has a high level of knowledge that can lead the nation to progress. The Cambodian-American stated that Mr. Hun Manet is qualified to be the next leader.
Mr. Neav Vichea also noted Mr. Manet's attitude when participating in activities with Mr. Hun Manet while working in the United States. Mr. Vichea saw Mr. Hun Manet as a person with an unassuming personality, even though he was the son of a national leader.
Mr. Vichea noted Mr. Manet's character like this: "He is an ordinary person, he does not think we come from any side, as long as the Cambodian people, he loves all. "He never thought he was the son of a high-ranking prime minister. He never boasted. He was not arrogant. He always communicated with the people in a friendly manner."
Please note that Mr. Hun Manet, 44 years old, currently serves as Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Cambodian Army. In terms of politics, Mr. Hun Manet is the youngest member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and he is also the Chairman of the Central Youth Committee of the Cambodian People's Party.
