(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, in a cabinet meeting led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has decided to set its position on the Indo-Pacific Initiative, a policy to counter China's Belt and Road Initiative.
According to the results of the Cabinet meeting, in the meeting of the Council of Ministers on December 16, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen set three principles as a compass for supporting the Indo-Pacific Initiative with the United States as a big brother. This.
The three principles are: First, to benefit peace and development, second, not to oppose any country, and third, to respect and provide support for ASEAN Centralism and ASEAN Indo-Pacific philosophy.
The Indo-Pacific Initiative is a policy initiative of four allied countries: the United States, Japan, Australia and India. The initiative is seen as a policy to counter China's expanding influence through the Belt and Road Initiative. Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach Burkri Appoints Chea Sang Dara as Personal Advisor
