(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has announced his commitment to protect the Tonle Sap Lake.
The announcement of the commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made at the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers this morning, Thursday, December 16, 2021.
On November 28, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued an urgent order to study, research and transport back the flooded forest land around Tonle Sap Lake, Kampong Chhnang Province, Pursat Province, Battambang Province, Banteay Meanchey Province, Siem Reap Province. And Kampong Thom Province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he will take strict legal action without exception for those who encroach on the flooded forest land if they refuse to return it to the state.
The order came after Mr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, went to study and found that thousands of hectares of flooded forest land around the Tonle Sap Lake had been encroached upon.
Immediately after Samdech Techo Hun Sen's hot order was issued, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara decided to set up a working group to visit and inspect the flooded forest lands in the six provinces around the Tonle Sap Lake. Also.
The group that invaded the flooded forest land was found to include government officials, the armed forces, traders and ordinary people. After the announcement of the order of Samdech Techo Chon, who occupied and encroached on the flooded forest land, announced the return of the land.
So far, no official report has been released on how much of the flooded area has been reclaimed. According to Mr. Sok Touch, tens of thousands of hectares of flooded forest have been encroached upon.
