(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 16, 2021, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army, met with Mr. Nikolai Patrushev, Secretary of the Security Council of the Russian Federation, who led the delegation. Senior member of the Security Council of the Russian Federation pays an official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
He also expressed regret over the disruption of cooperation activities in the past two years due to the Kovid-19 disease, hoping that from now on, things will be able to move in the right direction. Plan laid out.
On that occasion, General Oleg Salyukov, Commander-in-Chief of the Russian Army and a member of the delegation, thanked Hun Manet for focusing on strengthening cooperation between the two countries' Armed Forces. And confirmed the constant readiness to implement cooperation activities, especially to assist the Cambodian Army in training human resources in various fields.
In 2022, the commanders of the two countries' Armed Forces are scheduled to meet again to sign a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on Cooperation between the Cambodian and Russian Armed Forces, which is an important basis for promoting The momentum of cooperation between the two countries' armies has been strengthened.
