PRISME is a new, innovative and best-in-class entrepreneurship program that aims to build, develop and empower positively impacted, hybrid enterprises that integrate mission into business and focus on meeting social needs. Using entrepreneurial energy and marketing strategies to demonstrate that profitability and positive impact on society are not separate concepts.
These concepts are environmentally friendly and use the Sustainable Development Goals as a framework for decision-making and action.
The Memorandum of Understanding on Tripartite Cooperation was signed on December 15, 2021 by Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurship, Ms. Phean Sophoan, Director of Oxfam and Mr. Van Vichet, Managing Director of Partnership between Public and private sectors of Platform Impact.
Ms. Phean Sophoan said, “Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) have played an important role in driving Cambodia's economic growth by providing jobs and generating income for low-income people, as well as in making an impact. To society and the environment. However, small and medium enterprises are facing many challenges that require both technical and financial support to develop their potential.
Dr. Chheang Vann Monin said, “Small and medium enterprises are the catalyst for the Cambodian economy to move forward in a new competitive market. The program will not only promote small and medium-sized enterprises involved through skills training and operational development, but also expand their business to the next level by investing and reaping the benefits of National and regional networks. ”
This partnership demonstrates the commitment of stakeholders from the public, private and development sectors to support the entrepreneurial ecosystem to accelerate and increase revenue for the Cambodian economy.
PRISME provides two types of services to positively impacted enterprises, including supporting business ventures, developing growth strategies and building relevant business relationships for their businesses to grow, and supporting fundraising. Increase the capital they need to expand their operations and have a positive impact on Cambodia.
PRISME also aims to develop policies, frameworks, regulations and laws that enable a strong ecosystem to accelerate the growth of small and medium-sized enterprises that have a positive impact on Cambodia.
Mr. Van Vichet said, “Small and medium enterprises in Cambodia are facing a competitive environment where they have to create a niche market to expand their market and their products or services. "As well as linking the garment industry to ethical work standards three decades ago, which has continued to serve the industry, local enterprises must strive to incorporate environmentally friendly business models into their business activities."
PRISME aims to enhance the competitiveness of local SMEs by connecting value chains, increasing market access and financing, business efficiency, as well as integrating environmental, social and governance components. This will put Cambodia on the map of ecosystems that improve the environment, society and governance in the near future.
Mr. Sok Khorn stated that under the wise leadership of Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Chairman of the Management Committee of the National University of Battambang, decided to open a Chinese language department for the purpose of training students and the public to respond to High demand for labor market and growing investment volume of leading Chinese companies in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Khorn added that the Chinese language skills have been officially approved by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports through Prakas No. 1157 IK. Translated on December 7, 2021 on the creation of new majors at the National University of Battambang.
Prof. Dr. Wang Jianian said that the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang has trained Chinese language courses for more than 300 students and staff and organized 10 cultural exchange activities as a bridge. Establish a good friendship between the people of Cambodia and the people of China.
He said China will accelerate and expand the process of opening up education to the outside world through a three-pronged model of cooperation in language teaching, vocational training and education. The job market. Teaching Chinese will help students in the job market opportunities and help develop the National University of Battambang now and in the future.
He added that the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang will continue to promote all-round cooperation in the field of Chinese language education and other essential skills to build a bridge of sincere friendship between China and Cambodia and contribute to the development of our two countries. Got better.
It should also be noted that the Chinese Department is one of the departments under the Institute of Foreign Languages of the National University of Battambang, including the English Department, the Korean Department, the French Department and the Thai Department.
Entrepreneurship Development Fund of the Ministry of Economy looks at the contribution to increase the price potential of Cambodian agricultural products from the Chinese company "Hun Ti Group"
(Phnom Penh): The Entrepreneurship Development Fund is a public fund under the Ministry of Economy and Finance established to seek and provide support to potential entrepreneurs in Cambodia, especially those who are working to solve barriers and Expansion of its business.
Through research on a number of key agricultural products to meet the needs of export markets and interviews with a number of local entrepreneurs, the Entrepreneurship Development Fund sees Ti Group as a company with entrepreneurial ideas. New initiatives with a high conscience, with clear business objectives and the most unique technical capabilities to contribute to the preservation of the value of Cambodian agricultural products.
The company owner has more than 30 years of experience in this business abroad, especially in countries in East Asia, South Asia and the Middle East. When visiting Cambodia for the first time in 2013, the team decided to start investing and building cold storage for warehouses and investing in equipment with a total investment of up to 15 million US dollars.
Experts in the field generally recognize that cold storage is one of the key infrastructures to address the constraints on the value chain of agricultural products, especially in developing countries such as Cambodia.
However, despite the investment in cold storage, warehousing with modern technology and experts, it is not possible to guarantee a complete solution to the constraints and challenges in this field to achieve one goal is to increase value added. To Cambodian agricultural products above the current market price.
1: What motivated you to start a business in Cambodia?
Ty Group also sees this opportunity to become a pioneer in agriculture. We love to take Cambodian agricultural product standards to the next level and bring new food processing models to Cambodia based on our more than 30 years of experience in this business.
2: What is the importance of your project to Cambodian agricultural products?
Example: The Ty Group's cold storage warehouse, located in Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, was built in 2016 on an area of 2 hectares and is currently the largest warehouse for traders. All. By 2020, the cold storage will hold up to 10,000 tons per day, and the demand for cold storage will increase year by year.
3: What do you think about the strategic direction of agricultural development in Cambodia?
Therefore, our company plans to open a well-functioning industrial park to support agricultural products. At the same time, Hun Ti Group has accelerated the construction of local construction sites in Kampong Seila, applied for various licenses and requested policy support to operate smoothly and can be guaranteed in accordance with the conditions of foreign customers. We aim to initiate another project, the Free Trade Area for Agricultural Products.
Ongoing services include: production, processing, freezing management, import and export trade, logistics and distribution, e-commerce, information exchange, food safety testing, cooperation Agriculture and trade, fruits and agricultural products for foreign markets (meat and fishery products) and frozen food.
In addition, the company will bring leading enterprises into the country to integrate with the Trading House and will do its best to ensure food standards for local and international markets, and become As a food marketing distribution center in Cambodia and in Southeast Asia.
The industrial park will enhance all aspects of Cambodia's agricultural products in the region and internationally, attract food processing operators and compliant traders of industrial food safety, attract investment in technology and science, agriculture and modern food, establish a museum. National for showcasing Cambodian agricultural products, and the food industry training center.
Through the interconnectedness of supply chain integration, the project will be a provincial and Cambodian economic center that will help transform the traditional agricultural economy into a model of an agricultural economy using technology. Modern with high productivity, value added and rich diversification of Cambodian agricultural products.
This will help boost the export trade of enterprises participating in the industrial park and help transform Cambodia into a world-class exporter of agricultural products.
