France pledges to increase concessional credit and seeks to mobilize grant funding to help revive Cambodia's economy after Kovid 19 crisis
This confirmation was made during a working meeting with Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance on the afternoon of December 15, 2021. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy, which was received by Fresh News on December 16.
In fact, in 2021, France and Cambodia signed two co-financing agreements worth a total of 20.30 million euros to support the development of agriculture, water and the fight against climate change.
The French government, through AFD, has pledged to increase the size of concessional loans and to mobilize grant funding from the European Union and other sources to contribute to the development and recovery of Cambodia after the Kovid-19 crisis in line with national development policies and strategies. Of Cambodia.
Taking this opportunity, the Deputy Prime Minister also thanked the Government of the French Republic and the people of France once again for their continued support, both technically and financially, as well as for their cooperation. Good relations between Cambodia and France in the past and asked France to continue to help attract more French and European investors to invest in Cambodia.
