According to the South Korean ambassador, the Korean government has formulated new policies, especially seven existing policies and key points that the Korean government will strengthen closer cooperation with the nation. ASEAN as well as achieving future partnerships.
Park Ing-kyeung said the government of the Republic of Korea will continue to cooperate in ASEAN for the training community, the Center for Peace and Prosperity in the region.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Muth Chantha, a close associate of Mr. Kem Sokha, on Thursday came out to criticize Mr. Sam Rainsy again, saying that the leader of this opposition group is stupid but difficult to discipline.
The criticism comes after Sam Rainsy posted a statement that the planned visit of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Burma in January 2022 was "not representing Cambodia and ASEAN".
Through his Facebook page, Mr. Muth Chantha stated: "It is not necessary to read the full press release, just read a short post by Mr. Sam Rainsy and find that the above statement indicates ignorance and ignorance. "Diplomatic politics is the bilateral nature of sovereign states and the multilateral politics of regional organizations, especially the role of peace-loving member states of the United Nations."
The five-point agreement was approved by the ASEAN Leaders' Summit on April 28, 2021 in Jakarta, Indonesia, including the appointment of an ASEAN chair to chair Burma. According to the agreement, ASEAN has a role to play in finding a peaceful solution to the Burmese crisis aimed at restoring democracy, ending violence and human rights abuses.
It is a dark ignorance of political leaders to issue a political statement claiming that diplomatic intervention by sovereign states aimed at finding peace, ending violence and restoring democracy is illegal.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch chairs a meeting of the Board of Directors of the 4th Demining Project for Video Results to Review Achievements in 2021 and Action Plan for 2022
On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch praised the implementation of the demining project for its results and expressed his deep gratitude to the donor countries and development partners who have joined the Royal Government of Cambodia through the demining project. Mine for the fourth phase results include UNDP, Australia, the Republic of Korea and New Zealand.
The Senior Minister welcomed Allisa Chaker, Country Director of the United Nations Development Program (UNDP), as a strong partner in seeking support for demining projects for both financial and consulting results from 2006 to 2025.
The Senior Minister briefed the meeting on the results of Cambodia's successful development partners and friendly countries in demining Cambodia, despite the challenges facing the global Covid-19 disease. As of November 2021, Cambodia has cleared 153 square kilometers of landmines and explosive remnants of war, destroyed 2,026 anti-personnel mines, 372 anti-tank mines and 73,566 explosive remnants.
Australian Representative Ryan Tierney, First Secretary of the Australian Embassy in Cambodia, expressed his support for the project implementation process and confidence in the Mine Action Authority's ability to implement the project until 2025 and the coordination of UNDP partners in the fourth phase of demining. Will succeed according to the agreed plan. Australia will help plan for the fourth phase, although the world is diverting some of its funding to fight Covid-19.
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of a civil society in Cambodia, Mr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, expressed his commitment to increase cooperation with Chinese civil society to continue to improve the lives of Cambodians. Encourage Chinese civil society to continue to work closely with Cambodian civil society to continue to meet local needs.
The above encouragement to the Chinese side was made when Mr. Chea Monirith addressed the first dialogue on Cambodia-China cultural exchange relations organized by the Institute of Asian Studies of Beijing University of Foreign Languages this afternoon. December 16, 2021.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Monirith emphasized that culture is an important basis of human life. The dialogue will provide an opportunity for more scholars, researchers, investors and tourists to join forces with the government in national development. He supported the sharing of successful experiences of a new culture for humanity: peace and development.
Mr. Chea Monirith also highlighted the great achievements such as highways, bridges, roads, construction of many national and sub-national infrastructure projects with the help and contribution of the Chinese government, investors, tourism and civil society.
He said that in the spirit and willingness, support and contribution from Chinese friends have really contributed to improving people's lives, scholarships, business students and job creation, child welfare assistance and social protection. Cambodia's economic and social development would not be possible without the substantial and unconditional assistance of China, including the active participation of Chinese civil society.
The President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association also praised the achievements of the cooperation between the civil society of the two countries, especially between the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association and the Chinese civil society in Participate in meeting local needs in Cambodia, in addition to the great achievements that have emerged from the steel relations between Cambodia and China under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He also stated that the Cambodian Association of Progress Researchers was established in 2017, replacing the Cambodia-China Relations Research Group, which was established in 2008. For more than a decade of its establishment, the association has published a number of open scientific seminars, conferences, and conferences, both nationally and internationally, on Cambodia-China relations.
Not only that, the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association is also ready to coordinate and actively participate with Chinese civil society in participating in the development of Cambodia. Mrs. Tep Rainsy Sey Khieu Kanharith commended the teachers and school leaders for taking care of and helping to teach children with intellectual and autistic disabilities in Takhmao City
