(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Public Administration Reform Committee, chaired the second meeting of the Public Administration Reform Committee to discuss and promote the process of collecting additional inputs to be completed soon. The official document is the National Public Administration Reform Program for implementation from 2022 to 2035.
The meeting was held on the morning of December 15, 2021 online (Zoom) with the participation of committee members who represent all ministries, institutions at the national level and the chairperson of the Public Administration Reform Working Group, who is the governor. Or representatives of the 25 provincial administrations, including relevant professional officers at the national and sub-national levels, a total of 150 participants.
In his opening remarks, Minister Prum Sokha, Chairman of the Public Administration Reform Committee, gave an optimistic assessment of the progress of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Public Administration Reform Program under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Operating from 1993 to the present.
Public administration reform plays a central role in building and strengthening the rule of law in Cambodia, building the capacity of state institutions and human resources in the public sector, as a strong support for the private sector and ensuring the normalization of people's lives. Strengthening the causes of peace, progress, welfare and prosperity of the society.
Closing remarks, Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Public Administration Reform Committee, reaffirmed the importance and significance of public administration reform in the high-level speech of Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Cambodia is "reform for life, not reform for death."
The Minister also stressed that the success of all reform programs depends on the active participation of all stakeholders at all levels, both at the national and sub-national levels, and with Support from the people and society as a whole.
Thirty Families in Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang II Receive Precious Humanitarian Donations from Samdech Kittipritthbandit
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 16, 2021, Mr. THEM Sam An, Governor of Boeung Keng Kang District and Sub-Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, distributed the precious humanitarian gift of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the people. There are 30 elderly families living in villages 2 and 3, Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang II, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
