China says Lithuanian diplomats' safety concerns are fabricated
BEIJING (Reuters) - Concerns over the safety of Lithuanian diplomats in China are baseless, the Chinese Foreign Ministry said on Thursday. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, December 16, 2021.
Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin made the remarks at a briefing in Beijing a day after Lithuanian diplomats and their entourage left. From China urgently due to security concerns and threats.
A source close to Reuters reported on Wednesday that a total of 19 diplomats at the Lithuanian embassy in Beijing and their subordinates had left for Beijing. Paris, France, citing their departure due to security concerns and threats.
China downgraded diplomatic ties with Lithuania in November after the Baltic states allowed Taiwan to open a representative office in its capital.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol: The private sector is the engine of Cambodia's economic growth The Royal Government acts as a facilitator
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, stated that the private sector is the engine of Cambodia's economic growth, the Royal Government has acted as a facilitator, not the boss of the private sector. Success.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this on November 14, 2021 on the occasion of being the guest speaker at the Annual Meeting of the United States Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia with the participation of Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union. The Youth Federation of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Cambodian Mine Authority, Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and leaders of the Ministry.
The Senior Minister further noted that peace and political stability under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen are indispensable factors in attracting foreign investors, creating jobs for the people, attracting tourists to visit Cambodia. Agricultural markets have contributed to the national economic growth of around 7% in the last 20 years.
In addition, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also thanked the private sector, especially the United States Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, for standing with the Royal Government of Cambodia during the difficult period of the Kovid-19 crisis to contribute to economic development. Cambodia will also highlight the role of the Royal Government of Cambodia in facilitating the business of the private sector in Cambodia.
South Korean government to speed up internal free trade agreement (FTA) between Korea and Cambodia soon
(Phnom Penh): The Korean government will soon expedite the internal procedures for a free trade agreement (FTA) between Korea and Cambodia, said Park Ing-kyung, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia.
Bilateral trade relations between Cambodia and Korea have been running smoothly. In fact, in the first eight months of 2021, from January to August 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and Korea reached more than 514 million US dollars, an increase of 11.52% compared to the same period in 2020.
In the first eight months of 2021, Cambodia exported more than 129 million US dollars to Korea, while imports from Korea amounted to more than 385 million US dollars.
Cambodia's exports to Korea include garments, electronics, footwear, beverages, rubber bags, medicines and cardboard, etc. While Cambodia imports most of its goods from Korea, such as textiles, trucks, beverages, electronics, machinery, home decor, medicines, soaps and plastic products.
"In terms of mutual prosperity, Korea will expedite our internal procedures for the early entry into force of the Free Trade Agreement (FTA) between Korea and Cambodia," said the Ambassador of the Republic of Korea. This.
Park Ing-keng said that with the comprehensive partnership at the ASEAN level, the Korean and ASEAN governments will sign on January 1, 2022, which will see the flow of people between ASEAN and the Republic of Korea. Increasing trade volume to strengthen the Korea-ASEAN peace community and strengthen security cooperation with ASEAN, such as climate change, climate change and demining management.
"Next year, the Korean government will hold a dialogue with the Cambodian government on win-win cooperation with Cambodia. We will build prosperity in the region," he said.
The ROK Ambassador added that Korea will strengthen sub-regional cooperation, especially narrowing the regional development gap among ASEAN countries. Decided not to withdraw cooperation until 2022.
"We also strengthen the climate sector as well as disaster management. We will establish cooperation next year to expand on other security challenges. Korea will continue to assist ASEAN in organizing bilaterally or multilaterally." . This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Park Ing Kyeung.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh, seeing the need for globalization, especially after the inauguration of President Moon Jae-in, Korea has introduced an additional policy to strengthen ties with The countries in Southeast Asia are the "New South Policy" with three main pillars or 3P: people, prosperity and peace.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh stressed that the new South-West policy will be an important tool for coordination and a mechanism to strengthen closer ties between ASEAN and the Republic of Korea so that Korean influence can be firmly rooted. In ASEAN, both now and in the future.
The President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia continued, "If we talk about the framework between Cambodia and Korea, even though our two countries are far apart, we have the same will, it is this will that has brought us closer. Let us work for the benefit of mankind on earth.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in front of Mr. Moon Jae-in, President of the Republic of Korea at the 22nd ASEAN-ROK Summit held on video, expressed his pleasure at the signing of the trade agreement. Free trade between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea on October 26, 2021.
Samdech Techo expressed strong belief that this free trade agreement will be an important driving force in boosting trade and investment flows between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea.
For the negotiation of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement, the aim is to strengthen the economic partnership and expand the liberalization of bilateral trade by providing mutual benefits to enhance the economic interests and well-being of the people and Business of both countries.
The agreement will further boost Cambodia's exports to the Republic of Korea on goods previously exported, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
