(Phnom Penh): In the first 11 months of 2021, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia collected 2065 million dollars for the national budget. This was confirmed by Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on December 15, 2021.
According to the Minister of Finance, for the management of 2021, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia must collect revenue of 2,363 million dollars. But this revenue collection may not go according to plan.
The minister expects that by 2021, the General Department of Customs and Excise will be able to collect 97 percent of the plan, equivalent to $ 2.3 billion.
At the same time, Mr. Kun Nhem confirmed the trend of increasing the revenue from customs duties at the end of 2021 after the Royal Government reopened the economy and the demand for imported goods also increased.
Please be informed that tax is the main source of national income with two sources: first: internal tax revenue as tax revenue and second: customs tax revenue. In the first 11 months of 2021, the General Department of Taxation collected 2,560.12 million USD, an increase of 14%. Thus, the total revenue from both customs and excise Cambodia received tax revenue of 4,625 million US dollars.
