50 million and 800,000 What do these two serious figures mean? The first figure is one-fifth of the total 19 cases of Kovids found worldwide, and the second figure is the total number of Kovid 19 deaths, which is more than the sum of World War II deaths. The First World War, the North Korean War, the Vietnam War, the Iraq War and the Afghanistan War.
Recalling the whole process of the outbreak and spread of Kovid 19 in the United States, the outside world can easily see that from the beginning, Kovid 19 prevention work failed because politicians thought only of results. Political interests. In the run-up to the general election, the previous president of the United States rejected the scientific prevention of Kovid 19 and put political interests above the lives of the people.
In order to divert the conflict abroad, the current US leaders have resorted to the so-called "political search for the origins of the Kovid 19 virus" in a way that puts the blame on other countries, which has severely hampered the prevention process. 19 American Kovid disease. Many American media outlets have suggested that if the United States could fight the disease scientifically, many people would not have to sacrifice their lives.
In addition, many enterprises have closed, causing many Americans to lose their jobs for a long time. Monetary policy has pushed inflation higher. The US CPI in November rose 6.8 percent from a year earlier, the highest level in nearly 40 years. It is clear that such a situation makes the American people increasingly worried and hopeless.
The 19 epidemics of Kovid have exposed controversy in all areas of the United States, including politics, economy and society, which have become a magnifying glass of the flaws of American democracy. According to France's Le Monde newspaper, the 19-crisis Kovid crisis has exposed the fragility of American-style democracy.
The 50 million and 800,000, both serious figures, once again gave a warning to politicians in Washington. They should focus on the health and safety of the people as a priority and put the people first.
