Customs chief hopes that Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal will encourage tax-free car owners to pay more tax
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, expressed his expectation that the call of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to tax-free car owners who take refuge under the label Numbers Please hurry to pay the tax on time of the 10% tax preference, which must be completed by December 31, 2021, will make tax-free car owners hurry to pay more taxes.
Kun Nhem made the remarks at a press conference on December 15, 2021.
Mr. Kun Nhim said, "This morning, at the inauguration ceremony of the Hyatt Regency Hotel in Phnom Penh, Samdech Techo urged and urged duty-free car owners to come in and pay their taxes on time. He said that with only 15 days left, the 10% tax preference will expire. "This is a very important message to remind and urge car owners who have not yet paid their taxes to hurry up and pay their taxes on time."
He added that Samdech Techo Hun Sen further stated that from January 1, 2022 onwards, the tax duty is no longer favorable, having to pay 100 percent tax.
"This is an important message, so we expect that according to Samdech Techo's statement this morning, car owners are really in a hurry to pay taxes," he said.
At the same time, Dr. once again called on tax-free car owners to hurry up and pay the tax on left-hand drive vehicles before December 31, 2021 to get a 10% tax exemption.
He added that the crackdown on duty-free vehicles in the country has been suspended for a while to allow car owners to prepare their vehicles to pay taxes, but from January 1, 2022, the General Department of Customs will start cracking down on duty-free vehicles. Again, when suppressed, not only did not receive tax concessions, but also required to pay taxes and fines.
At the same time, the Minister also reminded that right-hand drive car owners have a chance to get 10% longer tax exemption than left-hand drive cars because right-hand drive cars need time to adjust the steering wheel, so the General Department of Customs has approved that car owners Taxes can be deposited from the start of the campaign until June 31, 2022.
After the expiration date, duty-free right-hand drive and left-hand drive vehicles will be actively and strictly cracked down on, especially right-hand drive vehicles, as right-hand drive vehicles are illegal in Cambodia's road traffic. When cracking down, there are two options: turn it into a spare part and destroy it at once.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, December 15, 2022, on the occasion of presiding over the inauguration of the "Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh" Hotel, Samdech Techo appealed to car owners duty free. Sheltered under various license plates, please come and pay the tax on time of the 10% tax preference, which must end by December 31, 2021.
Samdech stated that those who pay taxes after December 31, 2021 will not be favored, while Samdech will not let the same problem happen again to the users of tax-free cars and right-hand drive cars driving on the road. Road.
