Pailin Governor Calls on Hotel, Guesthouse and Restaurant Owners Not to Raise Prices on High School Diploma Exam Day
(Pailin): Ms. Ban Srey Mom, Governor of Pailin Province, called on the owners of hotels, guesthouses and restaurants not to raise prices on the day of the 2021 high school diploma exam. She said this in a meeting to discuss the work of the Higher Secondary Diploma in General Education and Completion on the evening of December 14, 2021.
In that, she has prepared a plan to protect security, security and order for the candidates, especially to participate in the fight against Kovid-19. She ordered the health department to set up a team of doctors to measure the temperature, spray alcohol, disinfect and set up a reserve room for candidates with health problems. Ms. Ban Srey Mom is determined to organize this year's high school diploma exam will be better than previous years for Pailin province.
She added, "This high school diploma exam, please all relevant departments, units, security forces to work together to make the exam on December 27, 2021 in a good environment to achieve success." .
On the occasion, Ms. Ban Srey Mom expressed her concern about the housing problems of poor candidates who could not afford to rent a house. She also set up a place to send bicycles and motorbikes free of charge to candidates, and she called for hotels, guesthouses, restaurants not to raise prices on the day of the exam to facilitate the lives of candidates to some extent.
The provincial governor assigned the districts and districts with the examination centers to call on the photocopiers to suspend the photocopying for three days, on December 25, 26 and 27, 2021.
