The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the leader, who is known as a brilliant and strategic strategist, also suggested that the talks on the China Sea and ASEAN member countries could achieve better results. Each other in the long run should not meet in the short term.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized, "In my opinion, we should negotiate. It can be said that ASEAN goes to China for half a month, so we do not meet for 3 hours and then split up for 5 months. If there is no place, Cambodia will use the Hai Yat Hotel as a negotiating place to sleep in a five-star hotel, and Cambodia will pay for it. "It's too big a liver to help solve friends and not let the South China Sea issue become a hot stone to a better hot potato."
In a public message sent to the leaders of China and ASEAN members in conflict with, as well as analysts, Samdech Techo Hun Sen warned in advance that countries in dispute should not throw hot stones at him. When Cambodia chaired ASEAN in 2012. But Samdech wants to get hot potatoes instead, because hot potatoes are hot for a while, but a little can be eaten.
