The ASEAN Constitution was adopted and came into force on 15 December 2008 by a meeting of the Foreign Ministers of the 10 ASEAN countries at the ASEAN Secretariat in Jakarta, Indonesia. 10 ASEAN countries during the 13th ASEAN Summit 2007 in Singapore.
The ASEAN Constitution is the cornerstone of ASEAN in the establishment of the ASEAN Community and is framed by ASEAN, ASEAN Laws, ASEAN Values, ASEAN's clear principles and responsibilities in accordance with ASEAN Law. The ASEAN Charter has become a legally binding agreement of the 10 ASEAN member states.
Regarding the case of Myanmar or Burma, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will travel to Myanmar in early January 2022 to pave the way for the progress of the ASEAN Five-Point Consensus Agreement.
The visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in early January 2022 is at the invitation of the President of the State Council and the Prime Minister of Myanmar, while Cambodia will chair ASEAN in 2022.
Myanmar has been facing internal political crises and turmoil since a military coup overthrew Aung San Suu Kyi's party on February 1 after the election.
Democrat leader Aung San Suu Kyi and some of the party's top leaders have been detained. A Myanmar court recently sentenced her to four years in prison for inciting anti-military insurgency and violating COVID-19. However, the head of Myanmar's military government has called for Aung San Suu Kyi's prison sentence to be reduced to two years.
During the internal crisis of nearly a year, Myanmar, a young member of ASEAN, was absent from the 2021 ASEAN Summit, making it impossible for ASEAN to find its consensus.
Due to the absence of Myanmar in the ASEAN Summit in 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who just received the hammer to chair ASEAN in 2022, has claimed that such a situation should not happen when Cambodia Host of the ASEAN Summit.
