ASEAN tourism officials are discussing the reopening of ASEAN tourism in the near future.
To support the re-opening of the reception of international tourists to visit the ASEAN region, the ASEAN National Tourism Institution and its partners discussed and agreed as follows:
1: Organize work activities to implement the plan to restore ASEAN tourism after the Kovid-19 crisis 2021-2025.
2. Develop and develop a policy framework for the sustainable development of ASEAN tourism based on the assessment of the impact on ASEAN tourism due to the Kovid-19 crisis in collaboration with the Research Institute for ASEAN and East Asia in accordance with The spirit of the Phnom Penh Declaration on the development of ASEAN tourism that is sustainable, environmentally friendly and better resilient towards a common future.
3: Preparation of ASEAN Tourism Marketing Strategic Plan 2021-2025. It should be noted that the roadmap on the plan to restore and promote Cambodia's tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis of the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia is also covered in the ASEAN Tourism Marketing Strategic Plan 2021-2025.
4. Establishment of the ASEAN Policy on the Evaluation of Pre-Study in order to provide opportunities for ASEAN tourism employees who do not have a degree but have practical experience and practical knowledge to obtain a certificate. Their skills.
5. Implement the ASEAN Guidelines on Safety and Hygiene for Tourism and Community Employees in Readiness to Announce the Reopening of ASEAN Tourism during the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022.
6. Promoting Investment in ASEAN Tourism will issue a guide on investing in ASEAN tourism.
7. Organizing joint initiatives to use digital and AI to promote ASEAN tourism in line with the ASEAN Declaration on Digital Tourism issued by the 37th ASEAN Summit in Vietnam on 12 December. November 2020.
8. Encourage direct flights to Cambodia, especially major tourist destinations such as Siem Reap and Sihanoukville.
It should be noted that the above documents will be submitted to the ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting for guidance and guidance for implementation within the framework of ASEAN cooperation and other relevant partners. Kampong Speu Provincial Governor Considers the Activities of the Women's Movement as a Basis for Strengthening CPP Policy
