It should be noted that the Global Wage Report is an important report of the International Labor Organization (ILO) released every two years. The report, released in 2020-2021, examines the global minimum wage system and its role in reducing social inequality, as well as how minimum wage can be set or negotiated. Important for economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis.
This installation demonstrates the Royal Government's commitment to ensuring and maintaining the livelihoods of workers based on the approach of assessing the balance between negative socio-economic and employment impacts on the sustainability of factories and enterprises. Protecting the income of workers and their families in accordance with the recommendations of the International Labor Organization (ILO).
The workshop on disseminating the Global Wage Report 2020-2021 aims to raise awareness and update more information on the development of the regional minimum wage system, as well as ways to strengthen labor market institutions and policies. Effective wage policy in the context of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
The workshop also highlighted the continued active support of the ILO with the Royal Government in contributing to the development of employment and vocational training aimed at improving the living standards of workers, promoting attractiveness and resilience. Favorable environment for business, trade and investment activities in Cambodia and aimed at responding to current and future trends in changes in economic structure and labor markets.
The Minister also said that this workshop is a new vision in the field of labor, which reflects the importance of the National Council for the Minimum Wage to contribute to improving the living standards of workers and the harmony of industrial relations. .
In addition, the Ministry will continue to make more efforts to strengthen the implementation of labor laws and regulations, strengthen mechanisms and institutional capacity, and increase cooperation with relevant partners to improve the minimum wage. Year after year.
On this occasion, the Minister hoped that the members of the National Minimum Wage Council, representing the Royal Government, the representatives of the employers and the workers, would gain knowledge, information and good experience from the progress of the implementation of the wage system. Minimum wages from different countries to serve as a basis for strengthening the minimum wage setting mechanism and other benefits for workers.
Kampong Chhnang Provincial Authority has set a two-day deadline for four families living on 13 dilapidated flats to dismantle their belongings before the authorities take administrative action.
(Kampong Chhnang): Kampong Chhnang provincial authorities have set a two-day deadline for four families to live on 13 dilapidated flats in Phsar Chhnang village, Phsar Chhnang commune, Kampong Chhnang city, to remove all items before the authorities take administrative action.
The deadline set by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Authority was made on the occasion of the joint provincial working group led by Mr. San You, Deputy Governor, on the evening of December 14, 2021, inspected the removal of all goods. Construction of 13 dilapidated flats in Phsar Chhnang village, Sangkat Phsar Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang city, as scheduled on December 3, which ordered the 12 families to remove all their belongings before December 14.
Mr. Sun Yu said that in the past, the municipal and provincial authorities as well as the relevant ministries have issued a letter informing the 12 families living on the 13 flats to leave the dilapidated building, which has been notified so far. It has been three years since they agreed to leave.
Meanwhile, the provincial authorities requested the people who own 13 flats, 12 families, to write a joint letter to ask for a law to demolish this dilapidated building. The provincial administration will facilitate the issuance of a law to demolish the building quickly. The next task is for the people who own the 13 flats to apply for a permit to rebuild the flats, which the provincial administration will facilitate in drawing up the plan and issuing the construction permit quickly.
It should be noted that on the evening of December 14, 2021, yesterday, for the owners of 9 flats who left, the joint team bought the keys and locked all the doors of the houses without letting anyone in or out again. They also tied ropes in front of the house and put up dangerous construction signs to prevent accidents.
