(Phnom Penh): The specialized police force of the National Police General Commission has finally dismantled a large-scale drug processing case in which the reserve criminals successfully exported and reached the seizure of ketamine (powder). K) A total of more than 2 tons, while chemicals up to 80 tons.
Unprecedented large-scale crackdown on drug offenses in Cambodia Police have arrested a group of four ringleaders, one of whom was killed in a night-time gunfight. Overnight on December 12, 2021 along National Road 4, Kampong Seila District (Sre Ambel Intersection), Preah Sihanouk Province.
Until December 14, 2021, General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police in charge of anti-drug crime, held a press conference to reveal the details of the drug crackdown operation at the department. Anti-Drug of the General Commission of the National Police, with the participation of many journalists.
General Mak Chito revealed the professional work of some police forces to the public after the operation can be said to be almost completely closed after the mastermind of the criminal network was arrested and is building a case. To be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for the most severe legal punishment in Cambodia.
The anti-drug police chief claimed that the main reason for the authorities to lead the crackdown was after receiving secret information from the Chinese side that there is a drug processing network is intended to produce drugs. In Cambodia to export to foreign countries, including China.
After receiving this information, strictly following the orders of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, the Anti-Drug Department took about 3 months to fully control the activities of the criminals involved in the theft. And processing on the premises of Sin Yin Feng (Cambodia) Industry Co., Ltd., a manufacturer of alcohol and organic fertilizers, located in Dambang Venh Village, Sangke Satop Commune, Oral District, Kampong Speu Province.
According to General Mak Chito, when the specialized force was investigating by all means, it was found that the criminals used the night to process and process drugs. He said that this action is just a test of their first step in case of success will be able to scale.
In front of the media, the Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police continued that until the day of the incident, the specialized force had received information that the criminals would be transporting large quantities of drugs by truck to be exported by sea to foreign countries. They have to travel along National Road 4 to continue to the boat dock at the Wave Dam to Koh Tang. At Koh Tang, there is also another ship waiting to receive their goods to be taken abroad.
However, the criminals' plan failed due to the foreknowledge and ambush on National Road 4, including the Anti-Drug Department, the police of Sihanoukville, Kampong Speu and Koh Kong provinces under the coordination of the prosecution. The Anti-Drug Department's specialized force is led by Lt. Gen. In Song, Deputy Director of the Department under the command of Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, Director of the Department.
At this time, the joint police force used fire trucks, sirens and paramedics to block National Road 4 at the intersection of Sre Ambel to intercept the criminals. Clearly, according to the information obtained, the criminals' drug truck arrived, but seeing that the police were intercepting the criminals, they did not surrender, that is, they hit the police car and even used weapons Watering.
Simultaneously with the crackdown on National Road No. 4 at the intersection of Sre Ambel, another group of specialized police forces also raided the drug processing plant at Xin Yinfeng (Cambodia) Industry Co., Ltd. Dambang Venh village, Sangke Satop commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province, confiscated 9 types of chemicals weighing 84 tons, 454 kg, 165 grams and a large number of processing equipment and arrested a criminal named YE YONG.
However, on the afternoon of December 14, 2021, the specialized force continued to search the company's location in Oral District, Kampong Speu Province until they found an additional 757 kilograms of ketamine. In total, more than 2 tons of drugs and 84 tons of chemical compounds were seized during the operation, as well as some processing machines.
General Mak Chito added that the drugs were only used by criminals in Cambodia to produce and process them, not to distribute them locally, that is, to export them abroad. And ketamine is an expensive drug. He claims that upon arrival in the country, the final buyer can be worth up to $ 600,000 per kilogram.
General Mak Chito said that this operation is a great success of the police, in particular and in general for the whole of Cambodia, which has cracked down on drug criminals and all the masterminds. However, he said that the police force will further strengthen the capacity to prevent and lead to the subsequent crackdown on drug offenses.
According to the senior police chief, the three criminals will be punished in Cambodia directly, while the seized drugs will be destroyed by the decision of the court.
