Dr. Kin Phea: Why the US urges Cambodia not to make any concessions to Myanmar, because the United States does not want to see small countries have autonomy to solve problems
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the reason why the United States urges the Royal Government of Cambodia not to make any concessions to the military regime in Myanmar because the United States does not want to see small countries have autonomy to solve problems That.
According to Dr. Kin Phea, the United States wants to interfere in the internal affairs of the entire ASEAN region, that is, the United States wants to show that it is the solution to all problems in the world. Simply put, the United States still has ambitions to be the organizer of world order on behalf of all international actors.
The remarks by the president of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia came after US State Department adviser Derek Chollet did not want to see Cambodia play a role in resolving the crisis in Myanmar during Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022. The Royal Government of Cambodia has expressed its willingness to resolve the Myanmar issue and to invite Myanmar leaders to the ASEAN Summit and to reunite ASEAN into 10 countries.
