Regarding the hotel, guesthouse and tourism services sector, said that so far there is no problem because it is ready to receive tourists who will travel to Siem Reap.
Thuon Sinan, President of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association, said: "For tourism business, such as hotels, guesthouses, etc. are ready, so there is no problem, there are tourists, we get all the parts. All. ”
He said, however, that there are still some concerns because the problem of the new virus "Omi Krong" has affected tourists who are afraid to travel.
Ms. Khay Chanda, Vice President of the Hotel Association, said that the current hotel is not fully open, but can receive enough tourists, so there is no concern, even if not fully open. Most hotels now open major sections such as guest rooms and restaurants.
"As for the non-opening of some of these hotels due to lack of revolving funds and lack of tourists, because the full opening of each hotel requires a lot of money, when the cost is high, it is necessary to have tourists to stay, otherwise No, there is no budget to cover all the expenses. But sooner or later, the hotel will be fully open in the near future.
