Kratie Provincial Administration Holds Youth Forum for Food Security and Nutrition
(Kratie): Mr. Kong Kimny, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, on December 14, 2021, opened the Youth Forum for Food Security and Nutrition through Strengthening the Food System for Sustainable Development organized by the Council for Agricultural Development and Rehabilitation. Rural cooperation with Kratie Provincial Administration and with the participation of relevant departments.
Mr. Kong Kimny stated that the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the occasion of the 8th National Nutrition Day on November 6, 2021, stated that the Royal Government participated in the Summit on the important food system and Demonstrated commitment and launched a roadmap for a sustainable food system in Cambodia 2023 with four priorities.
He said that in order to improve food security and nutrition in order to contribute to the promotion of health, livelihood and ensure family harmony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the 7th Nutrition Day on November 6, 2020 provided strategies such as:
* First, to promote youth participation in the field of food security and nutrition, and to improve nutrition education for students through the provision of nutrition education services such as deworming, health monitoring, hygiene and food safety counseling.
* Second, mobilize young people to understand how to cook Khmer food and promote a traditional Khmer diet using salt, sugar, fat and other flavor additives in moderation and support rich Khmer food producers. Nutritious and safe.
MANILA (Reuters) - Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte on Tuesday withdrew from the race for the Senate. This is according to a spokesman for the National Election Commission of the Philippines, quoted by Reuters on Tuesday, December 14, 2021.
Duterte's six-year presidency will end in June 2022, and according to the Philippine constitution, he can no longer run for president.
