(Phnom Penh): The Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel, an investment by Chip Mong with a total investment of 180 million US dollars, both land and construction costs, will be officially inaugurated this morning, December 15.
Chip Mong signed an agreement with world-class hotel company Hyatt Hotel Corporation in 2016 to manage the Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh. The company has preserved a French colonial villa for about $ 5 million, and now it is a luxury guest house.
In 2017, the company opened the construction site of this five-star hotel located in the heart of Phnom Penh. Construction is complete and a trial run will begin in early 2021.
Chip Mong, which brings the Hyatt Regency Phnom Penh Hotel to Cambodia, believes that this luxury hotel in the heart of Phnom Penh will connect tourists and business people from all over the world to Cambodia and contribute to the industry. Hospitality serves the needs of luxury accommodation in tourism and especially creates job opportunities for Cambodians.
