Tripoli: Libya will hold its first presidential election next week, but the list of candidates and deep political divisions are raising doubts as to whether the election will go ahead as planned. Leave it or not. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, December 14, 2021.
The election is part of the UN peace process for Libya, which has been embroiled in war since former Libyan leader Gaddafi was ousted in a coup and killed in a pro-government uprising. By the West in 2011.
But despite hopes for peace, UN officials and experts remain concerned that the presidential election could exacerbate the current civil war.
The Libyan presidential election is scheduled for December 24, 2021.
