ABA buys $ 30 million worth of bonds from Techo International Airport
(Phnom Penh): Vattanac Asia Bank Limited (ABA Bank) on December 14, 2021 decided to invest $ 30 million in bonds of Techo International Airport Construction Company to support the construction of this new airport.
The investment proceeds from the bond will be used for the construction and development of the Techo International Airport project in Kandal province. The Techo International Airport project is currently 28% worth a total of $ 375 million (excluding the cost of land already invested by CAIC).
CAIC is a joint venture between the Royal Government of Cambodia (RGC) represented by the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation and OCIC. The Royal Government of Cambodia has authorized CAIC to design, build, finance and operate the Techo International Airport project.
The Prime Minister stated that the participation in the purchase of the certificate is an access to the development of the new airport, which reduces the use of foreign capital, and the financial institutions also benefit from interest rates. Zero risk guarantee from the Royal Government as well.
