WASHINGTON (Reuters) - No U.S. military or military official has been charged in connection with the August drone strike in Kabul, Afghanistan, the Pentagon said on Monday. This year 2021, which killed 10 Afghan civilians, including 7 children. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, December 14, 2021.
The US military strike took place on August 29, 2021, during the last days of the US-led withdrawal and evacuation of Kabul after the Taliban. Came to rule Afghanistan.
