Cambodian diplomat tells ASEAN and G7 foreign ministers about Cambodia's priorities in resolving Myanmar crisis and building ASEAN community (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian diplomat tells G7 leaders about Cambodia's top priorities for next year To contribute to the peaceful resolution of Myanmar's problems and to build the ASEAN Community as Cambodia chairs ASEAN next year.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, made the remarks while attending a meeting between the ASEAN Foreign Ministers and the G7 Minister of Foreign Affairs and Development in Bangkok. Liverpool, United Kingdom, online on December 12, 2021.
"The Deputy Prime Minister highlighted Cambodia's key priorities and achievements for the ASEAN Community Building Process next year, as well as the urgent need for the establishment of a peaceful process to resolve the crisis in Myanmar, which should "Owned by Myanmar and led by Myanmar." This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, which was received by Fresh News.
The Deputy Prime Minister informed the meeting about the planned visit of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Myanmar in early January to pave the way for the progress of the five points of the unanimous agreement. ASEAN.
Myanmar Foreign Minister Wunna Maung Lwin affirmed that the Myanmar military government looks forward to welcoming and coordinating with the special envoy of the ASEAN chair appointed by Cambodia in 2022 to implement the five-point unanimous agreement, including Improve the humanitarian assistance process.
The statement of the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Myanmar was made during a bilateral meeting with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, on the morning of December 7, 2021, during the visit of Mr. Vunna Monglwin. 2 days.
In the presence of the heads of diplomacy of ASEAN member countries and the G7 countries, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon reiterated that ASEAN has always been an outward-looking regional organization and considers the regional order, which is at the core of ASEAN, to be the foundation of peace, security, stability and development. Regional and global prosperity.
The Deputy Prime Minister affirmed that Cambodia stands for the principle of unity for cooperation and not for confrontation, while urging the need to work together to promote trust and confidence and work together to resolve The common security challenge is that in doing so, all states, large and small, can coexist with the competition for excellence.
