General knowledge: 8 famous ancient cities of China
(Phnom Penh): The rich geography and strategic location, easy to defend but difficult to attack, are the most special places to build the ancient capital, such as Lak Yang, Chang'an. Anyone who has ever watched Chinese ancient movies is familiar with these ancient Chinese capitals.
Luoyang is one of the most famous historical and cultural cities in China, dating back to 2070 BC, the longest-running capital in Chinese history. By now, Lakyang is more than 4,000 years old. It is now located in the western part of Henan Province, China.
The walls of Lakyang were destroyed by a series of wars and were subsequently rebuilt. The walls we see today were restored during the Chheng Dynasty.
In Liaoyang, there are the first Buddhist monasteries in China, and there are also ancient temples of the Han Dynasty, Western Zhou Dynasty, Sui and Tang Dynasties, and many ancient tombs. The most famous historical site in Lok Yang is the South Dragon Gate Cave in the city.
Source: Culture Book "Landscape and Architecture"
