Here is the announcement: Congratulations! 29th Anniversary of the Inscription of Angkor on the UNESCO World Heritage List
Angkor Wat was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List on December 14, 1992 in Santa Fe, USA, under the auspicious and wise patronage of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk. Father of independence, territorial integrity and national unity of Cambodia, His Majesty the King's highest reverence, he appealed to UNESCO to help save the Angkor temples.
The Angkor Park area refers not only to Angkor Wat, but to the entire Angkor resort, including archeological sites, archeological sites, the environment and human communities, with a total area of 401 square kilometers.
Angkor is just one of nearly 100 other temples on the list. In addition to giving great pride to the Cambodian people, Angkor Wat also contributes greatly to increase revenue and boost the national economy through its reputation, which attracts a large number of national and international tourists. Every day.
