Taiwan's Defense Ministry made the remarks in a report sent to the island's parliament, stating that China's transport capacity is currently limited and unable to send troops to Taiwan. Easy, as China has to rely on ports and air transport, which requires an airport to land.
The report emphasizes that Taiwan has a strong air and port defense system that can retaliate and not allow China to control airports or ports in the short term.
According to the Taiwan Ministry of Defense, in addition to transport problems, China will also face attacks by foreign forces that will come to Taiwan's aid. Therefore, China has to keep a part of the army to deal with those foreign troops and keep the army to monitor some sensitive areas such as the border area with India and the South China Sea.
