(Siem Reap): The organization of Cambodia to celebrate "Siem Reap as an ASEAN Cultural Tourism City" is to increase the dissemination and inspire the whole nation to participate in promoting the preservation and development of national culture. This is according to a senior official of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
Siem Reap was selected as the ASEAN Cultural Tourism City for 2020-2022 through the Joint Declaration of the ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Culture and Arts at the end of October 2020.
On December 12, 2021, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia also organized a celebration to celebrate the city of Siem Reap has become an ASEAN cultural city. The ceremony was held in front of Angkor Wat under the presidency of Mr. Hap Touch, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts: Mrs. You Sophea, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, Mr. Long Kosal, Deputy Director General of the National Authority and government officials from relevant ministries and institutions.
Mr. Hap Touch said, "Organizing a cultural event to celebrate Siem Reap as an ASEAN cultural tourism city really means a lot to promote and inspire the whole nation to participate in promoting the preservation and development of national culture to contribute to economic development. Society in accordance with the strategic plan of the Royal Government and the national policy on culture.
