In the first 11 months of 2021, nearly 500 trucks with incorrect specifications were found in Sihanoukville Port, fined nearly 300 million riels
(Sihanoukville): In the first 11 months of 2021, officials found 464 trucks out of 14,937 vehicles inspected at the port of Sihanoukville. Nearly 500 vehicles with technical defects were fined nearly 300 million riels.
Improper trucking is one of the leading causes of serious road accidents. The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the land traffic police and the relevant authorities have been actively working to prevent this technically incorrect truck. Preventing faulty vehicles early in the port is a mechanism that is seen as highly effective in eliminating faulty vehicles.
The purpose of this inspection is to strengthen the implementation of the law on land traffic and to inspect the technical specifications of container trucks, to inspect the safety of vehicles at the destination of the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, especially to educate the drivers of container trucks. Awakening to respect the law on road traffic to help prevent and reduce traffic accidents caused by container vehicles.
Regarding the technical inspection of vehicles, Mr. Seng Chhuon said that some container vehicles were found to have technical problems and used incorrect documents, including, for example, the container keys were broken or the tires were not working properly. Driving the wrong type of vehicle and the technical inspection certificate of the car is expired.
Mr. Seng Chhuon called on all container truck drivers to abide by the Road Traffic Law and strictly adhere to the technical conditions of vehicles. In particular, you must use the driver's license properly according to the type of vehicle you drive to avoid accidents eventually caused by negligence, carelessness, disrespect for the lives of themselves and others. Find out the 4 winners of the 2021 National Entrepreneur Awards
