In the first 11 months of 2021, nearly 16,000 dangerous American bombs dropped on Cambodian territory were found and destroyed!
(Phnom Penh): At least 15,837 US cluster munitions, UXO and UXO were found and destroyed by the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC-CMAC) This is the 11th month of 2021.
According to a senior CMAC official, the bombs were found mostly in the provinces bordering Vietnam, but also in some provinces such as Kandal, Phnom Penh, Kampong Speu, Sihanoukville, Kampot. US bombings, especially cluster munitions, have been threatening people's lives. The bombs were found on a daily basis.
From October 5, 1965 to August 15, 1973, the US bombing of Cambodia under the pretext of destroying the Vietnamese invaders killed more than 500,000 Cambodians. Directly and destroy only tens of thousands of Khmer houses. This is according to data presented by the CMAC demining unit.
The millions of tons of bombs not only destroyed infrastructure such as schools, bridges, roads, it also caused great pain for the Cambodian people from previous generations to the present. The previous generation of Cambodians, some of them lost their lives, some became disabled, became seriously mentally ill due to the weight of the huge bomb.
The American legacy is that nearly 27 million cluster munitions are still found in droves, to this day it continues to threaten the lives of the Cambodian people, which is a tragedy.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, once compared US bombs dropped on Cambodian territory with hammers or axes, which were used to strike Cambodians on the head, and when the hammer was stained with blood, they even demanded money to clean it. This act is very unjust and painful.
