The soil type in the Terpan area is composed of gravel and clay, thus making the soil type strong, the well wall and the water flow path not easily broken. These provide favorable topography for digging square wells. Thus, the people used this special land to lead the construction, such as using the slopes of the mountains to create luxurious ice pits, and used the groundwater flow to irrigate the fields to create green areas.
Although the ice pit area is hot, the wind blows fiercely, which causes a large amount of water to evaporate, but due to these factors, the square well or the Tephan irrigation system has a stable flow of water and ensures the sustainability of the irrigation system. More yourself.
The role of the Theppan Irrigation System is to benefit the livelihoods and agricultural products of the people in the green areas, which are the underground tunnels dug by the people and drain the water through the foothills of the Tien San Mountains to the surface.
With the extensive economic development and application of modern science and technology in the Terpan area, an electronic irrigation system has been widely built in the Terpan region. The people here have easy access to tap water, so the role of the tap system has gradually diminished.
