(Phnom Penh): Farmers still prefer to use the method of obtaining fertilizers, pesticides or other materials from the depot owners or traders, and when the harvest is completed, only to repay the money for pesticides, rather than using loans from microfinance institutions. Objects and banks to buy fertilizers, pesticides. This was confirmed by Mr. Dok Loun, Vice Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Agricultural Community Coalition.
He said, "In reality, farmers are using this method because they are not ready in time for the farming season, so they have to leave the service area." "A lot of fertilizers, pesticides and other materials for farming, so they work with the depot owners quickly and easily, but they do not think these conveniences increase the cost."
He stated that the only way to solve these problems is to educate and explain to the people the benefits of using loans from banks and microfinance institutions. In that, microfinance institutions and the Cambodian agricultural community have cooperated in imparting knowledge to farmers so that they know how to use loans and use them on purpose.
