Russia has accused Ukraine of escalating tensions with pro-Russian rebels in the disputed Donbass region of eastern Ukraine. Russian President Vladimir Putin was quoted by Russian media as saying that the current situation in Donbass was similar to that of genocide preparations.
Russian intelligence reports claim that Ukraine also sent a military ship to the Kerch Strait between Russia and the Crimean peninsula, but did not respond to a request from Russia to change the route. . The Ukrainian Defense Ministry said the warship was an unarmed search and rescue vessel.
Russia's Deputy Foreign Minister Sergei Ryabkov even said that current tensions between the West and Russia over Ukraine could turn into a crisis similar to the Cuban Missile crisis. 1962 Once again, the United States and Russia were about to embark on a nuclear war.
The Moscow rhetoric comes just two days after an online video conference between Biden and Putin aimed at easing tensions over Ukraine. Russia is seen as keeping tensions high pending the next steps of Biden, who has said he plans to hold further talks involving Russia and NATO members.
Ukraine, which is trying to join NATO, has said it fears it could be invaded by tens of thousands of Russian troops gathered near the Ukrainian border. Russia, however, claimed that the mobilization of military forces was carried out for purely self-defense purposes.
