Senate Complaints and Observation Commission Celebrates the 73rd Anniversary of International Human Rights Day 10 December 2021
(Phnom Penh): The Human Rights Commission for Complaints and Investigations of the Senate has issued a statement celebrating the 73rd anniversary of International Human Rights Day, December 10, 2021, under the theme "Equality, Reducing Inequality and Promoting Human Rights."
In the context of ensuring and promoting human rights, the Cambodian Parliament has established its Institutional Human Rights Complaints and Oversight Commission, which monitors and evaluates the impact of proposed human rights legislation or its compliance with International legal framework as well as help promote the resolution of citizens' complaints.
In addition, parliament has played a significant role in promoting human rights, including:
* First, the National Assembly ratifies the international legal frameworks related to human rights, which will bring them into force into national law to demonstrate to the international community and its citizens the will to implement their obligations. Stated in the framework of those international legal acts.
* Second, the National Assembly approving the annual national budget needs to ensure that the action plan or implementation of the protection and promotion of human rights is adequate. Not only that, Congress also has a monitoring role to ensure that the government actually uses those budgets in a targeted and effective manner.
