Cambodian human rights chief acknowledges that Cambodian society discriminates against homosexuals by their families, communities and people around them
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, acknowledged that Cambodian society has discriminated against homosexuals by their families, communities and people around them.
Mr. Keo Remy made this remark while presiding over the celebration of the 73rd Anniversary of International Human Rights Day 2021, organized by the Rainbow Community Organization of Cambodia in collaboration with a network of civil society organizations working on human rights. Gender, gender identity, gender and reproductive health and reproductive rights were held at Himawari Hotel, Phnom Penh on December 9, 2021.
In celebration of the 73rd anniversary of International Human Rights Day, a roundtable discussion on "Legal Protection for LGBT Couples in Cambodia" was held, with speakers from the Rights Committee. The Cambodian people, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the Ministry of Justice, as well as the participation of diplomats, representatives of the United Nations in Cambodia, authorities, civil society organizations, the private sector and artists.
On that occasion, Mr. Keo Remy also called on all journalists to support and participate in disseminating widely not to discriminate against LGBT people, and he also reminded LGBT people to live in society. Cambodia, do not cause any phenomenon that causes chaos for the peace of all.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always taken care not to discriminate against LGBT people, this is an important message that is invaluable for lovers. Same-sex in the entire Cambodian Rainbow community as well.
The President of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee also stated that according to Article 1 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, all human beings are born free and equal in dignity and rights, and that everyone has the right to freedom of association. Without prejudice. These principles are universal, equal and non-discriminatory in the UN Charter and the Human Rights Treaty.
Mr. Keo Remy also instructed all participants to pay attention to listen to the speakers and have a lively discussion.
The roundtable discussion focused on the issue of LGBT marriage registration. Because if he does not have a marriage certificate, they will have some challenges such as family book registration, birth registration, adoption, division of property when they are separated.
International Analysis: Gun control issues exposed the hypocrisy of "American democracy" (Video inside) (Beijing): The United States considers "the protection of human rights" as one of the reasons for promoting American democracy abroad. But the proliferation of guns threatens the fundamental human rights of all Americans and has become an indescribable pain in American democracy.
According to statistics, the United States has the weakest gun law in the world, but the largest number of guns is about 393 million. The risk that Americans become victims of shootings is 25 times higher than the population of other high-income countries. "Almost every American knows at least one victim of gun violence in his or her life."
But does the United States boast of being a "tower of democracy" and a "human rights defender"? Why is it that so many people have died unjustly in gun violence and still can not urge the US government to take action?
In the case of political gun control, money does not vanish. The American National Rifle Association (NRA) is the largest and most powerful gun-related organization in the United States, with at least 5 million members and considerable capital. The association has had significant influence in the presidential election, the National Assembly election, and even the appointment of judges of the Supreme Court.
That is why, despite the growing American call for gun control, these voices have been ignored forever. This is a fact that worries you: In America, fresh life is being lost to guns, but politicians are not only ignoring it, but also promoting gun ownership.
