Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: The army must respect the rules, regulations and regulations in order to maintain absolute peace
(Kampot): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Army, stated that the Army must strictly abide by the Constitution, the general statute, general rules and other relevant legal documents as well as the Royal Government's regulations. The Ministry of National Defense, the General Command and the Army Command aim to maintain absolute peace.
This statement was made by Lt. Gen. Hun Manet at the ceremony of announcing the establishment of the Bokor Armed Forces, appointing, changing positions, equipping the ranks and integrating the military in the Kampot Military Operations Area on December 9, 2021 yesterday.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet realized that the Commander and Deputy Commander are the center of internal unity, starting from respect for each other and maintaining the quality of quantity through a clear division of roles and responsibilities. Based on the art and technique of leading with equity, virtue and justice, build the trust of the lower classes.
In addition, the Commander of the Army stated that "the Army must strictly abide by the Constitution, the general statute, general rules and other relevant legal documents, as well as the regulations of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief. The work and the command of the Army aim to maintain the peace that is hard to find under the sacrifice of fresh flesh and blood of the previous generation.
Therefore, as the next generation, please reinforce the values of sacrifice as the heroic example of the previous generation of soldiers and resolutely defend against any actions that incite, distort the truth, lead to disunity, national unity, unrest and "Political and social instability in order to drag Cambodia into destruction by the flames of war again."
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also commended and thanked the local authorities at all levels, the Armed Forces of all kinds, and all the philanthropists who have always provided close cooperation and contribution to support the operation area. Sub-Kampot and its subordinates until there is strong growth in all areas, ensuring the ability to fulfill national defense duties and the people in all circumstances.
In addition to the work for the army, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet would also like to express our deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for making a quick, courageous and responsible strategic decision to select and open. We are proud to have successfully launched a vaccination campaign for the people of Cambodia until Cambodia can be reopened in all areas as it is now.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also thanked and commended the institutions and units under the Army, as well as all institutions and units throughout the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for actively participating with the Royal Government in the campaign against tuberculosis. 19 Including the national vaccination campaign for the people, as well as taking care to protect themselves, their families and organizations by striving to implement all health measures consistently.
