105 HIV-positive families receive donations from Tbong Khmum Red Cross branch on World AIDS Day
(Tbong Khmum): This year, the World AIDS Day, December 1, 2021, organized by the Cambodian Red Cross Tbong Khmum Branch was held at Memot OD Health Office on the morning of December 9, 2021 under the President "End Inequality, End AIDS, End Global Pandemic."
The event was held to remind the world that even during the Kovid-19 pandemic, the fight against HIV / AIDS is still a topic of great concern to global public health because it remains Hundreds of thousands of lives are lost every year.
The day was presided over by Mr. Keo Vannak, Director of the Provincial Health Department and Deputy Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, represented by Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan, Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross in Tbong Khmum, with the participation of Mr. Vong Vanny, Director. Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross Members of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, People Living and Living with AIDS and Stakeholders.
On that occasion, Mr. Keo Vannak read a meaningful message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross on the occasion of World AIDS Day, December 1, 2021.
He said the celebration was to commemorate people living with people living with HIV and AIDS and to continue to raise public awareness of the importance of blood tests, prevention and treatment of HIV and to seek support. Continue in this important battle.
(Kratie): Mr. Vath Thorn, Governor of Kratie Province and relevant departments, units and district authorities on December 9, 2021, met and brought gifts from the Royal Government to 100 poor people and the elderly from Two districts are Prek Prosop and Chit Borey.
