Pursat Provincial Governor Chairs a Meeting of Provincial Board of Governors for November 2021 and Introduces 8 Major Plans to Meet the Needs of the People
(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Administration on December 9, 2021 held the meeting of Provincial Board of Governors for November and proposed the implementation direction in December 2021 under the chairmanship of Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor. Deputy Governors of the Provincial Board of Governors, Directors, Deputy Directors of Provincial Administration, leaders of various departments around the province, the three armed forces, governors, districts and other units under the provincial hall.
In order to make the work more active, Mr. Chiao Tai has set out some important plans in response to the needs and requests of the people, including:
* First, the municipal, district, department and unit administration must complete the report before the 25th to be sent to the provincial administration for summary and 5 days for revision before submitting to each monthly meeting.
* Second, all district governors should check the challenges in each district administration to solve at the local level, if not resolved, send the case to the province together to solve, do not leave it long.
* Thirdly, in the case of arrest and detention, there must also be an inspection of crimes so that small things do not become big things that affect the minds of the people on the leadership.
* Fourth, on the issue of drugs, gambling, theft, gangster, the local authorities and relevant units should establish mechanisms and strictly implement the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats in order to maintain security and social order.
* Fifth, all decisions should be adjusted to the new equality, avoid leaving behind the old composition.
* Sixth, recently, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia issued an order on measures to suppress state land encroachment in the flooded forest area of the Tonle Sap Lake area in Pursat province. Therefore, the provincial administration would like to issue a letter of instruction to the district authorities adjacent to the Tonle Sap Lake, including Krakor, Kandieng and Bakan districts, to promote and widely disseminate the seven forward measures to the people within its jurisdiction. Body.
