Royal Government Introduces 7 Measures on the Invasion of Tonle Sap Flooded Forest in Pursat Province
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has decided to set out seven measures for the ministries, institutions, units and administrations of Pursat province to work together to crack down on encroachment on state land in the Tonle Sap floodplain in Pursat province. This is according to the letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers, which was received by Fresh News on December 9, 2021.
The letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers states that the Royal Government has decided to put forward seven measures as follows:
Pursat Provincial Administration shall issue a letter of instruction to the district / commune authorities to stop the examination of the certificate of land tenure and the letter of transfer of land in the flooded forest area, as well as to issue a letter rejecting all the documents that have been issued in the past.
2. Pursat Provincial Administration must take measures to stop the encroachment on the flooded forest land, identify the invaders in order to confiscate the land and take legal action by building facts and filing a complaint to the court.
3. Along with legal measures, the perpetrators must replant trees on the encroached land.
4. The National Gendarmerie must deploy patrols to prevent the encroachment of flooded forest lands and implement legal measures.
5. The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology shall be responsible for planting the missing and demolished flooded forest border posts and applying for state land registration of flooded forest land in the Tonle Sap area.
6: For people who have planted crops, especially rice, leave time to harvest and almost make a letter of acknowledgment and return the flooded forest land to the state.
7: Replanting trees gives priority to planting bamboo trees.
