WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US and Israeli military chiefs are expected to hold a meeting on Thursday this week (Washington time) to discuss the possibility of conducting military drills over Iran's nuclear plant in the event of a scenario. Bad things happen or diplomatic talks fail or the leaders of both countries issue any orders. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, December 9, 2021.
