(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Movement for Health has issued a press release in support of the tobacco tax increase to boost the economy and health of the people, stating that the increase in tobacco tax will give Cambodia a substantial tax revenue. To support the national economy, especially during the outbreak of Kovid-19.
The Cambodian Movement for Health states that Cambodia will receive an additional $ 235 million in tax revenue over the next five years and $ 933 million over the next 15 years if Cambodia raises the tax to 75% of the retail price of cigarettes. United Nations Research Study 2018).
In addition to the loss of state revenue, smoking also causes many diseases, including stroke, coronary heart disease, lower respiratory tract infections, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and lung cancer. Lungs and trachea, etc.
On the other hand, the overwhelming majority of Cambodians support an increase in tobacco taxes to reduce health risks and increase national tax revenue. In fact, according to a study by the National University of Meanchey published in 2021, 94% of Cambodians support an increase in tobacco taxes, which is to increase to 62% of the retail price, which is equal to 2 Times of current tobacco tax.
It should also be noted that about 15,000 Cambodians die each year from diseases caused by tobacco use and cost the national economy 649 million US dollars, equivalent to 3% of GDP. GDP) of Cambodia, according to a United Nations study for Cambodia.
