The announcement comes after a foreign newspaper, which publishes in Khmer and often exaggerated in Cambodia, wrote an article in Khmer entitled "International Lawyers Warn Hun Sen's Government There will be problems if you dare to convict Seng Theary. ”
The Royal Government of Cambodia has affirmed that the Kingdom of Cambodia is a sovereign state, as are the member states of the United Nations, which have national constitutions and laws applicable within their territorial integrity and sovereignty. No person shall be arbitrarily deprived of his nationality nor denied the right to change his nationality.
The Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia divides the powers into three separate branches, of which the judiciary is independent. All court decisions have nothing to do with the executive or the legislature.
