The following is the report of the laborers in the Charity Center: The Emperor of Japan presents the medal for spring 2020 to the Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port
The award ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. MIKAMI MASAHIRO, Ambassador of Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia, with the participation of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training. And many other distinguished guests on the night of December 8, 2021 at the residence of the Ambassador of Japan.
The awarding of the Emperor of Japan Medal is a recognition of Luo Kimchhon's contribution to the promotion of friendly relations between Japan and the Kingdom of Cambodia in the field of port development.
On April 29, 2020, the Cabinet of Ministers of the Government of Japan announced the foreign medals awarded for Spring 2020 in recognition of their merits in serving the public or national interest and outstanding achievements. Of them in various spheres in society. Among them, there are two dignitaries who have received medals for their contribution to improving relations between Japan and the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. MIKAMI MASAHIRO also mentioned the work of Mr. Lou Kimchhon in promoting relations between Japan and Cambodia through the port development sector. Appointed Director of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in 1992. Since 1999, as the Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, he has been promoting partnerships with Japan and has been working to develop Sihanoukville Port.
From 1999 to the present, Japan has been cooperating in the development of Sihanoukville Port using concessional loans. In addition, in his position as the business manager of Sihanoukville Port, Mr. Lou Kimchhon has developed infrastructure such as the organization of container stations and multi-purpose ports, as well as strengthened the management capacity of the port.
The Japanese Ambassador said that in order to gain experience and knowledge from private companies, he also made efforts to issue publicly traded securities of Sihanoukville Port. In addition, many Japanese technicians, including JICA Port Executive Advisers, experts through JICA Technical Cooperation Project, have been sent to Sihanoukville Port for cooperation in port operation and management.
He pointed out that Mr. Lou Kimchhon has contributed to the development of Sihanoukville Port for many years, and through the development of the port in Cambodia, he has promoted the friendly relations between Japan and Cambodia as a bridge between the two countries. Two.
