BEIJING (Reuters) - Mainland China reported 44 cases of 19 domestic Kovid cases in mainland China, the National Health Commission said in its daily report on Wednesday. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Wednesday, December 8, 2021.
On the same day, the commission also noted that 30 import cases were reported.
As of Tuesday, the total number of 19 Kovid cases in mainland China had risen to 99,371, of which 1,133 patients were receiving treatment and 22 were in critical condition.
Chhnuk Trou Commune Authority and People would like to thank the Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province for helping to build a 450-meter-long concrete road on National Road 52 for the people of Chhnuk Trou Commune.
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Saing Kim Sorn, Chief of Chhnuk Trou Commune, on behalf of the people in Chhnuk Trou Commune, on the morning of December 8, 2021, would like to express his deep gratitude to Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, who is currently helping to build a concrete road. 450 meters long on National Road 52 in Chhnuk Trou Village, Chhnuk Trou Commune, Baribo District.
In particular, during the beginning of December, through the provincial governor, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport helped build a 450-meter-long, 3-meter-wide and 2-meter-thick concrete road at the port in Chhnuk Trou village, Chhnuk Trou commune to facilitate transportation. Local agricultural and fishery products to local markets.
The commune chief also confirmed that the concrete road above was built 3 meters wide, 2 meters thick, 3 meters long and more than 200 meters long, and was built by the national budget. Authorities and residents hope that in the next one to two months, the concrete road will be completed, which will allow farmers and fishermen to easily transport agricultural and fishery products by truck.
