Kavan Damrei, the lone elephant in the world, is no longer lonely and healthy, strong, happy in the new sanctuary at Kulen Prohm Tep Wildlife Sanctuary, Oddar Meanchey Province
Currently, the cavalry has been adapted to live in the 12-hectare natural forest, and in that area, there are three domestic elephants, which so far have been in contact. This has made the lonely elephant van no longer lonely. The Cambodian Wildlife Sanctuary has taken great care of the caravan and other elephants, as well as other wildlife in the protected area.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, a senior official of the Royal Government of Cambodia, presided over the welcome of the Cavalry Elephant, which arrived in Cambodia on November 30, 2020 after living in a zoo in Pakistan for many years. Cameron is now 36 years old and has been living in his new home in Cambodia for a year.
In addition, the spokesman said that during the year that the cavalry lived in the new sanctuary that Cambodia has given a different from the first, in which the cavalry has changed color like an elephant living in nature. New hair growth on the back of the nails is no longer dull and there is a growth of ivory at the base of the nails, slightly longer, the body is firmer, obese as before and the shape has changed.
It should be reminded that Khavan, the loneliest elephant in the world, finally arrived in the territory of Siem Reap Angkor province of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the afternoon of November 30, 2020, after traveling for many hours on a plane. From Pakistan.
Cambodia has given new shelter, new life and new hope to this lonely elephant. After receiving a blessing from the monks at Siem Reap International Airport, the elephant was taken to a new 4,350-hectare sanctuary in the Kulen Promtep Wildlife Sanctuary in Oddar Meanchey province, which is protected by the Cambodian Wildlife Conservation Organization. Obtained permission from the Ministry of Environment to protect and conserve.
Neth Pheaktra recalled the event on his Facebook page: “Commemorating the one-year anniversary of the reception of the world's loneliest elephant, Khavan, in Suvarnabhumi on the afternoon of the 30th. November 2020, two days after the November 28 event of the first 19 cases of Kovid outbreak in the community.
On that day, more than 7,000 newspapers covered the arrival of the Cavalry in Cambodia. It is the second world-famous event in Cambodia after the story of the ship Westerstard docked at the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, which the world knows as a small country with a wide heart.
"On that day, I and the famous American singer @CHER and I waited to welcome Cavan to Siem Reap International Airport and continue the Cavalier overnight to the conservation area," the senior official added. Elephants in Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province. Despite the hairy soul event, I am really proud and happy to sacrifice to serve my beloved motherland Cambodia. ”
