Since its founding by General de Gaulle on December 2, 1941, the French Agency for Development (AFD) has maintained its humanitarian principles in the fight against global inequality and environmental change. In this sense, for almost a century, AFD has been providing grassroots support for solidarity activities around the world to and with other institutions.
For the history and projects implemented in recent decades, women and men have taken turns to support and build together sustainable projects. For its 80 years, AFD aims to look to the future with partners and raise the question of what kind of world do we want to build in 2011?
What is certain is that the future will not be possible without the presence of women. That is why AFD aims to promote the value of women on the occasion of its 80th anniversary.
The French Ambassador to Cambodia, Jacques Perle, sees the 80th anniversary of AFD at the French Embassy as a good opportunity to protect and promote equality between women and men. Since 2018, with an international strategy for gender equality, France has been committed to feminist diplomacy.
He said the anniversary was also a great opportunity to showcase French diplomacy based on sustainable development, protecting the planet from the negative effects of climate change and ensuring a better future. Acne for everyone.
France's development policy is in line with the framework set by the international community, especially the 2030 Sustainable Development Program, adopted in 2015 by the United Nations General Assembly, the Paris Agreement on Climate Change and the Action Plan. Addis-Abeda on financing for development. The policy is also in the new European Development Agreement, which was adopted in 2017.
New Ministry of Defense building allows helicopters to land on rooftops
(Phnom Penh): Great! The new Ministry of Defense building, which is almost complete, has built a helicopter landing pad on the roof.
On December 8, a test flight of the Z-9 helicopter landed and was also successful. Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, expressed his pride and happiness at the success of the helicopter landing.
Please be informed that the new building of the Ministry of National Defense has been completed and is scheduled to be officially inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on December 29, the 23rd anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia under win-win politics.
The new administrative building and meeting hall of the Ministry of National Defense opened the construction site on June 30, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh.
The new office of the Ministry of National Defense has an administrative building and a meeting hall. The new building of the Ministry of National Defense is 28 meters wide, 191 meters long, 32 meters high and has a basement parking lot that can accommodate 150 cars.
In the new building of the Ministry of National Defense, it is possible to host national and international delegations, to hold patrols, honor guards, and troops in the building when it is raining.
The new office building is divided into small and large meeting rooms, small and large courtrooms, a press conference hall and a large meeting hall with a capacity of 1,000 people for national and international meetings. .
