(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, on December 08, 2021, sent a message of condolences on the death of Mr. Chan Rasy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and former Secretary General of the Constitutional Council.
In the condolence letter, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum said, "My wife and I are saddened to learn that His Excellency Chan Rasy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and former Secretary-General of the Constitutional Council, passed away on Monday. "March, Chhlov Trisak, BE 2565, is on December 6, 2021 at 17:00 at the age of 63 due to illness."
"My wife and I would like to express our condolences and condolences to Lok Chumteav and his family for the loss of His Excellency Chan Rasy, the head of the family, the father, the grandfather, the pious and the noble," he said.
Samdech considered that "The loss of His Excellency Chan Rasy is the loss of an outstanding Cambodian descendant who sacrificed his physical, mental and mental strength and has the merit to contribute to the building of the motherland of Cambodia and achieve many tasks for the society so far." To this day. ”
The following is the condolence message of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum: Siem Reap Provincial Administration and JICA implement smart city approach to solve challenges
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration, represented by Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), represented by Ms. Kamei Haruko, Chief Representative of JICA Office in Cambodia, signed an agreement on December 08, 2021. Official launch of the Technical Cooperation Project on "Implementation of Smart Cities to Solve Challenges in Siem Reap".
The joint statement states that the project has a duration of 3 years and is scheduled to start implementation in early 2022.
JICA has been conducting a data collection study on "Improving the Urban Environment in Siem Reap (Basic Data Collection Study") since 2020. The data collection study shows that the potential of achieving a smart city, that is, combining a variety of approaches, including the use of smart technology, will contribute to solving all of the city's challenges.
Both sides sincerely hope that the effective capacity development through the project, together with the technology system and intelligent management will contribute to improving the environment of Siem Reap.
