Minister of Labor Supports Appropriate Work Program That Contributes to Achieving National Development Goals by 2030
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that the decent work program in Cambodia 2019-2023 really supports the participation to achieve common goals and it is also a framework for cooperation between The Royal Government of Cambodia and its social partners contribute to achieving Cambodia's national development goals by 2030.
It should be informed that so far, Cambodia has jointly implemented five appropriate work programs. The fifth phase coincides with the 50th anniversary of Cambodia's membership with the International Labor Organization (ILO).
On December 8, 2021, Cambodia organized the opening ceremony of the National Tripartite Workshop on the Annual Review of the Decent Work Program in Cambodia 2019-2023 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
The tripartite workshop aims to review key achievements for 2020, share best practices and discuss key challenges in implementing a decent work program in Cambodia, and set priorities for 2021 and 2022 to promote the successful implementation of the decent work program in Cambodia 2019-2023, which was approved on March 28, 2019.
Through the right policies set by the Royal Government, it is supported by all stakeholders and participates in successful implementation, especially in the field of employment and vocational training. The ILO has always provided both Technical and financial assistance to contribute to the implementation of employment development and vocational training to achieve five priority goals.
The five priority goals include:
1: Develop working conditions and harmonization of professional relations
2: Modernize the technical and vocational education and training system
3: Maintain and increase employment and employment in and outside the country
4: Development of social security system
5: Strengthen general support services.
The Minister hopes that this workshop will take a closer look at what we have worked together to achieve over the past year and identify challenges to put forward solutions, especially in the priority activities implemented. In 2020 and the direction for the next year.
