Mrs. Youk Sambath and Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor Inspect Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital Construction Project
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Yok Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, together with Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Provincial Board of Governors, and the Technical Working Group of the Ministry of Health and Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department on December 8, 2021. And evaluate the construction project of the Cambodia-China Friendship Hospital in Tbong Khmum Province, which is a grant from the People's Republic of China.
The hospital project was inaugurated on March 1, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The 24,300-square-meter hospital will be built on a total area of 55,815 square meters and will take 32 months to build.
The Secretary of State pointed out that the hospital building was built to a high standard in terms of exterior appearance, interior aesthetics and the installation of modern medical equipment.
At the same time, the Governor of Tbong Khmum Province thanked the Secretary of State for taking the time to lead the technical team to finally inspect and evaluate the hospital project and thanked the construction companies for their hard work in building the department. The doctors are ready as planned and informed the Chinese side that if there is any need, the province will cooperate.
Meanwhile, the representatives of CRCG and IPPR thanked the Secretary of State, the Governor of Tbong Khmum Province and all the working groups of the Cambodian side who always cooperated and supported the smooth implementation of this project and achieved as planned. Despite the circumstances of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health conveyed a message of thanks and appreciation from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to all staff of CRCG and IPPR for their hard work and completion. Set.
The Secretary of State also conveyed the high praise from the Prime Minister to the health officials, local authorities at all levels, the Armed Forces of all kinds in Tbong Khmum Province who have done their best to provide services to the people. High sense of responsibility.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch inspects cluster munitions clearance and community development work in Stung Treng province's Sesan district under a project supported by Japan JMAS
(Stung Treng): On December 8, 2021, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, inspected the CMAC Center's cluster munitions clearance work in collaboration with JMAS and community development work after clearing in Sesan district, Stung Treng province, with the support of the Royal Government and the people of Japan.
The visit was attended by Mr. Duong Pov, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province, Representative of Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Stung Treng Provincial Board of Governors, Sesan District Governor, Representative of CMAC, President of JMAS Cambodia, Stung Treng Mine Action Plan Working Group and local authorities.
In collaboration with CMAC, JMAS has started its three-year project in Stung Treng Province from February 2021, with funding to support demining and community development work, such as training about 600,000 people in agriculture. USD per year.
JMAS has been supporting mine clearance and community development in Cambodia since 2002, including: Rehabilitation of infrastructure, construction of schools and providing agricultural technical skills in four provinces, including Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Kampong Thom and Stung Treng, and currently JMAS support is limited to Banteay Meanchey and Stung Treng.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister appreciated the generous support of JMAS, which has been involved in demining and on-site development with the aim of improving the livelihoods of local people after the clean-up. Sustainable as well as appreciate and thank CMAC, especially the deminers who have sacrificed everything to provide safe land.
He stressed that deminers have not only contributed to saving the lives of local people, but also left behind valuable achievements for families and society.
