Banteay Srei to Hold Food Fair in Preah Dak Village
(Siem Reap): The governor of Banteay Srei district has revealed the rural food fair program planned to be held in Preah Dak village later this year.
Banteay Srei District Governor Khim Finang unveiled the "Rural Food Fair" which is scheduled to take place on the road through Preah Dak village during the upcoming Global New Year.
The food fair is also to congratulate Preah Dak villagers who have just won the environmental friendship award for 2021 and to promote the village clean house competition project in 2022.
The rural food fair is scheduled to run for three days from December 30-31 and January 1, with plenty of food stalls, seating, music, dance, drums and ample parking, but will be held in accordance with the rules. Extremely strict health safety.
