"Cambodia and Vietnam should establish stronger cooperation in all fields, especially in the fields of economy, trade and agriculture, in order to be worthy of strong and long-standing friendship and cooperation." This is an additional statement of Mr. Nguyen Huy Taing.
At the same time, the ambassador said that the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam has increased significantly in the last two years, despite the two countries facing a crisis of epidemics. In 2020, the trade volume between the two countries will reach $ 5.32 billion. In the first 10 months of 2021, it reached $ 7.87 billion and is expected to reach $ 9 billion in 2021 as a whole.
