Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth recommends five points to help promote the national program "New Business Cambodia" for sustainable success
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, December 8, 2021, officially announced the launch of the national program on "New Business Cambodia" to support the entrepreneurial ecosystem and new business through entrepreneurship and Promoting new business in terms of capacity and financial resources.
The event was presided over by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and was attended by representatives of ministries, institutions, embassies, associations, civil society organizations, development partners, private sector educational institutions, institutions, training and business acceleration, new investors and businesses.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth made five recommendations to all stakeholders to help promote the national program "New Business Cambodia" for sustainable success.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth stated that he would like to highlight some important priorities for all stakeholders to participate in organizing the national program "New Business Cambodia" to achieve sustainable success for the benefit of all. Each as follows:
1: All stakeholders must contribute to increasing the interaction between the actors in the new business ecosystem to design new business support programs to improve quality, strengthen technical capacity, increase entrepreneurial skills, increase capital and provide opportunities. Investment, as well as participation as a recipient of new business services / products and as a support provider
2. All stakeholders must actively participate in the New Cambodia Business Community program, including: demonstration of activities, product / service promotion, experience sharing, consulting and technical and financial support to create gift conditions. - Impact on Cambodia's new business ecosystem
3: Students, business people, and innovators need to strengthen their own abilities, both hard and soft skills, through institutional learning, research, internships, and participation in new business support programs to be competent. In the competition to create a new business with innovation and high chance of success
4: Relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government shall provide support for new businesses and new business ecosystems in their respective sectors through the integration of support activities into the annual plan and the provision of incentive policies.
