(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong has announced 50 scholarships for poor students, including 25 associate degrees and 25 bachelor's degrees at the Prek Leap Agricultural Institute for the 2022 academic year, which will begin in January 2022.
Conditions for Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong's scholarship include:
* Associate degree scholarships are for students who have passed the high school exam in 2021. * Bachelor scholarships require students to have a high school diploma in 2021.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong stated that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the country has achieved peace and development in all areas on an equal footing with other countries in the international arena. Bamboo has all the opportunities to study in the country and continue to other countries to increase knowledge for the future of themselves, their families and society as a whole.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong "continued that what the people and society want is the peace and prosperity of the country in all areas, a prosperous nation depends on good human resources. Therefore, the next generation of young people who continue to take care of peace to turn our country into a prosperous and rich country in the future.
For more information related to these 50 scholarships, please contact Ms. Keo Serey Sokuntheary, Tel: 017 569 041.
Minister of Commerce Encourages Economic Operators and Investors in French-Speaking Countries to Select Cambodia as a Venue for New Cooperation Expansion (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Held in Phnom Penh in collaboration with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the Organization of the French-speaking countries (OIF).
The event was also attended by the French Ambassador to Cambodia, the Council for the Development of Cambodia, inter-ministerial representatives, development partners and representatives of the private sector on the evening of December 7, 2021.
Minister Pan Sosak welcomed and supported the Francophone Economic and Trade Mission initiated by the OIF with the aim of establishing economic ties between French-speaking countries and countries in the region.
At the same time, the Minister reaffirmed his willingness to strengthen trade, economic and diplomatic ties with OIF member countries, which will be important for Cambodia and other countries in the region, especially in multi-sectoral cooperation, including culture and tourism. Social work will contribute to economic recovery after being affected by the global Kovid-19 pandemic.
On that occasion, the Minister encouraged OIF economic operators and investors from all continents to explore the trade potential that Cambodia has and new opportunities and to select Cambodia as a location for expanding new regional cooperation and participation. The emerging value chain is growing.
The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, cremated his body for cremation.
The cremation ceremony was also attended by Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate; Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly; Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia; To the afterlife.
December 08, 2021 is also the day that the Royal Government has designated a day of mourning throughout the country to pay tribute to him for his other achievements for the motherland.
During the mourning ceremony, the Royal Government set the flag to be flown at half-mast in public and private institutions, banning radio, television and other media from playing entertainment programs. In the entertainment club, karaoke bar is also suspended.
It should be noted that Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh passed away on Sunday, November 28, 2021 at 9:40 AM in France. : 40 minutes in the Kingdom of Cambodia at the age of 77 due to illness. His body left France for Cambodia on December 5, 2021.
Samdech Krom Preah was born on January 2, 1944. Son of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and concubine Phat Kanoul, a royal courtier. Samdech Krom Preah has five sons and daughters: Prince Norodom Chakravuth, Prince Norodom Siharith, Princess Norodom Ratanadevi, Prince Norodom Sothearith and Prince Norodom Ranavong.
Samdech Krom Preah served as the First Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia from 1993 to 1997 and served as the President of the National Assembly from 1998 to 2006.
