On the morning of December 7, 2021, Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), met with HE Teo Eng Dih, Undersecretary of State. Ministry of National Defense of the Republic of Singapore and a visiting delegation in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
During the meeting, the Undersecretary of State highlighted the good cooperation between the two countries' armies, Cambodia-Singapore, which has been implemented in the past and praised the culture, civilization and achievements made by peace. And national unification manifested through the delegation's visit to historical sites such as the National Museum, the Tuol Sleng Museum and the Victory Monument.
In response, the Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Army welcomed the delegation for a visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia and also informed of the efforts of the Royal Government as well as the people throughout the country to unite. Maintain this existing peace to continue the progress and prosperity.
At the same time, the Deputy Commander-in-Chief praised the cooperation between the two countries' armies, especially the many cooperation activities at the army level, such as exchange visits, training exercises and support. .
Finally, Lt. Gen. Commander of the Army thanked the Government of Singapore for the good relations and cooperation and supported the forward direction of the two governments and the Ministries of Defense of the two countries in further promotion. Cooperation in the field of security and defense, which is an important strategic cooperation.
