The following is a statement: Comment: US-Taiwan conspiracy is destructive to the situation in the Taiwan Straits
Regarding the Taiwan issue, China has repeatedly stated its position that in the world there is only one China, Taiwan is an inseparable part of Chinese territory and the government of the People's Republic of China is The only legitimate government of China. The Taiwan issue is purely an internal affair of China, never allowing any outside force to interfere.
China is willing to make every effort to achieve the future of peaceful national reunification on both sides of the Taiwan Straits with the utmost sincerity. However, if separatist forces "want Taiwan to be independent", provoke and coerce, or even break the red line by then, "China will take decisive action."
Letters from readers: The road to a peaceful and stable political transition
Since the end of the civil war in 1999, Cambodia has achieved complete peace under the win-win policy of Prime Minister Hun Sen, which has made Cambodia one of the fastest growing economies in the world. That change is brought about by peace, stability, the rule of law and democracy.
Cambodia's past is marked by civil war and Cold War political power. When the nation was liberated in 1979 from the Khmer Rouge regime, important national political figures appeared. One of them was Hun Sen, who dared to sacrifice his life to liberate the nation from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime, as well as to protect the interests of his people and his country.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen led the country towards peace and prosperity. Cambodia now holds regular national and sub-national elections under the lines of a free national constitution that guarantees civil and political rights.
Phnom Penh, December 08, 2021 Mr. Sous Yara, Member of the National Assembly from the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), set the work direction to reduce blindness to 0.35% by 2030
(Phnom Penh): Speaking at the Consultative Workshop on the National Strategic Plan for the Prevention and Management of Blindness 2021 to 2030 on December 7, 2021, Prof. Ngy Meng, Advisor of the Ministry of Health, Director of the National Eye Health Program and Director of The Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital stated that under the joint commitment between Cambodia and development partners, the work direction to reduce disability to 0.35% by 2030 has been set.
This strong commitment comes after Cambodia achieved a series of remarkable achievements, with the prevalence of blindness declining from 1.2% in 1995 to 0.38%. In 2007 and will continue to fall to 0.37% in 2019.
He said that this achievement, which also includes the cooperation of ministries, departments and national and international development partners.
He added that for this national strategy is a map pointing to:
* Quality eye care services, reasonable prices, more comprehensive and can achieve high quality
Adequate number of properly trained, multi-skilled and well-motivated staff
* Quality medicines, equipment and supplies for eye health and expand the use of equipment and technology to expand and improve the appropriate infrastructure
* Increase available financial resources for eye health by improving the cost-effectiveness and reducing the financial crisis in access to eye health services through health care programs.
* Strengthen a well-integrated eye health information system that provides timely and high quality information for decision making, planning, monitoring and evaluation of effective implementation and provision of eye health services.
Strengthen institutional capacity and governance practices to effectively manage the eye health system, which is an important part of expanding the health system towards universal access to quality eye health services.
