CMA: Stopping the issuance of deposit licenses to microfinance institutions is right, Cambodia now has 61 banks and microfinance institutions accepting deposits
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy, Spokesman of the Cambodian Microfinance Association (CMA), said that the decision to suspend the issuance of new licenses by the National Bank of Cambodia for the business of accepting deposits to microfinance institutions will have a positive effect. Much for the existing microfinance sector to strengthen and expand its services to provide better quality to customers.
Speaking to Fresh News on December 8, 2021, Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy stated that the decision of the National Bank of Cambodia will help microfinance institutions to accept existing deposits, strengthen and expand the services of It has more quality to attract people to get into the habit of saving at official institutions without using the savings of piglets as before.
"The decision of the National Bank of Cambodia is correct because now the Cambodian Microfinance Association sees that the provision of financial services, including depository services, has reached almost all parts of the country," he said. "Therefore, Cambodia does not need to issue licenses to any new institutions at this time."
He said that as of now, there are 55 commercial banks and six microfinance institutions in Cambodia licensed to accept deposits, which is enough for this sector.
The spokesperson emphasized that encouraging clients to save money through official institutions remains a priority for the microfinance sector, as saving habits will help reduce problems and create opportunities for Cambodians. Not yet in good savings habits.
He said that as of the end of September 2021, according to the six deposit-taking microfinance institutions, the number of depositors increased to 2,849,344, an increase of 33,686 from the previous quarter. While the volume of deposits increased to 4.073 million US dollars, an increase of 190 million US dollars compared to the second quarter.
Please be informed that on December 7, 2021, the National Bank of Cambodia has decided to stop issuing new licenses for microfinance institutions to accept deposits from the date of this announcement to further strengthen the capacity. Of banking and financial institutions maintain financial stability and contribute to national economic development.
The Bank of Cambodia welcomes investors to invest in existing banking and financial institutions and encourages the integration of existing banking and financial institutions to promote the provision of quality, efficient and effective financial services. Reasonable prices for companies, enterprises and the public.
