It should be noted that Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh passed away on Sunday, November 28, 2021 at 9:40 AM in France. : 40 minutes in the Kingdom of Cambodia at the age of 77 due to illness.
Samdech Krom Preah was born on January 2, 1944. Son of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk and concubine Phat Kanoul, a royal courtier. Samdech Krom Preah has five sons and daughters, including: Prince Norodom Chakravuth, Princess Norodom Siharith, Princess Norodom Ratana Devi, Princess Norodom Sothearith and Princess Norodom Ranavong.
Indonesian president visits volcano-hit area, vows to step up rescue, rehabilitation efforts
The 3,676-meter-high Semeru volcano erupted last Saturday, sending ash into the air and engulfing surrounding villages. At least 34 people have been killed and 17 are missing, according to the latest figures from the Indonesian Disaster Management Authority. Nearly 3,700 people have been rescued from the affected areas.
After visiting evacuation centers and inspecting the affected areas by helicopter, the Indonesian president confirmed that rescue and rehabilitation efforts would be stepped up and extended. Joko Widodo added: "After the relief, we hope that the repairs will begin immediately, including the relocation of people who have been unable to return to their homes."
On Tuesday, Semeru erupted three more times as Indonesian authorities warned that tensions could continue. It is one of nearly 130 active volcanoes in Indonesia. It once erupted in early January 2021, but no one was injured.
Ministry of Health receives Singapore Government grant to Royal Government of Cambodia to prevent Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, together with Ms. Teo Lay Cheng, Ambassador of the Republic of Singapore to Cambodia, on December 7, 2021, attended the handover ceremony of the Government and the people of Singapore. Government and people of Cambodia to use to prevent and respond to the spread of Kovid-19.
Speaking at the event, Prof. Mam Bunheng stated that the government and Singaporean assistance provided to Cambodia includes: a Kovid-19 virus testing machine, 1 million surgical masks and 200,000 hand gels. Bottles.
The Minister of Health added that the noble generosity of the Government and people of the Republic of Singapore is remembered by the Royal Government of Cambodia and health officials and victims of Kovid-19.
At the same time, the Ambassador of Singapore expressed his appreciation for the Cambodian health sector, which has improved the health of the Cambodian people, as well as the prevention and response of Kovid-19 disease, vaccination for Cambodians and foreigners. The population of Cambodia is over 88% of the total population of 16 million, including all Singaporeans living in Cambodia, especially all Singaporean diplomats.
