Pyongyang: North Korean leader Kim Jong Un has said his country's military education system must redouble its efforts to train as well as produce the resources of loyal military officers loyal to the Korean Workers' Party. (WPK). This is according to North Korean state media quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday, December 7, 2021.
Kim Jong Un made the remarks at the eighth conference of the Korean People's Army military trainers in Pyongyang last weekend. Speaking on the occasion, Kim stressed that North Korean military officials must be genuine, loyal to the leadership of the Labor Party and adhere to the party's principles, methods and guidelines.
Last November, North Korea held a similar conference, at which time Kim Jong Un announced plans to expand the reward system and encourage loyalty to the Labor Party. Holds sole power in North Korea.
