(Phnom Penh): The body of Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and President of FUNCINPEC will be cremated on Wednesday, December 08, 2021 tomorrow in Preah Meru Wat Botum Vatey, Phnom Penh.
The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, will pay his respects at the cremation.
The cremation ceremony will be attended by Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as many other national leaders and political figures will also attend the cremation ceremony, as well as the enthronement of Samdech Krom Preah to the afterlife.
According to the planned program of the cremation, there will be the visit of both groups of Samdech Preah Moha Sangkha Reach (2 Samdech Preah Aphitham), 8 monks and 67 monks, a total of 77 monks. 38 monks of the Mahanikaya, 39 monks of the Dhammayutnikaya, 39 of the monks of the Sattapakarnaphitham (genealogy).
Tomorrow, December 8, is also a day set by the Royal Government as a day of mourning throughout the country to pay tribute to him for his accomplishments for the nation.
Radio, television and other media are prohibited from playing entertainment programs. Karaoke club bars also suspended
It should be noted that Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh passed away on Sunday, November 28, 2021 at 9:40 AM in France. : 40 minutes in the Kingdom of Cambodia at the age of 77 due to illness. His body left France for Cambodia on December 5.
National Authority for Combating Drugs Inspected the Implementation of Drug-Free Village Plans in Village 2 in Preah Vihear and Stung Treng Provinces
(Preah Vihear - Stung Treng): With the permission of General Meas Virith, Secretary General, on December 7, 2021, Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs inspected the implementation of village, commune and sangkat plans. Drug free in two provinces, Preah Vihear and Stung Treng, with the participation of stakeholders from national and sub-national levels and local authorities.
On that occasion, the village chiefs of the four drug-free villages, communes and sangkats of the two provinces welcomed the progress report of the villages, especially the implementation of the drug-free commune / sangkat village plan, highlighting the achievements and the remaining work. Challenges that must continue to be implemented in order to contribute to maintaining security and order for the people.
Speaking on behalf of General Meas Virith, Secretary General, Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea praised and appreciated the efforts of the village through the support of the national, sub-national and local levels, especially the participation of the people. It deals with the prevention and problem of drugs, helping people and their children not to fall into the trap of drugs, causing harm to themselves, their families and communities.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Nak Yuthea also informed about the importance of the direction set by the higher level and encouraged the participation and support from the local level to make sure that all villages that are implementing village, commune and sangkat plans White without drugs to succeed.
It should be noted that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, have previously instructed all border provinces to establish at least two drug-free villages in each province. Kheng and Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan recommended the establishment of every village.
The working group of the National Authority for Combating Drugs will continue to inspect the implementation of the drug-free village, commune plan in Kham Phan village of Samaki commune, Stung Treng city, Stung Treng province, and visit the project to establish a village in Stung Treng province on the 8th. December 2021 onwards.
