UNICEF calls for unprecedented humanitarian aid for Afghans
The United Nations Children's Fund (UNICEF) on Tuesday issued a call for $ 2 billion in aid to meet humanitarian needs in Afghanistan. This is according to the release by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday, December 7, 2021.
Since the Taliban took control of Afghanistan in mid-August, the country has faced a major economic collapse.
"The humanitarian situation in Afghanistan continues to deteriorate, causing alarming disruptions in health and nutrition services in the face of food crisis, drought, measles outbreaks and diarrhea," the statement said. Polio and preventable diseases, as well as disabilities, as well as the onset of winter.
UNICEF estimates that one in two Afghan children under the age of five will be severely malnourished by 2022 due to the food crisis and the lack of clean water and sanitation.
