(Rattanakiri): 531 certificates of ownership of real estate were handed over by the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Rattanakiri Province to the people in Tharang Svay Village, O'Chum Commune, O'Chum District, Rattanakiri Province.
The ceremony of handing over and receiving the certificate of ownership of real estate was held on the morning of December 7, 2021 in the presence of Mr. Muong Pang, Deputy Governor, Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri.
Mr. Ly Usaphea, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Ratanakkiri Province, said that the distribution of property ownership certificates in Tharang Svay village, O'Chum commune, O'Chum district, on a total area of 657.05 hectares, has a certificate of ownership. 531 real estate titles, including: 216 residential land certificates, 312 agricultural land certificates and 3 state land certificates.
On this occasion, Mr. Muong Pang commended the land registration team and all stakeholders for their efforts in accomplishing this work responsibly and transparently.
Mr. Muong Pang stated that the title deed received by the people today is a very important document, a document representing the property of the people, a document representing the exclusive right of the owner of their land to use and depend on. Efficiency in sales, transfer to others, guaranteeing loans, transfer to children. Therefore, people should keep this card better.
On this occasion, he also instructed all people to continue to take good care of their health and to continue to protect themselves from Kovid 19 by strictly implementing health rules and to protect good health in this winter. .
Preah Vihear Sraem Roundabout, Built at a Cost of More Than 120,000 USD, Officially Inaugurated
(Preah Vihear): Sraem Roundabout in Sraem Commune, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province was officially inaugurated on the afternoon of December 6, 2021 in the presence of Mr. Meas Sophea, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the Provincial Government Working Group. Church.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Sous Yara, Member of Parliament for Preah Vihear District, Mr. Long Sovann, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as leaders of government officials in various departments around the province.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Meas Sophea said, "Today we celebrate the inauguration of this roundabout as an event related to the history of our country, we want to connect with our December 2".
He said why do you want to commemorate the event on December 2? He said that our country from 1975 to 1979 fell into a genocidal disaster, then our Cambodia suffered no rights, no freedom, no market, no pagoda, no school ... Not only that, but also killed innocent people. Also.
The Senior Minister said that our patriotic dignitaries gathered to form the United Front for National Salvation on December 2, 1978 to overthrow this genocidal regime. "Without December 2, 78, we would not have January 7, and without January 7, we would not have had the Paris Agreement, we would not have had the restoration of a liberal, multi-party democracy, we would not have had peace," he said. Economic restoration and development as it is now.
Separately, Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, said that the construction of this roundabout started on January 2, 2019 and will end on May 30, 2020. He said that the statue of the temple in the center of the circle is modeled on the 5th gop, the temple of Preah Vihear is 70 percent of the original temple, the cost of construction of $ 125,000, which came from the contribution of philanthropists. Use the national budget.
