On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also instructed all technical teams to diligently inspect the quality of paved roads to ensure strong quality and long-lasting use.
The Senior Minister also urged the relevant technical experts to examine the possibility of planting flowers in front of the entrance to Angkor Wat to attract national and international tourists to be suitable as a cultural and historical center, as well as to help increase the beauty to another level and to pay attention. Thoroughly transport the road irrigation rubber to the construction site to avoid shedding on the road, causing loss of the beauty of the road already built.
As a result of the inspection related to the rubber concrete, the Senior Minister also checked for minor technical errors during the rubber stamping and advised the technical team of the construction unit as well as the relevant technical experts to make appropriate adjustments. And technical standards of construction.
