She added that the United Kingdom, as well as other donors, will continue to help clear mines from Cambodian territory. Longan growers have hope again after Chinese ambassador announces that Cambodian longan fruit will be able to be exported directly to Chinese market next harvest season
(Phnom Penh): Pailin longan growers have expressed their admiration for China's decision to study and analyze the risks of longan fruit through remote video, which will enable Cambodian longan fruit to be exported to the Chinese market during the harvest season. Next.
He added that most of the longan farmers, both members of the Pailin longan association and non-members of the association, were trained in good agricultural practices according to GAP standards, some of which were registered with the Ministry of Agriculture. This will ensure that the evaluation of phytosanitary techniques and risk analysis on longan will run smoothly.
"He gave a lecture on good agricultural practices, and we sent samples to him for inspection, and he evaluated and issued a certificate of good agricultural practices," he said.
He said that after Mian Pailin officially exported to China, it will help open more markets as well as increase prices.
Pailin longan harvest season is from August to May every year. According to the Mean Pailin Association, each year, the Mean Pailin Cambodia exports an average of 20,000 tons, most of which are exported to Thailand.
During the inauguration of National Road No. 11 in Prey Veng province on the morning of December 6, 2021, Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, said that the Chinese side has made a decision to study and analyze the risks of Cambodian longan and trout. From a distance video, if smooth, Cambodian longan can be exported to the Chinese market during the next harvest season.
