(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dok Loun, Vice Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Agricultural Community Coalition, which has 1,200 agricultural community members, equivalent to more than 100,000 farming families, said that currently the interest rate from the banking and financial sector for the agricultural sector is still the same. Still high, an average of 10 percent per year.
He said that although interest rates were still high, the banking and financial sectors played a key role in agriculture.
"Farmers and agricultural communities use banking and microfinance, so compared to the cost of production the use of banking and microfinance for agriculture is still high," said Dok Loun. "However, the agricultural sector still benefits from the use of banking and microfinance services, which help the agricultural sector to continue to improve."
Mr. Rom Ratha, Commercial Director of Amret Microfinance Institution, responded to the issue of high interest rates of banks and microfinance institutions that provide to the agricultural sector that interest rates depend on costs. As for Amret, it has tried to provide cheaper interest rates to farmers and farmers. Obviously, for Amret Direct, the interest rate for the agricultural sector is lower than the interest rate of other sectors.
Mr. Dok Loun, Representative of the Cambodian Agricultural Community Coalition, said that there are still some challenges in obtaining credit from farmers because farmers and farming communities have limited knowledge of the financial sector and banking, so they Not ready to take credit from all those institutions.
He added that currently the agricultural sector faces a number of challenges, such as: 1. High prices for the use of fertilizers, drugs, machinery, labor consumption. 2. The distribution of demand in the domestic and foreign markets is not clear by region Some are over-cultivated, but others are not-cultivated.
According to the report of the National Bank of Cambodia, as of August 2021, banking and financial institutions have provided loans to the agricultural sector of about 17 trillion riels, equivalent to about 4.2 billion US dollars. Lt. Gen. Hun Manet and Mrs. Pech Chanmony Pay Tribute to the Body of Prince Norodom Ranariddh
(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army and Mrs. Pech Chanmony paid a courtesy call on the late King Norodom Ranariddh on the afternoon of December 7, 2021. The body will be kept at his residence on Samdech Panh Street, Sangkat Boeung Reang, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh.
Through meetings with senior government officials and interviews on television as well as the Thai media, Dr. Sok Sokretya provided an opportunity to promote the potential of tourism and encourage Thai investors. Invest in tourism in Cambodia as well.
Recently, Dr. Sok Sokretya was invited by Thai Channel 2 (NBT), a well-known television station in Thailand, to give an interview on the topic of tourism in Cambodia.
In this interview, the host asked many questions related to tourism potential in Cambodia, opportunities for investment, as well as Cambodia's strategy to develop and attract tourists to visit Cambodia.
Through those questions, Mr. Sok Sokretya outlined some of Cambodia's strategies to promote and rehabilitate tourism in the aftermath of the Kovid 19 crisis. Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the key factors in the restoration of tourism in Cambodia is the success of the control of Kovid 19 and the vaccination of Kovid 19 achieved as planned.
Mr. Sok Sokretya also confirmed the reception of tourists, vaccinations, as well as easing health check conditions for travelers entering Cambodia.
Dr. Sok Sokretya also presented a plan to import Thai tourists by air, land and sea and working with Thai tour operators to arrange tour packages from Thailand to Cambodia. The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism confirmed that the project could start sending visitors in February 2022.
In this interview, Mr. Sok Sokretya also mentioned the tourism potential in Siem Reap. He said that when they visit Siem Reap, they always think of Angkor Wat. But in this area, not only visit the temple, there are countless other places to visit.
He emphasized in the interview that "most tourists who visit Angkor Wat in the past just look at the temple does not know anything deeper than this. I would like to emphasize that the tourism sector that we are talking about is also religious tourism, and our Ministry of Tourism is raising this project.
In addition to showing the potential of tourism, Mr. Sok Sokretya also presented some good opportunities for investors to invest in tourism in Cambodia with the support and encouragement of the Royal Government.
Mr. Sokretya also highlighted the development of interconnected infrastructure from urban to rural areas, which enables tourism in Cambodia to travel anywhere easily.
Dr. Sok Sokretya "I would like to emphasize that tourists can visit Cambodia by any means convenient, whether by land, sea or air, which means that if we travel by land, the cost can be cheaper. . If the road is to Surin Sisaket province, the road is good almost everywhere.
Before concluding the interview, Mr. Sok Sokretya called on Thai people to visit Cambodia and also encouraged Thai investors to invest in tourism in Cambodia because Cambodia has a policy to promote the development of the sector. Realistic and attractive tourism.
Please note that the interview that Dr. Sok Sokretya conducted with the media in Thailand received a lot of attention and views from the Thai people.
