Speaking at the opening ceremony, Mr. Lim Kean Hor stressed the importance of the Mekong-Lanchang River, which provides water and related resources to help promote economic and social development for the countries along the river, as well as support the livelihoods and The well-being of the people in the whole basin.
The Cambodian Minister of Water Resources stressed that due to challenges including population growth, increasing demand for water, food and energy security in riverine countries and rapid development in the basin, combined with the impact And the risks of climate change are putting pressure on river resources and sustainability.
He affirmed that it is the joint responsibility of all riverside countries to strengthen regional cooperation and work together towards achieving sustainable results in the context of ensuring water security to support sustainable development. Sustainable management and development in the Mekong-Lanchang region.
Minister Lim Kean Hor praised the significant progress and achievements so far in the framework of the Lancang-Mekong Cooperation, which has contributed to the river countries in sustainable and socio-economic development. Help bring about regional prosperity, productivity and tangible results, including water resources cooperation.
He also reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment and readiness to continue to work closer in the spirit of shared responsibility towards achieving common prosperity with inclusive growth and a prosperous future. Sustainable for each river country and for the entire Lancang-Mekong region together.
