Senior trade official asks UNCTAD to help Cambodia become a model country for all least developed countries
(Switzerland): A senior official of the Cambodian Ministry of Commerce has requested the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD) to support WTO negotiations and support Cambodia as a model country for all least developed countries.
Mr. Sok Sopheak said that Cambodia is preparing to leave the Least Developed Countries (LDCs), which needs to develop strategies and policies for the country to ensure continuous development, as Cambodia may lose the benefits that Cambodia Used to be as a less developed country.
At the same time, the representative of the World Trade Organization said that it will look at the practical possibilities to participate with Cambodia in various events and encourage Cambodia to actively participate in the work of the World Trade Organization to take full advantage of Multilateral trading system.
Cambodia has been a member of the World Trade Organization since 2004, enabling Cambodia to take advantage of the multilateral trading system that contributes to Cambodia's economic development.
Please be informed that Cambodia has set a goal by 2030 to become a middle-income country and by 2050 to be a high-middle-income country.
