Speaking to Fresh News on December 6, 2021, Mr. Sok Raden, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association, expressed his happiness and happiness at the news that China is evaluating Cambodia's trout to reach a decision. There are direct exports to the Chinese market.
Mr. Sok Raden said, "On behalf of the Cambodian Fishermen's Association, as well as on my own as a fish farmer, I am pleased and pleased with the news that China may bring trout from Cambodia to China. "Good news for the whole hydropower plant."
Apart from trout, Sok Raden expects that tilapia can also be a target of the Chinese market, as Cambodian tilapia has the capacity to produce because this species is fast growing and has good meat, which is the target of the international market.
Ms. Keo Yada, a fish farmer, also expressed her happiness and joy after receiving the news that Cambodian trout can be exported directly to the Chinese market in the near future.
Ms. Keo Yada said, "It's not just me and the farmers when there is an export or a local market, we are always happy, but just what their export conditions are, what our farmers can accept. Can it be taken? ”
She said that the current situation of fish farming is quiet due to the problem of Kovid-19 and the lack of market, so a large number of fish farming has been suspended and some aquaculture brothers have reduced the number of fish in farming. .
Mr. Chhay Chheang, a fish farmer in Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, is waiting to see the actual situation of the fish that is exported to China, whether to buy fish from the people or buy fish from the company.
Mr. Chhay Chheang also complained about the large import of fish from abroad, which left a lot of local fish, while the current situation in the fish farming market is still normal as usual, only the price of feed for fish has increased, but for fish prices. Not expensive.
On the morning of December 6, 2021, the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, Wang Wentian, announced the good news for Cambodia, with the Chinese side deciding to study and assess the phytosanitary risks of Cambodia's gourds and trout through Remote video system as an important measure. He said that if the evaluation process goes smoothly, the export of trout will be able to export in the near future.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also said that the acceleration of the export of lentils and trout is a major achievement from the recent meeting between Samdech and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang. Also.
