Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Advises to Accelerate Prosecution of Major Drugs and Confiscation Procedures
(Phnom Penh): In the meeting of the National Authority for Combating Drugs on December 6, 2021, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, instructed the relevant ministries and institutions to speed up the trial of perpetrators related to major drugs. And procedures for the immediate confiscation of property.
This is in the direction of 10 points of Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan to submit to the Ministry, institutions, anti-drug units and all stakeholders to carry out their work effectively, including:
First, continue to promote the implementation of operational activities in the 6th Anti-Drug Campaign Plan to be more active, especially to promote the work of the commissions in each sector.
Second, continue to educate and disseminate the dangers of drugs according to the subjects to be educated and the main goals. Prepare to strengthen drug educators in schools and other factories, while the socio-economic situation and the gradual reopening of schools.
Third, continue to expedite the implementation of law enforcement, such as: expediting the prosecution of perpetrators related to major drugs and procedures for confiscation of assets related to drug offenses quickly.
Fourth, continue to strengthen the management and control of chemicals, organize comprehensive training to organize the management structure of chemicals thoroughly.
Fifth, to strengthen the National Center for Treatment and Rehabilitation of Drug Addicts in Preah Sihanouk Province. Prepare the basic conditions for drug addicts to be taken for long-term treatment at the National Center. Strengthen the human resource structure and management at the National Center. Strengthen the quality of doctors providing treatment to drug addicts at 355 community health centers.
Sixth, for the strengthening of sub-national mechanisms, it is necessary to integrate the composition of the Village-Commune-Sangkat-Drug-Free Committee into the composition of the Committee to lead and implement a safe village-commune policy. Request each province to complete drug-free villages by early 2022 to start work. Strengthen BLO mechanisms and 1511 anti-drug operations for border provinces.
Seventh: Complete the preparation of a policy on drug-free villages, communes, and sangkats at the border. Continue to cooperate with the Chinese side on assistance in setting up drug education libraries in the main target schools (one is almost completed at Boeung Trabek High School).
Eighth: Continue to implement the spirit of the 7th Ministerial Meeting on Drugs, which is hosted by Cambodia.
Ninth: Prepare a multi-sectoral policy for the relevant units on drug control.
And 10th: The National Authority for Combating Drugs must prepare all relevant documents to be ready to serve as a staff to the Royal Government in the ASEAN meeting.
