(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has released an official report on the results of inspections and measures to suppress state encroachment in the flooded forest area of the Tonle Sap Lake area in Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom provinces. This is according to the letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of December 6, 2021.
The report details the following:
* A: Kampong Chhnang Province
* First, assign the task of the Anti-Corruption Unit to investigate and take legal action against Chhour Chandoeun, former Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province.
* Second: Confiscation of 2,100.66 hectares of state land in the flooded forest area as defined in Sub-Decree No. 197, dated August 29, 2011, which was illegally occupied. Chronok and Dar communes, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, as attached map and standard table.
* Third: Assign the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to prepare a billboard to disseminate the map of the flooded forest area in the spirit of Sub-Decree No. 197, dated August 29, 2011.
* Fourth: Assign the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration to lead the tree replanting campaign.
* Fifth: Assign the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, Tonle Sap Authority and Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration to take measures to protect state land in the flooded forest area to ensure sustainability and to strengthen the implementation of Royal Government Regulation No. 01 BOP dated July 2, 2010 and Sub-Decree No. 197 dated August 29, 2011.
* 6: Assign the task of Tonle Sap Authority and Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration to dissolve the boundaries of the land and remove the illegally planted land border posts.
* First, assign the task of Kampong Thom Provincial Administration to promote the court proceedings in the case of encroachment on state land in the flooded forest area of the Tonle Sap area.
* Second: Assign the task of Kampong Thom Provincial Administration to lead the specialized unit to prepare the report with map and standard to propose to the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to adjust the boundaries of the two areas in the affected areas.
* Third: Assign the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration and Departments around Kampong Thom Province to continue to take measures to prevent and suppress encroachment on state land in the flooded forest area around the Tonle Sap Lake to ensure sustainability and to strengthen the implementation of Royal Government Regulation No. 01 BOP dated July 2, 2010 and Sub-Decree No. 197 dated August 29, 2011.
* Fourth: To assign the task of Tonle Sap Authority and Kampong Thom Provincial Administration to promote the implementation of Letter No. 1003, dated September 2, 2015 and Letter No. 1044, dated July 22, 2014 of the Office of the Council of Ministers to People can have the right to own and enjoy.
