Phnom Penh Forestry Administration cooperates with the authorities to catch ferocious monkeys that disturb the people living around Wat Phnom
(Phnom Penh): According to the request for intervention from the authorities and the insistence of the people of Village 11 and Village 12, this morning, December 6, 2021, Phnom Penh Forestry Administration District cooperated with the Department of Wildlife of the Forestry Administration and the authorities. Sangkat Khans arrested wild monkeys that attacked and chased the children of villagers in Village 11 and Village 12, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh.
Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration, confirmed that on the order of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and on the instructions of the Director of the Department, he led professional officers and together with local authorities to catch the ferocious monkeys to prevent them. Fear of the people.
On the occasion of capturing the ferocious monkeys, the authorities would like to call on the people living near the monkeys to not be alarmed, because the officers captured the monkeys and released them at the animal care center. Safe. May you live in peace.
There are nearly 20 monkeys released by the authorities and experts at Phnom Takhmao Zoo and will continue to be hunted until the wild animals no longer disturb the people living around Wat Phnom.
It should be noted that the residents of Wat Phnom, Srah Chak and Phsar Chas communes in Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh have expressed concern about the safety of small children as well as household items, claiming that recently there have been large and ferocious monkeys. Some invaded their homes, causing great fear because some of the monkeys were aggressive and could bite or destroy property in people's homes.
Residents disturbed by the monkeys said that some of the monkeys were very aggressive and invaded people's homes. At the same time, they requested the local authorities as well as professional officers to arrest and take care of them because they had children and their children who had been bitten by ferocious monkeys.
Residents say they no longer dare to open doors and windows because they are afraid of monkeys entering the house. The child was taken to the hospital, while the items left on the porch were also bitten or destroyed by monkeys.
