China promises to open all direct flights with Cambodia and encourage Chinese tourists and investors to come to Cambodia
(China): Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, affirmed in front of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, that China will encourage Chinese tourists and investors to come to Cambodia and Consider opening all direct flights between the two countries.
In addition, the Chinese diplomat also promised to facilitate the return of Cambodian students to study in China.
As for economic cooperation, the two foreign ministers noted with satisfaction the growth of bilateral trade during the Kovid-19 pandemic.
The two sides also welcomed the entry into force of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement early next year and pledged to make the most of the agreement. Both to boost bilateral trade to 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also thanked the Chinese friends for their commitment to increase the import of Cambodian agricultural products into the Chinese market.
Wang Yi reiterated China's support for infrastructure development and other projects, as well as Cambodia's post-crisis economic recovery efforts.
According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), as of October 2021, Chinese investment in Cambodia totaled more than 27 billion US dollars.
