Cambodia reaffirms its commitment to enhancing relations between the Indian Ocean countries and ASEAN, especially during its chairmanship of ASEAN
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has reaffirmed its commitment to enhancing relations between the Indian Ocean countries and the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), especially during Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN next year.
This was stated by Mr. Ouch Borith, Deputy Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, during his speech at the 5th Indian Ocean Conference in Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates on 04- December 05, 2021.
"I would like to reaffirm Cambodia's strong commitment to promoting mutual relations between the Indian Ocean countries and ASEAN, especially when Cambodia will play an important role," he said. "ASEAN chair from January 2022 so that we can all build harmony, peace, sustainability and prosperity for the whole region."
Related to the above topic, according to Mr. Ouch Borith said that the Indian Ocean is a major sea route that connects the Middle East, Africa and East Asia with Europe and the United States. These major shipping lanes facilitate maritime trade in the Indian Ocean, which holds more than half of the world's oil and hosts 23 of the world's top 100 container ports.
With the Kovid-19 crisis expected to ease in the near future, Ouch Borith added that improving the flow of trade, business and investment in line with global change It is an important and urgent task to restore and promote the socio-economic development of the Indian Ocean region.
"International trade is an important engine for economic growth and job creation. "With the changing trends in trade and the global supply chain, I see the Indian Ocean region paying more attention to supporting the multilateral trading system, especially the further strengthening of trade liberalization." This is according to Mr. Ouch Borith.
In addition, adaptation to new norms will further accelerate the adoption of digital technologies for industrial development and economic industrialization. Therefore, we must work together to push the Fourth Industrial Revolution to the maximum to create a new pillar of resilient growth. Five killed after Myanmar security forces crash into protesters in Rangoon
