(Phnom Penh): The President of the Cambodian Dermatologist Association, Dr. Chan Vichet, called on people to be more aware of skin health problems, not to choose products that make the skin white faster, which has a serious impact on skin health to the point of danger. To life.
Dr. Chan Vichet said that some people are currently affected by the use of medicines, skin care products and care or without the control and permission of the Ministry of Health, especially the distribution of these products through social media. Or online, which has affected the health of the skin or serious complications can affect life.
In addition, some people are suffering from the consequences of services such as Botox Fillers injections and cosmetic surgery by doctors or beauty salon owners who are not properly trained and licensed.
"The use of peeling products or skin whitening products without proper regulations and recognized by the Ministry of Health is extremely dangerous to the health of the skin, causing rashes, redness, bruising, acne, wrinkles and stretch marks. Sometimes it leads to loss of life. Therefore, before using any product, you must know how to choose a product or consult a doctor to avoid using the same product, especially peeling skin and fast.
This statement was made by Dr. Chan Vichet at the 6th Annual Meeting of the Cambodian Dermatologists Association Online, held at Sofitel Angkor Phokitra Hotel, Siem Reap, under the theme "Kovid Dermatitis". 19 "which lasts for 2 days, 3-4 December 2021.
He said that the 6th annual meeting of the Cambodian Dermatologists Association to discuss and strengthen the unity of the association together to raise awareness of people who have previously used non-technical products and formulas. Recognized by the Ministry of Health.
In this meeting, the association also elected the executive committee of the Cambodian Dermatologists Association for the new mandate for 2022-2023, in which the members of the association elected Dr. Chan Vichet as the president of the association for the fifth mandate.
