Sihanoukville beach area is beautiful, no garbage under the attention of relevant officials
(Sihanoukville): The Cambodian government is working to turn Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose special economic zone, as this coastal province is one of Cambodia's key economic boosters due in large part to trade, logistics and tourism. Home, etc.
Therefore, in order for this coastal province to have potential, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, led by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, the provincial governor, has tried to change the face of this coastal province to be more beautiful, that is, to organize the coastal area in the city. Sihanoukville no longer has garbage, while now the cleaning staff of Sihanoukville cleans every day to maintain a clean, hygienic and aesthetic environment that attracts tourists.
The new status of Sihanoukville as a multi-purpose special economic zone reflects the Cambodian government's ambitions to develop the provinces and the capital to become an important player for production and trade that boosts exports. With more investment in infrastructure and incentives, Sihanoukville has become one of the most attractive destinations for foreign investment in Cambodia.
Speaking to reporters during the preparations for the 7th East Asia Sea Summit in 2021, Mr. Ey Sok Leng said that the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration has selected two companies to collect garbage with 320 sanitation workers to clean up. The beach will work on garbage collection on the beach and elsewhere in Sihanoukville and there will be 108 garbage trucks to the landfill.
He said that the municipal administration has set people to dispose of their garbage at the designated location at night from 7 pm to 3 am to facilitate the collection and transport to the dump, otherwise Will be fined between 20,000 riel and 400,000 riel, while the company's delay in collecting garbage is also fined according to the contract with the municipal administration.
Separately, Mr. Samuth Sothearith, Director of the Department of Environment of Sihanoukville said that all of the company's garbage trucks are equipped with GPS tracking, while the waste in Sihanoukville is between 350 to 400 tons per day.
He said that the amount of garbage on the beach on a normal day is small, but for big holidays, the number has doubled, which at this point, both the relevant authorities as well as company staff must work together to collect in time. Maintain a clean, hygienic and aesthetic environment for tourists.
Separately, Mr. Hok Sophannaro, Managing Director of Sihanoukville Solid Waste Landfill, said that currently between 400 and 500 tons of waste collected from Sihanoukville and Prey Nup districts per day. To dump at the new technical standard landfill in O Ta Sek village, O Oknha Heng commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province, about 3 km down from National Road 4.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, the first technical landfill in Sihanoukville in the first phase was dug four different pits on more than 5 hectares of land. It burys seven layers of garbage and is 21 meters high, which is estimated to hold nearly 1 million tons of garbage in five years.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that the guards and the demarcation of the border for swimmers is to ensure safety as well as give confidence to tourists who visit the beautiful beach in Sihanoukville, especially to tourists. The provincial governor said that so far, officials are building 12 more coast guard towers to be ready to rescue people and foreign tourists in the event of an accident.
According to the provincial governor, the tower for guarding the safety of tourists has been set up according to the actual situation, while not having enough human resources capable of rescuing when tourists are in danger due to More than 20 more drowning officials will be sent to the drowning rescue school.
He called on people, especially tourists, to be extra careful when visiting the water in any location, have airbags and do not visit the sea where there are big waves and deep water. In addition, for beach vendors to participate in maintaining the cleanliness of the environment in their locations to be clean, because the clean environment can attract tourists and increase revenue because guests need clean and good environment.
