The Center for Strategic and Rhetoric Eyes and the Asian Vision Institute join hands to promote research on economic diplomacy and regional-international affairs
(Phnom Penh): The Center for Strategic Networks - Rhetoric and the Asian Vision Institute (AVI), which represented the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on December 3, 2021 to promote research on diplomacy, economy and regional and international affairs. Both co-organize training programs to develop the capacity of young people.
During the signing ceremony, Dr. Chheang Vannarith, President of the Asian Vision Institute (AVI), said that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between the Center for Strategic and Rhetoric Networks and the Asia Vision Institute is a joint commitment to increase the work. Research and dialogue in the field of international affairs.
Dr. Chheang Vannarith added that this MOU will provide an opportunity for young people and young leaders to better understand Cambodia's diplomacy, economy, politics, foreign affairs and geopolitical situation in the region through various training from the two institutes. Well.
"For research, the two research institutions will continue to work together on economic diplomacy to raise awareness among young people about economic diplomacy strategy," he said.
Mr. Sam Ath Chansomith, Executive Director of the Center for Strategic-Rhetoric Networks, also confirmed that the signing of this MOU will lead the youth to participate in research and participate in discussions on policy dialogues. At this point, Mr. Sam Ath Chansometh stressed that all those contributions are worth it.
The forum of the research institution is to value diversity, adhere to a constructive spirit and environment in inviting all stakeholders and stakeholders to discuss and find solutions to key policy issues facing Cambodia.
Mr. Sam Ath Chansometh also expressed his commitment that the two institutes will focus on how to promote joint research projects and organize training programs for young people, as well as policy dialogues related to foreign policy and Economic diplomacy.
