Landfill in Sihanoukville is the first landfill in Cambodia built in accordance with proper technical standards
"Sihanoukville:" The landfill in Sihanoukville is the first landfill in Cambodia to be built in accordance with proper technical standards. " This is the statement made by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment on November 30, 2021, during a group of journalists on a visit to learn about solid waste management at a landfill in Preah Vihear province. Sihanouk.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the landfill in Sihanoukville is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia implemented by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and transferred under the control and operation of the Ministry of Environment on November 5, 2021.
The senior official said that according to the technical standards built by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the site will be a five-year landfill with four pits of more than five hectares that can bury seven layers of rubbish and be 21 meters high. The calculation can hold nearly 1 million tons of garbage.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, in 2022, at least six such standardized landfills will be launched as a collaboration between the Royal Government and development partners, including the Asian Development Bank and the World Bank. .
According to the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, for the project that the Royal Government cooperates with development partners to establish a technical landfill and is scheduled to open during 2022, such as landfills in Kep, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Kampot.
At the same time, the Royal Government through the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Ministry of Environment will work with more partners to build landfills in accordance with the technology, such as Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, etc., which is the goal of the Royal Government to manage solid waste well. The purpose of the national solid waste management policy implemented by the Royal Government.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that the goal of the Royal Government is to manage solid waste well as part of the national policy and, more importantly, the Ministry of Environment will continue to provide technical assistance to train officials in sub-national administration. Manage garbage in the town.
Regarding the issue of garbage, the Secretary of State added that more than 10,000 tons of garbage is generated per day, and about 4 million tons per year. Separately, in Sihanoukville, between 350 and 400 tons of garbage is generated per day. According to the study, 65% of this waste is organic waste, 20% is plastic waste and the rest is solid waste.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra pointed out that the Ministry of Environment has encouraged the separation of technical waste and recycling to reduce the amount of waste to be dumped on the field, because waste is economically valuable if we separate. By type and recycling.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that with an annual increase of between 10 and 15%, the landfill, which is planned to be dumped for five years, could be changed and could not be used at any time due to the increase in waste and confiscation. To process is still limited. For Sihanoukville, the Royal Government is paying attention to waste management because it is a target province to become a multi-purpose special economic zone.
He added that at the landfill in the province, in addition to the standard garbage disposal, they still make the right distribution, in which each type of waste can be recycled according to its own type.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inspects the possibility of opening the Thmar Da International Border Crossing
(Pursat): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, December 4, 2021, inspected and studied the possibility of opening Thmor Da International Border Crossing in Thmor Da Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province. Trat of Thailand.
The trip was attended by the technical team of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Ministry leaders, technical officials and stakeholders, and Tycoon Try Pheap, CEO of Try Pheap Group, which is developing in the area.
The Thmar Da border crossing has been becoming an attractive area after the Royal Government of Cambodia built National Road 55 connecting the provincial town to that area. In particular, this area, which is highly conducive to natural tourism, has been eager for tourists to visit. Currently, Cambodians in the area often cross into Thailand through this port to exchange goods.
It should be noted that this port is planned to build various infrastructures, including: immigration building, customs and excise building for joint inspection, parking for the transfer of goods through the warehouse, container yard and administrative building and dormitory building to open up opportunities for cooperation. International investment, cross-border trade, job creation and tourist attraction are also aimed at boosting the economy, family and society of the two nations.
Deputy Prime Minister Pravid Vongsovan's promise was made during a recent courtesy call and a working conversation with Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism. The meeting was held at the house of Mr. Pravid Vongsovan directly in the barracks "R1".
During the cordial and sympathetic discussions, Deputy Prime Minister Prawit Vongsovan and Dr. Sok Sokretya discussed a wide range of issues related to Cambodia-Thailand relations and cooperation. Mr. Pravid sent his condolences and greetings to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and reminded of the good relations between him and Samdech Techo Prime Minister and many other senior Cambodian leaders.
Mr. Pravid Vongsovan also expressed his appreciation for the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to bring Cambodia full peace and rapid development in all areas. He also expressed the Thai government's position to continue to improve the traditional relations and cooperation between the two countries.
During the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya requested the Thai Deputy Prime Minister to continue to promote good cooperation in trade exchanges along the Cambodian-Thai border, the fight against false information, the suppression of human trafficking crimes and the prevention of opposition groups using social media from the country. Thailand to attack the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as to fight drug trafficking crimes along the Cambodian-Thai border.
In response to this request, Pravid Vongsovan promised to prevent all illegal activities and against the Royal Government of Cambodia. The former Thai Deputy Prime Minister has claimed that he will not allow anyone to take Thai territory to take action against the Royal Government of Cambodia.
It is noteworthy that in recent times, a number of people who insulted the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia and acted against the Royal Government of Cambodia have been arrested by the Thai authorities and handed over to the Cambodian authorities.
