Kampong Chhnang Provincial Governor Allows More Than 1,000 Families in Chronok Commune to Farm in Three Areas for Another Season, But After Harvesting, Land Must Be Returned to the State
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, on the morning of December 4, 2021, said to the farmers in Chronok Commune, Kampong Leng District that at their request through Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Another season of rice cultivation is allowed on the land in three areas in the mainland after the confiscation, but after the harvest, the farmers have to return all the land in the three areas as state property.
Regarding the request of the people, Mr. Chhum Chieng, Chief of Chronok Commune, said that Chronok Commune has 4 villages and a total of 1,928 families, of which 1,602 families are farmers in 3 areas. In fact, there are 118 families who have already sown in three areas. In addition, all the farmers have transported the rice seeds by fertilizer by boat when the water rises to the hills where the rice fields are ready to be fertilized.
In that, the working group distributed in 2 different locations: at Peam Bang Primary School for 190 families and Wat Pov Veay for 587 families on December 3, 2021.
