(Phnom Penh): A group of Cham youths, known as Cham youths, have jointly organized an exhibition of traditional cakes of their people under the program "Cham Cham Traditional Cake Day" for the public to visit freely on Saturday, December 4. 2021 tomorrow from 3 pm to 6 pm.
Mr. Lap Ker added that all the cakes in the program are handmade, without any molds or aids, and made especially by the Cham community in the area, mostly from Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Tralach district. In this event, there is also the Cham drum (Bana drum or Yike drum), a traditional song that the Cham people always celebrate during the flower festival (Mao Lut), weddings, weddings, anniversaries and many other ceremonies. More.
This program is supported and supported by the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, allowing the day to be organized at the Khmer Kite Museum (opposite the new National Assembly) from 3pm to 6pm.
