Cambodian Red Cross Provides Humanitarian Donations to 777 Families in Peam Bang Commune, Stong District
(Kampong Thom): Mrs. Hourn Chanbora, Director of the Department of Communications of the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, on December 3, 2021, distributed humanitarian donations in the form of materials and food items of the Cambodian Red Cross. To 777 poor families in Peam Bang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Say Kimlam, Governor of Stong District, reported that there are 13 communes in Stong District. Give them hardships and livelihoods due to insufficient fishing, lack of morning, lack of evening, lack of morning, lack of morning.
Mrs. Hourn Chanbora conveyed the greetings and greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all the people and assigned the Central Red Cross Working Group together with the Chairman of the Branch Committee. The Cambodian Red Cross in Kampong Thom province brings gifts to parents and siblings who are experiencing difficulties at this time.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak stated that these donations came from the Red Cross Volunteer Agency, the village chief, the commune chief, who conducted home-based research on people's livelihood issues, and reported to the provincial Red Cross branch to the Central Red Cross. Due to the difficulties of the people, Samdech Kittipritthbandit decided to assign a working group and bring these gifts to distribute to the people who are experiencing difficulties in a timely manner.
In addition, Mr. Nguon Rattanak called on all people living on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake to participate in the conservation of protected areas to protect natural resources to be abundant and sustainable for future generations.
He said that the provision of food and supplies today is not divided by caste, color or party affiliation, but to provide families with real difficulties.
He said that although today's small humanitarian donations do not help people in the long run, but it can help people solve difficult times for a while and be very careful about hygiene, such as eating raw meat. Raw vegetables, raw water that causes diarrhea, various infectious diseases that affect health.
It should be informed that the material received in each family is 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of shirt. Stung Treng Municipality Organizes a Workshop on Three-Year Rolling Investment Program Integration (2022-2024)
