Sihanoukville authorities build towers along the coast and deploy experts for patrols after a series of drownings
(Sihanoukville): After a series of drowning deaths while visiting the sea, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration has set up a tower along the coast for guards to wait for rescue and security demarcation. For water players and so on.
In fact, after the Royal Government reopened to the public within the framework of internal tourism after the relief of the outbreak of Kovid 19, 6 people died from drowning in the coastal area in Sihanoukville.
Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Sihanoukville Province, told reporters during the preparations for the 7th East Asia Sea Conference in 2021: Set up airbags in the coastal area where tourists visit. "This tower can save tourists in the event of an accident."
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that the guards and the demarcation of the border for swimmers is to ensure safety as well as give confidence to tourists who visit the beautiful beach in Sihanoukville, especially to tourists. Play water.
The provincial governor said that so far, officials are building 12 more coast guard towers to be ready to rescue people and foreign tourists in the event of an accident.
Kouch Chamroeun said, "The guards must be aware of the methods of rescuing drowning tourists, not just whistling."
