(Sihanoukville): The 7th East Asia Sea Conference, hosted by Cambodia for the first time for two days from December 1-2, 2021, has successfully concluded.
There are 11 PEMSEA member countries, including Cambodia, Singapore, Laos, the Philippines, Indonesia, Vietnam, Timor-Leste, China, South Korea, North Korea, Japan and many other partner organizations.
"The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Environment and the administration of the four coastal provinces, has developed policies, strategic plans for coastal conservation, marine resources, including the reduction of marine pollution and "Adapting to climate change, improving the well-being of the sea and the livelihoods of people in communities living along the coast and islands."
The spokesman said the world would be more aware of the potential of Cambodia's coastal provinces, including Sihanoukville, Kampot, Koh Kong and Kep, which have beautiful beaches for 440 km. Also among the most beautiful beaches in the world.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun added that the East Asia Marine Environmental Management Network is committed to working together as a network to effectively implement the PNLG Action Plan 2022-2030 in line with three major programs:
* First: Strengthen governance and partnership
* Second: Participation in the implementation of management programs related to the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs): Goal 6 on water use and management, Goal 11 on marine protection and pollution reduction, Goal 1 13 on climate change mitigation and disaster risk reduction, Goal 14 on biodiversity conservation and ecosystem restoration.
* Third: Improve management, evaluation and reporting as network members to develop sustainable activities for the new decade with renewed commitment at the regional and international levels, such as the Strategic Plan for Sustainable Development for the East Asia Sea. SDS SEA) 2023-2027 and PEMSEA 2030 Roadmap for Biodiversity Development Framework and Strategic Plan for Coastal and Marine Development.
It should be recalled that the Ministry of Environment hosted the East Asia Maritime Conference 2021 and the 7th Ministerial Forum on Partnership in East Sea Environment Management under the theme "Creating a new decade of human and maritime welfare". Economy ”which took place for two days from December 1 to 2, 2021 in Sihanoukville.
The main objectives of the Maritime Conference include:
* First: Share lessons as experiences, monitor past work progress and expand the implementation of strategies implemented at the regional, national and sub-national levels.
* Second, establish and reorganize existing management mechanisms and promote the creation of new opportunities for regional partnerships through innovative technologies, investment and financing to sustain the coastal and marine environment.
* Third: Define a clear roadmap for solutions to maritime issues in the coming decades, in accordance with the United Nations Decade of Action for Ocean Science, Agenda 2030, United Nations Framework Convention The nation on climate change and the global biodiversity framework after 2020, as well as related frameworks.
