(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Economy, will take more drastic measures to strengthen the capacity and governance of officials in charge of revenue collection. In particular, the fiscal revenue consists of the General Department of Taxation and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia for the benefit of the national budget.
"This is an important key that provides appropriate and adequate resources to the government as well as the development of political programs," said Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth.
He added that in addition to strengthening the collection of fiscal revenue, non-tax revenue is also important and the Royal Government will continue to take sharp measures in various frameworks.
He said the ministry was currently preparing to finalize a draft law on non-tax revenue, which could be finalized in the near future, as part of strengthening governance to manage revenue, both tax revenue and revenue. Not fiscal.
