(Phnom Penh): Real estate and construction experts have presented various tips to the public to rehabilitate the business after the business was affected by Kovid 19 in the past.
Four Cambodian experts participated in a panel discussion on "Guide to Business Recovery in the Context 19 in Real Estate and Construction" organized by the Cambodian Young Entrepreneurs Association. Online on December 2, 2021.
Oknha Dr. Kim Heang, President of KW Cambodia, said that in fact, in the context of Kovid 19, almost everyone has faced many challenges in terms of business, so to keep the business going. To recover, business owners need to have the cooperation of partners, which means finding partners to rebuild the business.
He said that each business owner can share by selling shares of their business to a partner to get working capital to keep the business alive.
"Obviously, my own company has been affected by Kovid 19 for almost two years, but the factor that keeps the company afloat as it is today is the maintenance of human resources," he said.
Mr. Din Somethearith, President of the Cambodian Hotel Association and Founder and General Director of Phka Trakoun Village, said that in addition to maintaining human resources, sharing to keep the business afloat is not forgetting to do something. Have a clear plan When there is a clear plan, any obstacles can be solved. Another factor is debt management, debt management must be good and use the right circumstances.
Dr. Ieng Sotheara, Cambodian-Japanese Trade and Investment Association and co-founder of Arakawa Residence, said that the above factors are a good key to the recovery of the business, but the most important part is the preparation and maintenance. Maintain good physical health, mental health and strengthen the ability to stay. To take care of physical health is to get enough rest, eat a healthy diet.
The doctor stated that for mental health, it is necessary to meditate well, prepare the mind well, do not get angry too much, make the mind happy and so on. Another point is to strengthen the capacity, both the ability to make money and the ability to knowledge must be strengthened.
In addition to sharing tips on how to recover a business after being affected by Kovid 19, experts also presented and shared about the real estate sector.
He said that in the case of low-middle-income Boreys, middle-income and high-income Boreys have only a small impact on lower-middle-income Boreys, but expensive and middle-income Boreys are not yet affected. Not much affected because the 19 outbreak of Kovid affected the income of the poor, but not the rich.
Dr. confirmed that in the next 2-3 years, real estate traders still have the opportunity to profit and there are no problems, but if investors have to invest in real estate to invest. Use the money you have without borrowing money from anyone to invest, because borrowing money to invest will not be profitable because you have to pay interest back to the original owner.
Dr. Ieng Sotheara also mentioned the vision of the real estate sector over the next 2-3 years that if the disease of Kovid 19 gradually decreased and the business people have recovered and the workers can have a return on income, so for The real estate sector will be in a better position.
