China translates biographies of Quan and 9 other books to be kept in the National Library
(Phnom Penh): The book "Life of Quan: Territory and Tradition of the People of Chenla" and 9 other good books related to the history of Cambodia-China relations, philosophy, culture were handed over to the Cambodian side by the Chinese side for study For the general public, after being officially translated from Chinese into Khmer.
These 10 books, a total of 100 books, were donated by the People's Publishing House of Jiangxi Province of the People's Republic of China to the National Library of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the morning of December 3, 2021. This cooperation was facilitated by Dr. Chea Monirith, President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association.
Qian Yuankang, director of the Chinese Cultural Center in Cambodia and a representative of the Jiangxi Provincial People's Publishing House, said the books would be kept in the National Library to be used as a research document for the general public.
Ms. Khlot Vibola, Director of the National Library, expressed her appreciation and appreciation to the Jiangxi People's Publishing House for its active contribution in strengthening and expanding the people-to-people ties through historical documents and Culture.
Ms. Khlot Vibola said that these documents will be an important bibliography (lecture series) for scholars of the history of relations between Cambodia and China, along with a better understanding of Chinese culture and history.
