Anti-Counterfeiting Commission Educates and Contracts Garage Owners Who Buy and Sell MOBIL Lubricants in Infringement of Intellectual Property
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Counterfeit Products Commission has educated and contracted the owners of garages, washing and oil change stations in Phnom Penh, some of which continue to buy and sell MOBIL lubricants in violation of intellectual property rights.
Police from the Secretariat of the Anti-Counterfeit Products Commission inspected and found that some garages and car washes, motorcycles, and engine oil change continue to buy and sell MOBIL lubricants of unknown origin, and the police educated and instructed Contracts to stop buying and selling and to buy from companies that have the right to import a clear source to avoid buying and selling counterfeit products.
