500,000 doses of vaccine vaccine and three Cambodian vaccine trucks to be handed over to Lao government on Friday
(Phnom Penh): 500,000 doses of 19 vaccines against Kovid and 3 trucks of vaccines donated by the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia will be handed over to the Government of Laos on Friday morning, December 3, 2021 for use in The fight against Kovid 19. This is according to Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, who confirmed to Fresh News on December 2, 2021.
Ms. O Vandin said that the handover ceremony was held on the Cambodia-Laos border at the border between Stung Treng and Champasak provinces, with the Cambodian side led by Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, accompanied by Secretary of State O Vandin. As Chairman of the Commission for the 19th Framework for Kovid vaccination nationwide.
