(Phnom Penh): 500,000 doses of 19 vaccines against Kovid and 3 trucks of vaccines donated by the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia will be handed over to the Lao government on Friday morning, December 3, 2021. To be used in the fight against Kovid 19. This is according to Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, who confirmed to Fresh News on December 2, 2021.
Ms. O Vandin said that the handover ceremony was held on the Cambodia-Laos border at the border between Stung Treng and Champasak provinces, with the Cambodian side led by Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, accompanied by Secretary of State O Vandin. As Chairman of the Commission for 19 Kovid vaccines nationwide.
In connection with the fight against Kovid 19, in 2020, the Royal Government of Cambodia provided 2 million humanitarian aid and 11 other medical facilities to the Government of Laos. In addition, on September 29, 2021, the Royal Government of Cambodia also provided 200,000 doses of Sinovak vaccine to Laos.
