Cambodian Chamber of Commerce signs MOU with Philippine Chamber of Commerce and Industry to promote and strengthen economic and business cooperation between the two countries
The signing of the MoU took place during the third meeting of the Joint Commission on Cambodia-Philippines Bilateral Cooperation, chaired by Mr. Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia; The Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of the Philippines, Mr. T. L. Sen., will be joined by senior officials of both countries and stakeholders.
The two chambers of commerce will regularly share information with each other, as well as organize business and investment missions, seminars, conferences, exhibitions and business meetings. In line with the above objectives, the two chambers of commerce also agreed to establish the Philippine-Cambodia Business Council, headquartered in the Republic of the Philippines, and the Cambodia-Philippines Business Council, headquartered in Cambodia, to discuss, plan and implement joint work. Also.
