Senior Minister Osman Hassan asks Turkey to help develop Phnom Penh Islamic Center to boost Khmer Muslim community economy
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Osman Hassan, President of the Islamic Center of Phnom Penh, requested the Turkish Cooperation and Coordination Agency (TIKA) to review the possibility of developing the Phnom Penh Islamic Center to boost the economy of the Khmer Muslim community, especially the provision of scholarships to students to help children. Orphans, the elderly, the poor, and so on.
On this occasion, the Senior Minister gave a presentation to the delegation on the history of the location of the center and mentioned the main master plan for the development of this area.
The Senior Minister requested TIKA to review the feasibility of helping to develop the Islamic Center in Phnom Penh in order to boost the economy of the Khmer Muslim community, as well as to join the Royal Government of Cambodia for the development of society as a whole.
He said, "The location of the Islamic Center in Phnom Penh, which already has the Al-Sar Mosque in Boeung Kak, Phnom Penh, will be developed to get back the economic resources to support and develop the Cambodian Muslim community in some areas, especially the provision of scholarships to students." Students, orphans, the elderly, the poor and so on.
The Senior Minister also requested TIKA to review the possibility of helping to develop this location to boost the economy of the Khmer Muslim community, as well as to join the Royal Government of Cambodia for the development of society as a whole.
In response, the Turkish side TIKA has expressed its full support for the projects and accepted the senior minister's request for further study, promising to facilitate co-operation in supporting the projects.
The Turkish Cooperation and Development Agency (TIKA), a national agency of the Republic of Turkey, was established in 1992 with the aim of providing technical assistance to developing countries in the fields of economy, trade, agriculture, culture, technology, education and social development. Through the development of projects and programs.
