Senior Minister Osman Hassan Meets with Turkish Cooperation and Coordination Agency to Focus on Humanitarian and Education Work
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of December 2, 2021, Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions, met with a delegation from the Turkish Cooperation and Coordination Agency (TIKA) led by Ms. AYDA UNLU, Ambassador of the Republic of Turkey to the Kingdom. Kingdom of Cambodia at the Peace Palace.
The discussions focused on strengthening cooperation in humanitarian affairs, education, vocational training and other activities to contribute to the development of the Cambodian Islamic community as well as society as a whole.
TIKA was established in 1992 with the aim of providing technical assistance to developing countries in the fields of economy, trade, agriculture, culture, technology, education and social development through the development of projects and programs.
TIKA is headquartered in 60 countries, cooperating in more than 150 countries, with a focus on technical cooperation for human resource development. TIKA also finances infrastructure projects such as irrigation, sanitation and transportation projects, as well as the construction and renovation of schools, hospitals, architecture and humanitarian assistance.
Given the vast scope and vibrant activities of TIKA across the globe, Senior Minister Osman Hassan also requested that TIKA be headquartered in Cambodia to facilitate cooperation in various fields.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also asked TIKA to provide scholarships for Cambodian students to continue their studies at universities in Turkey, especially for halal technical assistance and humanitarian assistance and disaster relief.
In response, TIKA accepted the offer and pledged to continue to be a good partner to strengthen cooperation in this regard. Lawyer Ky Tech would like to express his full support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement in support of His Excellency Hun Manet as the future candidate for Prime Minister
