(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Osman Hassan, President of the Phnom Penh Islamic Center, stated that the location of the Phnom Penh Islamic Center already has the Al-Sarq Mosque at Boeung Kak Lake in Phnom Penh and will be developed to regain economic resources to support and develop the Khmer Muslim community. Cambodia in some fields, especially the provision of scholarships to students, orphans, the elderly, the poor and so on.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan on the occasion of receiving a working delegation from the Turkish Cooperation and Coordination Agency (TIKA) led by Mr. AYDA UNLU, Ambassador of Turkey to the Kingdom of Cambodia at the Islamic Center in Phnom Penh on the afternoon of December 2. This year 2021.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan presented a delegation to the delegation on the history of the center's location and outlined key master plans for the development of the compound. The Senior Minister also requested TIKA to review the possibility of helping to develop this location to promote the economy of the Khmer Muslim community, as well as to join the Royal Government of Cambodia to develop the whole society.
