Vietnam: 18 missing in floods, landslides in central country
HANOI, Dec. 2 (Xinhua) - At least 18 people are missing after floods and landslides triggered by heavy rains hit Vietnam on Thursday, December 2, 2021. Central of this Southeast Asian country. Many homes were destroyed and many roads were damaged. This is according to a release by Reuters.
Vietnam is very vulnerable to rainstorms and floods due to its long coastline. Natural disasters, mostly floods and landslides caused by rainstorms, killed 378 people by 2020. Admiral Srun Saroeun, Deputy Commander of the Navy, would like to express his full support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement in support of His Excellency Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister.
