Cambodia-Turkey to expand cooperation on humanitarian work, education, vocational training through the Cambodian Islamic community
(Phnom Penh): Turkey, through the Turkish Agency for Development and Cooperation (TIKA), will expand cooperation with Cambodia on humanitarian work, education, vocational training and other activities to contribute to the development of the Cambodian Islamic community, as well as The whole Cambodian society.
This cooperation was discussed during a working meeting between Senior Minister Osman Hassan and a delegation from the Turkish Agency for Development and Cooperation (TIKA) led by Ms. AYDA UNLU, Turkish Ambassador to Cambodia on the afternoon of the 2nd. December 2021 at the Peace Palace.
TIKA was established in 1992 with the aim of providing technical assistance to developing countries in the fields of economy, trade, culture, technology, education and social development through the development of projects and programs.
TIKA is headquartered in 60 countries, cooperating in more than 150 countries, with the main activities being technical cooperation for human resource development. TIKA also funds infrastructure projects such as irrigation, sanitation and transportation projects, as well as the construction and renovation of schools, hospitals, architecture and humanitarian assistance.
For Cambodia, through TIKA, Cambodian students receive scholarships to continue their studies at universities in Turkey and to assist in humanitarian work, such as distributing beef, vending programs and disaster relief.
During the meeting, Senior Minister Osman Hassan went to Ms. Ida Unloo to set up a TIKA office in Cambodia to expand cooperation on humanitarian work, education and vocational training.
