Ministry of Education allows the launch of activities and services in private educational institutions
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on December 2, 2021 issued a notification on the permission to launch activities and services to support the process of learning and teaching in bulk in private educational institutions.
The Ministry of Education has approved the start of the process of learning and teaching in private schools in the phase of full national re-opening in all fields and living with Kovid 19 "in a new normal path". A set for general education institutions and the reopening of higher education institutions.
To support this phase and in accordance with the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has decided to allow the launch of activities and services to support the learning and teaching process in the following private educational institutions. Under:
The launch of activities and services to support the learning and teaching process as described above will be implemented in accordance with the "Standard Operating Procedures (SOP)" on school bus services, library services, physical education and sports activities, arts activities and canteen services. In public and private educational institutions in the context of Kovid-19 disease, dated October 22, 2021 "and other guidelines in force.
Private schools wishing to launch the above activities and services must first consult with their parents and guardians.
