Svay Rieng Municipality Administration Starts Ordering and Dismantling Balconies That Violate Street Food at Veal Yon Market After Vendors Do Not Listen to Instructions
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Sor Sodany, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng City, claimed that from December 2, 2021, the authorities will use hot measures to organize order and dismantle the porch to stop understanding some groups of traders who sell street food at the market. Mechanical field.
He said that following the instructions of the municipal administration today, he led the force to implement order by using hot measures against some vendors who sell food on public roads, causing traffic jams after several instructions. Sa remains stubborn, refusing to follow the instructions around the field market.
He added that the Svay Rieng Municipality has disseminated information through the microphone, written warning letter and all other means, to raise awareness among traders to cooperate with the municipal administration.
As for sales, they are happy to sell goods and make a better life, but there are also some traders who imitate each other without thinking of common interests, but only think of winning and losing each other. Trafficking in street food, and as a municipal authority, is also unhappy.
People traveling around Veal Yont Market are very enthusiastic about the Svay Rieng Municipality administration, led by the Deputy Mayor and the forces, as well as the team that organized a large traffic order, easy to pass through without congestion as before.
Siem Reap Provincial Authority and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management chaired a meeting to investigate deforestation in the Tonle Sap Lake area in Chi Kreng district.
(Siem Reap): Mr. Leang Monirith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Representative of the Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, held an emergency meeting at Chi Kreng District Hall to review the area data map in Area 2 and Area 3. The jurisdiction of the Chi Kreng district administration to prevent corrupt people from stealing and destroying the flooded forest area of Tonle Sap Lake.
According to the report of the Director of Fisheries Administration of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, from 2016 to 2021, there were 86 cases of encroachment on flooded forests in three areas in the seven Tonle Sap communes of the district. Chi Kreng covers an area of 745.88 hectares and has identified the perpetrators and perpetrators to court.
He added that the flooded forest is important for spawning fish habitats and biodiversity in the Tonle Sap Lake, but if the flooded forest disappears every year, it will greatly affect biodiversity, especially fish production and There is a decrease every year as well as birds.
Mr. Aphi added that the inspection of the flooded forest at this time is difficult to determine the area because the water has not receded and can not clearly see the lost forest area.
