Minister Chea Vandeth Announces Winners of 2021 Information and Communication Technology Award
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Information and Communication Technology Awards 2021 announced the winners of the year under the chairmanship of Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, with the participation of distinguished guests from ministries, public institutions, the private sector, new business community and development partners. Organized at the Innovation Center of the Academy of Digital Technology of Cambodia.
The Cambodia Information and Communication Technology Awards 2021 is the seventh year of the awards since 2015 by the former National Institute of Posts, Telecommunications and Information Technology (NIPTICT).
This year, about 200 candidates competed in six categories, including: (1) Best Digital Government Service Award of the Year, (2) Best New Digital Business Award of the Year, and (3) Digital Innovation Award. Best of the Year (4) Best Social Innovation Technology of the Year Award (5) Best Digital Content of the Year Award (6) Best Digital Research and Development Award of the Year
Only 25 candidates were shortlisted for the finals, which were held on October 26, 2021 at the Innovation Center.
Dr. Seng Sopheap, President of the Academy of Digital Technology of Cambodia, emphasized, “This year's Cambodian ICT Award reflects the ability and ability of new digital technology and business companies to turn the challenges of the 199 Kovid spread. "An opportunity to innovate products and business models to prepare for the recovery of business operations along the New Normal."
The judges of the 2021 ICT Awards have decided on the final nominees who have shown the best innovation in each category.
Mr. Chea Vandeth said, "The ICT Award of Cambodia is a model of success for our innovative IT entrepreneurs and new digital businesses, aiming to inspire innovation and innovation to contribute to the development of the digital economy and society for our country." "
