Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the results of the Indonesian Foreign Minister's official visit to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. Reth Noel P. The Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Indonesia, Marsudi, led a high-level delegation to pay an official visit to the Kingdom of Cambodia from November 30 to December 1, 2021 to promote and deepen bilateral relations; Cooperation between the two countries. The visit was made at the invitation of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia.
Mrs. Reth Noel P. Marsudi praised the effective management of the Kovid-19 epidemic and the successful vaccination program for the people of Cambodia as Cambodia gradually reopened its socio-economic activities. Ms. Reth Noel P. Marsudi also praised Cambodia's rapid development in the areas of economy and infrastructure.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Mrs. Reth Noel LP Marsudi also recently exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern in contributing to regional and global peace, stability and prosperity.
Regarding defense cooperation, Mr. Prak Sokhon highly commended Indonesia for providing support to military capacity building as well as training for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Prime Minister Hun Sen's bodyguards.
In trade and investment cooperation, the two foreign ministers agreed to push the two sides to double efforts to work closely together to increase trade volume. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon further encouraged Indonesian companies to invest in Cambodia in accordance with the favorable conditions for investors under the new investment law.
The two Foreign Ministers agreed to strengthen cooperation between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs and expected the 5th Joint Commission Meeting on Cambodia-Indonesia Bilateral Cooperation to be held soon in Cambodia.
