Cambodia-Australia launches new water purification technology in Battambang
(Battambang): Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation (MISTI) and Australian Ambassador to Cambodia Pablo Kang jointly inaugurated a new water purification technology installed at a water treatment plant. Clean in Battambang and disseminate the results of the research "Provincial investment plan for clean water supply in Cambodia."
Pablo Kang said he was proud to see an Australian company bring safe and environmentally friendly water technology to Cambodia. He hopes that the PIP study will also provide a useful road map and policy tool for the Cambodian government to achieve its goal of providing clean water to all Cambodians by 2030.
Please be informed that Ambassador Kang last September visited a factory in Battambang province and decided to introduce Australian water purification technology to supply clean water to the people of Cambodia. The water treatment system uses UF technology and a reservoir to distribute 120,000 liters of clean and safe water per day to about 5,000 people in 12 villages in Battambang province's Prek Chik commune.
