(Phnom Penh): In the implementation of measures across Cambodia on December 1, 2021, yesterday, there were no perpetrators of health measures and administrative measures. However, yesterday, the police educated and disseminated the law in 54 locations and educated 232 land traffic targets (174 vehicles).
The following is the announcement: Mr. Sok Lou warned the officials at the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Battambang province to continue to strengthen humanitarian work to help people
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province and Chairman of the Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross, urged the leaders and officials of the Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross to continue to strengthen humanitarian work to continue to help the people.
Mr. Sok Lou's warning was made during a meeting with the leaders of the branch committee and executive officers of the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Battambang at the branch office of the Cambodian Red Cross in Battambang on the afternoon of December 1, 2021.
Mr. Sok Lou discussed the division of roles and responsibilities of the Branch Committee to assist in strengthening the work system and roles and responsibilities of the Branch Executives and fundraising by philanthropists, adhering to the seven fundamental principles of the International Red Cross and Red Crescent Movement. Perform humanitarian duties.
He also instructed the branch management and executive officers to continue to maintain unity within the branch committee, direct the branch executive team to perform their duties and responsibilities in accordance with the strategy of the Cambodian Red Cross and to consult with the branch committee honorary committee.
In addition, we must work together to solve the challenges faced by women with high responsibility in humanitarian causes, mobilize forces to contribute to alleviate the suffering of victims and vulnerable people in Battambang province, especially to strengthen and promote the activities of the branch network. The Konrad Adenauer Foundation in Cambodia shares knowledge on international relations and teacher development at the National University of Battambang.
Teaching involves the preparation of detailed lesson plans, the preparation of lesson materials, the selection of teaching methods, and the evaluation of students' studies to adequately prepare them for international communication skills training.
This workshop has 4 main objectives as follows:
1. Provide education officers with international relations skills of the National University of Battambang with the basic philosophy of both theory and practice of teaching and learning in higher education.
2: Help the International Relations Education Officer of the National University of Battambang to prepare detailed lesson plans, subjects using pedagogical methods and educational evaluation work.
3: Share experiences on teaching practice and good learning from the Department of International Studies of the Royal University of Phnom Penh with education officials in the International Relations Program of the National University of Battambang.
4: Encourage education officials in the first generation international relations program to get the quality of teaching.
It should be noted that the organization of a workshop to share knowledge on international relations and develop the capacity of teachers based on the spirit of the Memorandum of Understanding between the National University of Battambang and the Royal University of Phnom Penh on February 22, 2021.
In the academic year 2021-2022, the Institute of Foreign Languages of the National University of Battambang will provide undergraduate training in International Relations for students taught by professors and well-known national and international speakers who have experience in teaching international relations, diplomacy, economics, law. Original.
In addition, the new education program will include many other important activities, such as study visits to ministries, public and private institutions, as well as the implementation of various national and international meetings.
