The Prime Minister of Cambodia wants to lift the ban on travelers from 10 countries in Africa, but must strengthen test measures (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has instructed the relevant ministries and institutions to discuss Concluding the decision to ban travelers from 10 African countries, Samdech recommended that in order to prevent the spread of the 10 new Kovid virus "Omikrong", test measures must be strengthened.
On the occasion of the official inauguration of all 37 roads in Sihanoukville on December 2, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to reconsider the ban on the above 10 countries entering Cambodia.
The Prime Minister stated that currently the 10 countries do not have direct flights to Cambodia, but in the event of a transit passenger arriving in Cambodia, officials stationed at the international airport must strengthen the PCR test measures. Necessary, not a quick test.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Those who need to travel from those countries should increase the test, even if he (the passenger) has a vaccine, but we ask for his forgiveness so that we can test. PCR, rather than us parasites.
The head of the Royal Government also stated that the change in attitude through the lifting of the ban and the strengthening of health measures is to avoid discriminatory behavior against those African countries, while Cambodia has also announced the reopening of international tourist destinations.
Once again, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called for urgent discussions between the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Secretary of State for Civil Aviation, the Ministry of Tourism and other stakeholders, if agreed, and the Royal Government will announce the end of the old ban. Return immediately.
