The announcement of the closure of the Ream port came after Cambodia had previously allowed the US military attaché to visit the Ream naval base, but after the visit, the United States accused Cambodia of not allowing its military to enter. Go everywhere in that Ream naval base.
Although not mentioned by name, Samdech Techo Prime Minister wants to refer to the United States, which is constantly making up stories about attacking Cambodia, the port of Ream as a place for Chinese military bases. Due to a series of unsubstantiated US allegations against Cambodia, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided not to care about the allegations.
The issuance of the statement drew strong reactions from the Cambodian Ministry of Defense, which saw it as an attempt to create new problems and distort the facts, leading to further tarnish of military relations between the two countries. The Department of Defense considers that the creation of new US scenarios has brought negativity and undermined Cambodia's sovereignty and military secrecy.
In this case, according to the statement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the visit is not to inspect or check. Samdech also claimed that the US action was a violation of Cambodian sovereignty and a violation of international law.
In the past, some US media outlets have repeatedly attacked Cambodia for allowing China to set up military bases in the Ream region, while Cambodia has repeatedly stated that it does not violate the country's supreme constitution. And there are no foreign military bases in Cambodia like the propaganda.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh stated that Cambodia only received assistance from China, a steel friend, to help build a larger and more modern Ream port, and this assistance was not on the same condition as other powers. Samdech Picheay Sena has made it clear that after the construction, Cambodia will use this modern port without handing it over to China as alleged by the United States.
Please be informed that the US Treasury Department and US State Department on November 10, 2021 also unilaterally imposed sanctions on General Chao Phirun, Director General of the General Department of Technical Equipment and Admiral Tea Vinh, Commander of the Armed Forces. The navy has been accused of corruption in the development of the Ream navy and the implementation of Global Magnitsky law.
This is not the first time the United States has unilaterally imposed sanctions on senior Cambodian military officials. In the past, the United States has also made a series of allegations regarding the development of the Ream navy and the construction of an airport in Darasakor, Koh Kong province. The United States has also been involved in the demolition of a small building it helped build in Ream.
