Samdech Techo Hun Sen Celebrates the 43rd Anniversary of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia December 2, 1978-December 2, 2021
Samdech Techo stated that the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia was established on December 2, 1978 and issued its 11b statement in the Snuol Liberation Area, Snuol District, Kratie Province.
The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation was formed by the great unity of the people, both inside and outside the country, including Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Samdech Akka Moha Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and patriotic heroes. Many others organized the forces to overthrow the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and won this regime on January 7, 1979.
In response to the call of the Front, people everywhere have stood together as a force of national unity, with the overwhelming support of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army and the support of close friends around the world to overthrow the Democratic Kampuchea regime. Until the glorious victory on January 7, 1979.
The Great Victory of January 7, 1979 ended the darkest period in Cambodian history, ushered in a new era, and the Cambodian people regained their rights, freedoms and opportunities to rebuild their homeland. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that all people clearly understand that without the birthday of the Front December 2 and the victory of January 7, there would be nothing like today "This is the truth of history."
Congratulations on the new achievements of Sihanoukville under the shadow of peace! This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated a road and wastewater treatment system worth about 300 million USD
(Preah Sihanouk): The result of peace that is spreading throughout Cambodia has brought more new achievements in Sihanoukville: 37 roads and 3 wastewater treatment plants at the expense of National for construction totaling about 300 million US dollars.
The road and wastewater treatment plant, which started construction in November 2019, have been completed and will be inaugurated on December 2, 2021 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Sihanoukville is the core of the 440-kilometer coastal area of Cambodia, covering four provinces, including Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampot and Kep, under the common name "Cambodian Coast", which is included as a club member. The most beautiful beach in the world on May 25, 2011 in Senegal at the 7th General Assembly of the World's Most Beautiful Beach Club.
Sihanoukville is also one of Cambodia's potential economic and tourism poles. In recent years, Sihanoukville has developed rapidly in the field of construction and investment. However, the road and sewer infrastructure was severely damaged.
In order to make Sihanoukville a truly quality city that attracts investment and develops to compete with other cities in the region, the Royal Government of Cambodia has assigned the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia to study and prepare a project. Build road and sewerage infrastructure because this city has special potential for national growth.
In order for this project to emerge as soon as possible, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Chairman of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia, has set out a plan to build these 34 roads in a timely manner. 8 months to be completed starting from November 16, 2019, which is the opening day under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Eight companies and entities, both public and private, that have experience and good work in implementing cooperation projects and are not blacklisted by the Ministry of Economy and Finance and development partners have participated in the construction of this project.
The 34 roads in this development project have been studied to classify the road hierarchy into three categories in accordance with urbanization, urban suburbs, residential areas, commercial areas and tourist areas with construction specifications.
In addition to the 34 roads in the project, the authorities also built a number of connecting roads, including: Techo Street, more than 1 km long, connecting from Street 502 to Street 2 Thnou, and on the road connected to Techo Square, Street Poy Ochheuteal is 350 meters long and Otres Street is more than 300 meters long.
On the sidewalk, there are lanes for pedestrians, the disabled and cyclists. To ensure road safety, there are more than 500 security cameras and smart lights. Control the desired light level from Phnom Penh for street lighting in Sihanoukville.
In developing these 34 roads, the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia has also taken into account the cultural connection as a national identity by building a large copper statue in three roundabouts. The three statues at the site include:
First, the statue of Preah Thong Neang Neak is located at the intersection of Chumteav Mao Blvd. and Ream Beach Boulevard, 21 meters high from the foot to the top of the crown. This statue represents the first Khmer monarch and the birth of the water, the birth of the land, the birth of the Khmer culture and civilization, facing the sea as an attitude of going to the royal tomb of the sea dragon.
Second, the statue of Vishnu and Princess Uma Phakavati, also known as Uma Mahasvara, is located at the intersection of Ream Blvd. and Ream Beach Boulevard, 9 meters high, in the style of Koh Ker. This statue represents the harmony of the family, living in peace and happiness.
Third: The three-faced Siha Reach statue is 9 meters high from the base of Siha Reach to the top of the crown, located along National Road 4. This statue is copied in the Bayon style and represents Sihanoukville, especially as a tribute to His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, who sacrificed his body, wisdom and leadership to create and develop Sihanoukville first. Most.
In addition to the three statues above, the project also planted nine types of ornamental trees on the streets, including paper flowers.
Building a road by using palm leaves, packing palm sugar, and doing it all over the city in Sihanoukville, this is a great concept born from the ideas and works of pure Khmer children, because both project managers, engineers, architects, study projects, companies, project implementation units, you Supervise the construction techniques are all Khmer in the Techo Sen era, full of peace, stability and development, in short, "Khmer think, Khmer draw, Khmer can do".
(Sihanoukville): Minister of the Environment Say Sam Al said that members of PEMSEA expected that the 2021 East Asia Summit wishes for a better, stronger and smarter regional initiative. Strategically with key principles and goals of the world's oceans.
At the same time, Mr. Say Sam Al also highlighted the many achievements that come from our cooperation under the organizational mechanism of the East Asia Maritime Environmental Management Partnership. These achievements are laying a solid foundation for our agenda of ensuring maritime protection, sustainable livelihoods, sustainable blue economy, which is an important driver to ensure the growth we need to build on. These achievements.
The Minister of Environment said: "It is expected that the General Assembly will wish for better, stronger and smarter regional initiatives that are strategically aligned with the main principles and goals of the Oceans of the world. "We anticipate further coordinated efforts to achieve the SDGs, including significant improvements in effective coastal and marine management."
Regarding this case, Mr. Say Sam Al emphasized: "The second point I want to present on this topic is a good reflection of the development priorities of Cambodia, as well as Sihanoukville, one of the coastal provinces. 4 things of Cambodia.
The Minister stated that the coast of Cambodia is 440 km long and our seas and oceans sector includes: fisheries, ports and transportation and coastal tourism. According to the country's GDP growth of 16%, coastal tourism accounted for 85%. In addition, our trade in goods is highly dependent on sea freight. This represents an ocean-based economy with plenty of room for expansion and improvement.
PEMSEA has 11 member countries, including Cambodia, Singapore, Laos, the Philippines, Indonesia, Vietnam, Timor-Leste, China, South Korea, North Korea, Japan and many other partner organizations.
The East Asia Sea Summit is a source of pride for Cambodia, which has hosted this important conference, which aims to review past approved work plans and ongoing action plans, including consideration. From the funds to be implemented to protect and conserve the seas in East Asia.
