150 People Living with HIV Receive Humanitarian Donations from Cambodian Red Cross Siem Reap Branch
(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Red Cross branch in Siem Reap province on December 1, 2021 provided humanitarian donations to 150 people living with HIV from 3 districts: Sot Nikum, Chi Kreng and Svay Leu districts.
The event was held at Penh Chet Restaurant, Sot Nikum District, in the presence of Mrs. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, Vice Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, on behalf of Mr. Tea Seiha, Provincial Governor and Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee.
Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha sent a health education message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all Cambodians with the following content:
1: Educate and disseminate information on HIV / AIDS 19 to the community and support support for people living with HIV / AIDS in the topic "Live normally, live in a new way."
2: Encourage people who have committed or suspected that they are at risk of HIV infection, please hurry to seek counseling and HIV testing services voluntarily and confidentially in public services, civil society services. Private, etc. To be aware of the HIV status that can be used to decide to receive timely care and treatment.
3: All pregnant women, please hurry to seek care and pregnancy tests properly and regularly according to the instructions of medical staff to prevent the transmission of HIV from mother to baby.
4. Absolutely stop all forms of discrimination or stigmatization of people living with HIV and AIDS because it is against the law on the prevention and control of the spread of HIV and AIDS in Cambodia and is inhumane.
5: People who have a job or high risk of HIV infection, please use a condom 100% every time you have sex.
6: Join in a strong solidarity to prevent the spread of HIV and prevent the spread of Kovid 19, especially in the community.
