Mrs. Reth Noel P. Marsudi arrived in Phnom Penh at 5:40 pm on November 30, 2021 yesterday for a two-day official visit to Cambodia, from November 30 to December 1. The Indonesian Foreign Minister's visit comes at the invitation of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon.
During her visit, she paid a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and held bilateral meetings with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia considers that the official visit of Ms. Reth Noel LP. Marsudi to Cambodia will continue to strengthen and deepen the long-term relations and close cooperation between Cambodia and Indonesia in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks for the mutual benefit of both nations and The world.
Cambodia and Indonesia formally established their relationship on February 13, 1959. It was disconnected in 1975 and reconnected in 1992. After the reconnection, Cambodia and Indonesia also strengthened their relations and cooperation. The leaders of the two countries often exchange visits with each other.
