Samdech Techo Hun Sen Tells Sihanoukville Residents Who Lack Fresh Water for Watering or Raising Fish to Take to Free Wastewater Treatment Plant
(Preah Sihanouk): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of December 1, 2021, told the people of Preah Sihanouk province who lack fresh water for fish farming or irrigation can go to get filtered water. At 3 wastewater treatment sites in Sihanoukville, free of charge.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was made on the occasion of inspecting two wastewater treatment systems that have been built in Sihanoukville to be inaugurated on December 2, 2021 tomorrow.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "If in another developed country, they can use this water as drinking water, but we do not call for our people to accept this water to drink, but in case our people lack water. Sow to raise fish, please come and get it from the water filter because all three locations have more than 30,000 cubic meters of water per day. So in case people need water to irrigate crops or raise fish, please come and get water there for free. ”
Samdech confirmed that the wastewater treatment system in Sihanoukville is also the latest technology from Israel, which kills germs with a laser system before dropping it into the sea.
