47 Suspects Sent to Court by Siem Reap Provincial Authorities in Case of Invasion of Flooded Forest Land
(Siem Reap): On November 30, 2021, Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, led a joint force to inspect the flooded forest and the place where the criminals cut down the flooded forest for personal gain in Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
Mr. Tea Seiha said that in Siem Reap province, there are 6 cities / districts located next to Tonle Sap Lake: Kralanh, Puok, Siem Reap, Prasat Bakong, Sot Nikum and Chi Kreng districts with an area of more than 126 thousand hectares.
The provincial governor added that in Siem Reap city, there are flooded forests that criminals have cut down for 100 hectares for personal gain, and 47 suspects have been sent to court by the authorities to build a case. In other districts, the team is actually inspecting.
The provincial governor believes that flooded forests are very important for spawning fish habitats and biodiversity in the Tonle Sap Lake. Years.
Mr. Tea Seiha also thanked Samdech Techo for giving the authorities the opportunity to end the deforestation in Siem Reap because the flooded forest is not only beneficial for aquatic biodiversity but also for visitors. Also, after visiting the temples and natural resorts in the province, tourists continue to visit the Tonle Sap Lake to see floating houses, flooded forests and birds.
