The Second Special Meeting of the General Assembly of the World Health Organization is the second special emergency meeting attended by the Kingdom of Cambodia, one of the 194 member countries. The meeting aims to discuss the benefits of establishing the World Health Organization Convention as well as agreements and develop strategies for international use to strengthen the preparedness and emergency response to public health emergencies.
