(Battambang): The Faculty of Arts, Humanities and Education of the National University of Battambang, in collaboration with the University of Ionina, Greece, has organized an Information Day (INFODAY) program available online to train teachers in life skills and technology or teaching skills. 21st Century
This information day was held on the afternoon of November 29, 2021 in order to disseminate the progress of the project and share the potential and experience related to the curriculum and teaching pedagogy in the 21st century. The program was attended by 175 leaders, professors, researchers and students from partner universities.
This 21st Century Teaching Skills Project has six main objectives, including:
* Improve the quality of higher education and lifelong learning * Improve relevant education for the job market * Improve the capacity and skills level in higher education institutions * Improve the capacity for innovation and internationalization in higher education institutions * Promote cooperation with European University to develop curricula in higher education * Promoting interpersonal relationships and intercultural awareness
