On that occasion, Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, brought the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message to visit and express his deep gratitude to the company that brought these hand gel to the Cambodian Red Cross.
In response, Mr. Mak Ing Thou, General Director of HANYA HER CHONG (Cambodia) Trading Co., Ltd., thanked Mr. Bun Rany Hun Sen for allowing the company to contribute to the humanitarian work with the Cambodian Red Cross. By offering hand gel.
At the same time, the General Director of this company also expressed his appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a wise leader with a clear vision and strategic plan to better control the spread of Kovid-19 disease. .
(Phnom Penh): The Director General of Customs and the Government of Cambodia held the 8th meeting of the Customs-Private Sector Partnership Mechanism to review and resolve requests and issues of the private sector related to the implementation of customs procedures to ensure Implementing trade facilitation policies and promoting law enforcement compliance after the private sector faced a number of challenges surrounding customs procedures for exporting and importing goods.
The Customs-Private Partnership Mechanism Meeting was held in a semi-formal, face-to-face and video-on-Zoom mode. Director of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
The private sector welcomes and accepts the solutions proposed by the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, with both sides committed to implementing their respective solutions. The Co-Chairs also agreed to encourage each expert working group to continue to review, raise and discuss issues that may arise in the future in a timely and effective manner.
Mr. Kun Nhim said that the Customs-Private Partnership Mechanism is a platform for the private sector to find solutions to problems and suggestions related to customs procedures in order to further improve trade facilitation and compliance with special laws in the context of Recovering international trade activity after the Kovid-19 crisis.
Duke Kith Meng stated that the Customs-Private Partnership Mechanism is a forum for dialogue in partnership to consult and find solutions to all issues based on win-win principles and mutual understanding.
Governor of Kandal Province: Khmer culture is becoming more famous on the international stage and flourishing under the strong leadership and protection of Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, said that Cambodian culture, both tangible and intangible, has been incorporated into the heritage so much that Cambodia has become more and more famous on the international stage and these are growing. From the strong leadership and protection of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He said this on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the third anniversary of the inclusion of Wat Svay Andet in the UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on the afternoon of November 29, 2021 at Wat Svay. Floating in Lvea Em district, Kandal province.
The event was also attended by Mr. Sion Sophearith, Director General of the General Department of Cultural Technology, Representative of Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, monks, departments around the province, Lvea Em district authorities and many people.
"We must work together to preserve and preserve our cultural arts and expand them to our wider community, and to be the first to preserve and spread our culture on the international stage," he said. This is Samdech Techo, our Prime Minister. ”
The Governor of Kandal Province called on the monks and all the people to work together to preserve and develop the Puppet Theater of Wat Svay Andet in order to maintain the national identity and prestige and to remember that "the protection of cultural heritage The nation is the duty of every Cambodian child. ”
Please note that Cambodia has UNESCO World Heritage List of Intangible and Intangible Cultural Heritage, including: Angkor Wat, Royal Ballet, Big Skin Shadow Theater, Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum, Reamker Storytelling Audio Grud, Preah Vihear temple, tug of war, Chapey Dang Veng, Sambor Prei Kuk temple and Wat Svay Andet.
