Krakor District Police Detain a Young Woman in a Motorcycle Theft Case at a Ghost House in Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Pursat): A young woman was arrested by Krakor district police in connection with a case of theft (motorcycle theft) from near a ghost house in Phsar commune, Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province (border of Rolea Bier district) at 10:20 a.m. November 29, 2021.
Authorities then arrested a female suspect, Kuon Ratana, at a rented house with the Angkor Reach logo of the owner, Pen Khip, 52, in Toeng village, Anlong Thnout commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, at 12 o'clock. And 43 minutes on November 29, 2021.
Lt. Col. Suy Mao also confirmed that the suspect who was detained by the police in connection with the above case was named Kuon Ratana, a 20-year-old female resident of O'Romchek Village, Chak Commune, Boribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province. The deputy inspector said that after questioning the suspect, he admitted that he had stolen a motorcycle on National Road 5 near the haunted house.
The suspects and exhibits have now been handed over to the Judicial Police Division of the Rolea Bier District Police Inspectorate on the orders of HE Koy Kanya, Prosecutor of the Pursat Provincial Prosecutor's Office, to continue the proceedings.
