(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) on Tuesday morning, November 30, 2021, held a meeting with stakeholders via online video to disseminate the provisional results of the census and Voter Registration Submission of provisional results of voter list review and voter registration to the NEC Complaints related to voter registration and initial voter list preparation.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Hal Sarath, Member of the NEC. During the meeting, Mr. Hel Sarath stated that November 30 is the last day for voter registration and voter registration in communes across the country.
After completing the voter registration work in the communes / sangkats, the NEC shall continue to perform its duties, including:
* Summarize the results of voter registration nationwide * Resolve relevant complaints (if any) * Review and decide by the NEC on the results and data of registrants to prepare the first voter list and post the first voter list .
Mr. Hal Sarath said that the examination of voter list and voter registration in communes across the country within 49 days obtained the following results:
He added that as of November 29, 2021, Commune / Sangkat Councils and the NEC had not received any complaints regarding the voter list and voter registration process.
Stakeholders attending the meeting were interested in evaluating this year's voter registration and voter registration process as a smooth one, and commended the NEC for its voter registration techniques. Up.
At the same time, there are also some questions that were answered by the NEC as follows:
* This year's voter registration figures are higher than in 2020, when there were just over 200,000 registered voters. In 2021, there will be more than 440,000 registered voters. Taken as a whole, the voter registration team worked directly with more than 980,000 people, including voter registrants, data corrers, new communes, and those who would be removed from the list. Vote.
* Although the 2021 voter list and voter registration process faces challenges with Kovid-19, floods and dilapidated voter registration materials, the NEC has taken measures to prevent Kovid-19, which the number of registered officials Only about 0.1% of the cases were reported and the NEC resolved not to obstruct the work by replacing the voter registration officials and replacing the damaged materials in a timely manner.
Based on this year's experience, for the coming 2022, there will be new challenges, and the NEC will have to prepare further measures because it is the year of Commune / Sangkat Council elections.
* In the year of elections, the NEC often issues appeals through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation to allow foreign workers as well as ordinary people on the official voter list to return to the country to vote. Voting takes place in communes in Cambodia.
Stakeholders who attended the online video meeting included representatives of the Constitutional Council, the Senate, the National Assembly, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Information, the National Police Commission, officials of the Japanese Embassy, representatives of JICA, representatives of political parties, NGOs, media units and NEC officials. There are about 64 people.
