The following are the activities of the Phnom Penh Military Police and the police force involved in providing security for the Prime Minister of Laos: Sihanoukville is the first province to have two international standard wastewater treatment plants established by Khmer children.
(Sihanoukville): In order to treat wastewater and wastewater into clean water in accordance with environmental standards before discharging into the sea, Sihanoukville provincial authorities have already built two wastewater treatment plants that are currently in use. Actively for water purification in Sihanoukville.
For Cambodia at present, only Sihanoukville has built and operated a state-of-the-art wastewater treatment plant from Israel, created by a group of Cambodian engineers.
In fact, the operation of the wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville is the second treatment plant with the capacity to treat 7,200 cubic meters of wastewater per day and is divided into 9 main stages located in the village. 3, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville.
The treatment plant is powered by the latest technology of Israel MABR, it is capable of removing ammonia, carbon dioxide, bacteria and toxins, and the treated water is not toxic to the environment and marine biodiversity, it has high quality standards and It is the work of only 6 Cambodian children.
He said that the wastewater after passing through the treatment system will be good quality water without pollution and marine biodiversity.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, currently for Cambodia, only Sihanoukville has built and operated a standard wastewater treatment plant using technology from the country. Israel will be built by Khmer children.
On the occasion of inspecting the second wastewater treatment plant with the capacity to clean 7,200 cubic meters of wastewater per day on the afternoon of November 29, 2021 yesterday. He said the wastewater treatment plant has the ability to remove most of the waste particles and kill germs and bacteria, which can make the water up to 60 percent safe before being released into the sea.
According to Preah Sihanouk Provincial Governor Kouch Chamroeun, two wastewater treatment plants were built with the assistance of the Asian Development Bank (ADB), with the first being capable of cleaning wastewater per day. 5,200 cubic meters and the second station has a capacity of 7,200 cubic meters per day.
Another wastewater treatment plant on Ochheuteal beach with a capacity of 20,000 cubic meters per day will also be built in the near future, he said.
According to the master plan of the sewage system development project in Sihanoukville, presented by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in the past, in 2021-2023, 69 km of sewers will be constructed and nearly 40 kilometers of secondary sewers. More than 92 kilometers of residential and commercial buildings will be connected, while between 2023-2030, the station will be able to expand its processing capacity to 60,000 cubic meters or 80,000 cubic meters per day.
The project to develop wastewater treatment plant and sewage and drainage system in Sihanoukville is planned to cost more than 170 million US dollars.
