A three-star military man and his daughter-in-law were killed in a fire that killed both of them in Kambol district.
(Phnom Penh): A three-star military general and his daughter-in-law were killed in a fire that killed two people, one at home and the other at the hospital. This incident happened at 12 midnight on November 30, 2021 in Borey Kimsand, Ta Ker village, Sangkat Kampol, Khan Kampol.
According to the report, the three-star military officer, Chea Sophal, 60, was the Deputy Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, while his daughter-in-law was not yet identified. The two victims stayed in the house above.
According to sources at the scene, before the incident, they saw flames coming out of the house mixed with thick smoke and heard the owner shouting for help. Immediately, the people living nearby brought fire hoses to help put out the fire, but it did not go out, so they reported to the police to get out of the car to spray water and rescue the two victims and take them to the hospital. Unfortunately, the victims died one after another.
The house, which was 5 meters by 16 meters in size, was completely destroyed by the fire, three motorbikes and did not spread to neighboring houses. The cause of the fire is being investigated by the police.
For this rescue operation, the police used 5 fire trucks, such as 3 fire trucks of Borey Sangkum Thmey, 1 fire truck of Unit 911 and 1 fire truck of Kambol District Hall. .
