Please be informed that the party for the Prime Minister of Laos took place after the end of the bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Phan Kham Viphavan, Prime Minister of Laos at the Peace Palace on the evening of November 29, 2021.
At the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced an additional $ 13 million in aid and an additional 500,000 doses of Sinovak vaccine to the Lao government and people to fight 19 Kovid. $ 3 million from the Royal Government and $ 10 million from private companies.
It should be noted that in this working meeting, Mr. Phorn Kham Viphavan, Prime Minister of Laos, congratulated Cambodia on its success in all areas, including hosting the Asia-Europe Summit and hosting the meeting. ASEAN Summit in 2022 Regarding the hosting of the ASEAN Summit, the Prime Minister of Laos promised to cooperate with Cambodia to help Cambodia succeed in hosting the ASEAN Summit.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, during the meeting, the Prime Minister of Laos also requested Samdech Techo to continue to strengthen and expand bilateral cooperation. In particular, the continuation of bilateral cooperation with each other to end the issue of agreement reached in the past. In particular, the negotiations will discuss how to finalize the cooperation agreement in a comprehensive partnership.
The Lao Prime Minister also urged the two countries' joint border commissions to continue to work on border issues as scheduled. Mr. Phorn Kham Viphavan also proposed to boost cooperation on bilateral trade and strengthen cooperation in the fields of education, culture and other areas of tourism. The Lao Prime Minister also proposed boosting investment in Laos.
For his part, Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia asked the Prime Minister of Laos to make sure that the two peoples can travel to each other to trade across the border. Samdech Techo expressed support for boosting bilateral trade by boosting investment between the two countries, supporting investors from both countries, as investment is the basis for strengthening and expanding political and economic cooperation. .
