(Phnom Penh): Voter registration is very important for people to have the right to participate in the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council Election and the 2023 National Assembly Election.
If not registered on the voter list prepared by the National Election Committee (NEC), Cambodians of both sexes will not be eligible to vote.
For the year 2021, the NEC will start reviewing the voter list and voter registration from October 12 to November 30, 2021, which lasts for 50 days. As of November 30, 2021, this is the last day of the voter registration and verification process.
The NEC has announced that the voter list and voter registration process will take place daily, including on Saturdays and Sundays. In the morning, work from 7:00 AM to 11:30 AM and in the afternoon from 2:00 AM to 5:30 AM at Commune / Sangkat Hall and some locations in Commune / Sangkat.
In order to register to vote, Cambodian citizens of both sexes must meet the following conditions:
+ A: Khmer people living in the commune who are at least 18 years old at the time of the Commune / Sangkat Council Election (June 5, 2022) were born before or until June 6, 2004. Those who are not yet on the voter list of the commune where they live can apply to register to vote.
+ B: In order to register to vote, Cambodian citizens must meet in person with the voter registration team by presenting their Cambodian identity card to the head of the voter registration team:
* If the address on the Khmer Nationality Identity Card is in the commune / sangkat where the people are living and apply for registration, the Voter Registration Team will prepare to register in accordance with the NEC procedures.
* If the address in the Khmer Nationality Identity Card is different from the Commune / Sangkat where the citizen is applying for registration, the citizen must bring a family book or residence book or a certificate of residence in the Commune / Sangkat requesting registration.
* Proof of residence must be made in the commune / sangkat according to the Prakas of the Ministry of Interior, which requires a Cambodian identity card and a temporary residence permit (A9) and a witness who is a citizen who has the right to vote in the commune / sangkat. Together.
* In case the citizen does not have a Cambodian identity card, the citizen must go to the commune chief or commune chief to request the identity document for voter registration, which must be brought with the birth certificate or proof of nationality, 3x4 photo 2 ballots and 2 witnesses who have the right to vote in the same commune / sangkat (witness must not be a member of Commune / Sangkat Council (CPC), Commune / Sangkat Chief, Deputy Commune / Sangkat Chief or Commune / Sangkat Clerk).
+ C: If the people do not meet the conditions as mentioned above, the leader of the voter registration team will decide to reject the application for registration by issuing a rejection form 1009, and the rejected people can complain to the Commune / Sangkat Council. Within 3 days after the date of receipt of the 1009 rejection form, the procedure shall be followed in accordance with the election law until the Constitutional Council.
Please note that the NEC regularly checks the voter list and voter registration every year to provide opportunities for citizens over the age of 18 to vote. For 2021, the NEC plans to register 1,635,990 new voters and remove 83,043 names from the voter list.
