(Preah Sihanouk): The Ministry of Environment and Administration of Preah Sihanouk Province held a press conference before the start of the 7th East Asia Sea Summit to inform the media about Cambodia's readiness to host the 2021 East Asia Summit. And show the achievements of the Royal Government for Sihanoukville.
The press conference held on November 29, 2021 was attended by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province at the administration of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the 7th East Asia Sea Conference, which Cambodia is hosting, will be held on December 1 and 2, 2021 under the theme "Creating a New Decade for Ocean, Human and Economic Well-Being".
The East Asia Sea Summit 2021, which includes meetings of the sub-national administrations of PEMSEA member provinces, the International Conference and the Ministerial Forum is the seventh General Assembly after its first in 2003. In Malaysia. The East Asia Sea Summit is held every three years with the participation of member countries of the East Asia Maritime Environment Management Partnership.
