Director General of Immigration: From the day of opening to receive tourists without being required to do so, more than 6,000 foreign visitors came to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Since the head of the Royal Government announced the reopening of the country to receive tourists without being required to do so (November 15, 2021), a total of more than 6,000 foreigners have entered Cambodia, including Tourists, investors and other travelers. This is according to General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior.
It should be informed that on November 15, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced the reopening of the country to restore the national economy after being affected by the Kovid-19 epidemic. Re-open to international tourists without the need for Chattalysak.
In a meeting with the Ministry of Tourism and the working group of the Royal Government and the private sector to restore and promote tourism in Cambodia during and after the Kovid-19 crisis on November 29, 2021, General Kiet Chantharith said that during Of the Kovid-19 epidemic, an average of only 300 people enter Cambodia each day.
After the Royal Government announced the opening of a country that has the conditions for a three-day, seven-day, 14-day period from November 1, 2021 to November 15, 2021, there were 6,071 people entering Cambodia. With an average of 400 people per day, an increase of about 100 people per day compared to the period of the outbreak of Kovid-19.
The Director General of the General Department of Immigration said, "From the 16th, in fact, the Royal Government announced the reopening of the country on the 15th, but I count from 16 to 21 November 2021, there are a number of guests. "6,111 people, an average of 560 people a day, but sometimes more than 600 people a day."
Please be informed that in 2020, Cambodia received 1.31 million international tourists, a decrease of 80.2%. In particular, in the first ten months of 2021, Cambodia received only about 200,000 international tourists, a decrease of 89% compared to the same period in 2020.
However, there is optimism that after the announcement by the head of the Royal Government to reopen the country, the number of international tourists will increase, while the Ministry of Tourism expects the number of international tourists to reach 7 million. In 2025.
