Cambodia announces new investment law to Chinese investors, as of October this year, Chinese investment in Cambodia amounted to more than 27 billion US dollars
(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia, in collaboration with the Office of Economy and Trade of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia and the Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, on November 29, 2021, organized a seminar to disseminate the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Chinese investors and businessmen in Cambodia and abroad with about 300 participants.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, spoke about the good relations between the two countries that have existed for a long time and were nurtured by His Majesty King Father Norodom Sihanouk. And the Chinese leadership at that time will be promoted by the Prime Minister and the Chinese leadership in succession until achieving the level of "comprehensive strategic partnership" in 2010.
This excellent diplomatic relationship is reflected in strong economic ties, with China becoming Cambodia's largest trading partner, source of investment and tourism.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea thanked the Chinese government and investors for their contribution to the socio-economic development of Cambodia, especially through the construction of physical infrastructure, which is the foundation of development.
In fact, according to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, during 1992-2020, the People's Republic of China provided a total of 4.6 billion US dollars in financing to Cambodia, while Chinese investment totaled more than 27 billion US dollars as of last month. October 2021.
He thanked the Chinese government and people for providing Kovid-19 vaccine to Cambodia, making Cambodia a country with a high rate of vaccination and a speedy economic recovery.
He added that in order to promote investment cooperation, the Council for the Development of Cambodia, the Council for the Development of Cambodia and the National Committee for Development and Reform of the People's Republic of China have signed a series of memorandums of understanding and recently signed Memorandum of Understanding on Improving Cooperation, Production Capacity and Investment on November 12, 2021.
In this regard, he is optimistic that through today's seminar, Chinese investors have a better and deeper understanding of the investment law of the Kingdom of Cambodia and decided to invest more in Cambodia. He invited overseas Chinese investors to study in Cambodia, while Cambodia has exempted the vaccination of travelers who have already received the basic dose.
Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the Council for the Development of Cambodia and relevant ministries and institutions in drafting the investment law.
He said that good relations between China and Cambodia have existed for a long time, especially through the outbreak of Kovid-19, the relationship between the two countries is even closer. Under the wise leadership of the leaders and the efforts of the people of the two countries, bilateral relations have reached an all-time high and Cambodia has become an important investment destination for China.
He hoped that with the introduction of the investment law, the continued implementation of the One Belt One Road initiative and the entry into force of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, Cambodia-China investment cooperation would achieve remarkable results. Definitely better.
