(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, will co-chair with the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of the Philippines, Mr. Tevolor Loxin Jr., to chair the 1st Cambodia-Philippines Joint Commission on Bilateral Cooperation. 3 (3rd JCBC) on December 2, 2021 via video system. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on November 29, 2021, obtained by Fresh News.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that the 3rd JCBC Meeting aims to further strengthen the existing good bilateral relations and explore ways to further expand the scope and enhance the effectiveness of bilateral cooperation in various fields for development. Socio-economics and prosperity of both peoples.
The meeting will also review the progress made in implementing the minutes of the second JCBC meeting signed in 2017 in Manila, Philippines. The meeting will also provide an opportunity for both sides to exchange views on cooperation in the regional and international framework.
At the end of the meeting, Mr. Prak Sokhon and Mr. Thev Dorollin Sinjer will sign the minutes of the third meeting of the Joint Commission on Cambodia-Philippines Bilateral Cooperation.
