The Minister of Labor asks the union leaders to consider the Ministry of Labor as a partner and a mechanism to provide legal services to solve problems for workers.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, requested the union leaders to consider the Ministry of Labor as a partner and a mechanism to provide legal services. Time to solve problems for workers.
This statement made by Mr. Ith Sam Heng made Mr. Ath Thorn, President of the Cambodian Labor Union and the Tourism Services Trade Union Federation, lead the working group to discuss some issues related to tourism at the Ministry of Labor this morning. November 2021. The purpose of this meeting is to discuss the work in partnership with the Ministry and to provide better protection of rights and benefits to workers.
Mr. Ath Thorn expressed his gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which has always provided cooperation and support to help solve some of the challenges of the union in the mission to protect the benefits, rights, freedoms, working conditions of workers to be more. Effective in tourism, textiles, garments, footwear and travel products and bags, as well as some other sectors.
He said that in the phase of challenges caused by Kovid-19, efforts have been made to put in place measures from the first round to the present, the 10th round, to help maintain the balance of trade, business, production to ensure the sustainability of jobs, income and living standards of the people and Affected workers.
He said that the Royal Government has been working hard to improve the lives of workers and help factories to be able to open business production to continue to provide sustainable employment for workers.
He added that tourism was the worst hit in the Kovid-19 phase, with some companies struggling to cope with the two-year-long epidemic crisis. Its. This is a globally difficult situation in the field of tourism, any country is affected.
The Prime Minister called on the unions to be understanding in the phase of the Kovid-19 epidemic, in which both employers and workers in the sector are struggling, despite the government's intervention to help employers suspend work. Most in this sector can not handle the guarantee of benefits to workers, as in the field of garments and footwear.
He hopes that when the tourism sector can recover, consideration of working conditions, especially on benefits, including the expansion of the scope to the minimum wage, will also be discussed in the National Wage Council mechanism. .
"Unions must consider the ministry as a partner as a mechanism to provide legal services. If there is a problem that can not be resolved, they can come and consult with the ministry at any time," he said.
The Minister instructed the General Department of Labor and the General Secretariat of the Strike and Strike Resolution Commission to continue working more closely with the unions to resolve the remaining issues as soon as possible and to review and prepare additional guidelines or legal documents to ensure implementation. Labor laws are more effective. Turkey plans to help Cambodia improve health
