Mr. Nhem Sary considered the field of employment and vocational training as a sector to be taken care of by the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. In addition, the sector has driven the development of the private sector and contributed to the growth of the national economy through a skilled workforce and the growth of factories, enterprises, handicrafts, restaurants, hotels and a large number of private companies. Also.
Mr. Nhem Sary also expressed his sincere admiration for the efforts of the Director of the Center for Civil Servants, Professors of Stung Treng Vocational Training Center, who have worked hard to train human resources for many years. Comes to contribute to the success and effectiveness of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy.
Mr. Bou Virun, Director of Stung Treng Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training, thanked the Director and Director of Techo Sen Polytechnic Institute of Siem Reap and Svay Rieng for signing the Memorandum of Understanding between the Institute and Stung Treng Provincial Vocational Training Center.
In addition, Mr. Bour Virun believes that through the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding, the teachers and teachers will get to use their abilities better, young people in Stung Treng will have the opportunity to continue their studies, internships and opportunities. Jobs in both provinces and in the future, the center will change and grow to provide more skills to young men and women in Stung Treng.
