Thai Minister of Transport tells adviser Samdech Techo Hun Sen that building a transportation system is a priority for boosting economic growth
(Bangkok, Thailand): The Minister of Transport of Thailand, Dr. Saktis Siam Chitchop, said that the construction of roads, infrastructure, roads and bridges is a priority of the Royal Government to promote better connectivity and economic development in the country.
The Thai Minister of Transport made the remarks during a recent meeting with Dr. Sok Sokretya, personal adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism in Bangkok, Thailand.
In this meeting, Dr. Sakti Siam Chitchop and Dr. Sok Sokretya discussed a lot about the importance of connecting infrastructure between Cambodia and Thailand. Both Dr. Sakti Siam Chitchop and Dr. Sok Sokretya said that connecting the transportation system is a political issue that ASEAN is paying close attention to.
Dr. Sok Sokretya also highlighted the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to build infrastructure, roads and bridges. Mr. Sokretya emphasized that roads are one of the four priority areas that Samdech Techo has set out since liberating the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Dr. Sok Sokretya emphasized that "Currently, the Royal Government of Cambodia is working hard to build national roads and bridges across rivers to connect urban areas to rural areas. "Currently, Cambodia has interconnected roads to travel across the country and is improving even more."
Dr. Sok Sokretya, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Personal Adviser, also thanked the Royal Government of Thailand for agreeing to temporarily open the Cambodia-Thailand International Border Crossing "Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ean" in the near future, despite the administrative buildings and roads. The connection on the Cambodian side is not yet complete.
During the meeting, Dr. Sok Sokretya highlighted the efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the process of building the country by maintaining peace and bringing rapid development to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo's advisers also highlighted Cambodia's success under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the fight against Kovid 19 and the rapid vaccination of Kovid 19 to the people. Districts not to hide crimes in their localities
"The district inspector must not hide crimes or incidents in his local area for fear of being blamed, but must report any crimes and co-operate in cracking down," he said.
