(Phnom Penh): Police forces from the Kambol District Inspectorate arrested a young man after a woman alleged that he raped her and even stole some of her phone and money.
Mr. Chhim Savuth, Deputy Inspector in charge of Criminal Planning of Kambol District Inspector, told Fresh News Agency on November 29, 2021 that the above incident happened on November 25, 2021 at around 12 o'clock at night. Kob Phluk Village, Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roret, Khan Kambol, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Chhim Savuth continued that the suspect was named Pheng Pheakdey, alias Nixin, male, 24 years old, occupation, worker, currently residing in Taing Ronam village, Preah Lang commune, Kampoul district, Phnom Penh. The victim, 22-year-old S.S.S.A.N, is a massage therapist and currently resides in Kork Khleang village, Kork Khleang commune, Sen Sok district, Phnom Penh.
However, the suspect did not take the victim home, took the victim to a quiet place in the field and raped her. After the rape, the suspect stole her phone and money. Come along.
Mr. Chhim Savuth said that after receiving a complaint from the victim, Mr. Hang Mony, the police inspector of Kambol district, ordered him to lead a specialized force and a police force to search and arrest the suspect.
The suspects have now been sent to court for legal action. Government Spokesperson Unit Holds Two-Day Workshop on "Office of Information Intelligence and Good Governance in the Information Sector" in Tbong Khmum Province
(Tbong Khmum): The Office of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government led by Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, this morning, November 29, 2021, organized a workshop on "Office of Information Intelligence and Good Governance in the Information Sector" in the province. Bee gemstone that lasts for 2 days.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Phay Siphan stated that information is a special substance in the participation in maintaining peace and political stability of the society. In this context, the information must be in the discipline and traffic from the official source to the public for understanding and participation in building the rule of law and accountability in accordance with the good governance policy of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy.
Mr. Phay Siphan added that the two-day workshop on "Information Intelligence and Good Governance in the Information Sector" aims to share the basic concepts, mechanisms and strategies of the state information sector. In order to build good governance in the field of information at the sub-national level to promote the effectiveness of disseminating information to the people for personal benefit at the local level.
The Head of the Royal Government Spokesperson expressed his sincere hope that the two-day workshop would be a success and a fruitful event to contribute to the noble mission of maintaining peace, stability and development. Develop the nation, which is the strong will of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, also thanked the Head of the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government for paying attention to the capacity building training of information officers and spokespersons of the sub-national administration during the period. In the past, sub-national administrations have been provided with significant resources in the field of employment, professional information officers and spokespersons of public institutions.
