Phorn Kham Viphavan is the new Prime Minister of Laos, who took office in March 2021, succeeding Lao President Thongloun Sisoulith. Prior to this, he served as Vice President of Laos from 2016 to 2021.
Cambodia and Laos are border villages with a border of more than 540 km, and both sides have agreed to set up 86% of the joint border posts, with 121 out of a total of 145 posts. . Cambodia and Laos were officially established on June 15, 1956.
Based on this good relationship, the leaders of the two countries have frequently exchanged visits between the two countries. In addition, the two countries always help each other in times of disaster.
In fact, in 2018, the Royal Government of Cambodia provided about $ 100,000 in humanitarian assistance, and the Cambodian Red Cross provided $ 50,000 to Laos to help victims of the Sepian-Senamai dam collapse.
During the outbreak of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia provided 2 million humanitarian aid and 11 other medical equipments to the Government of Laos to fight Kovid 19 on the 16th. November 2020 On September 29, 2021, Cambodia provided 200,000 doses of Sinovak vaccine.
In terms of trade and investment between the two countries, the report shows that in the first eight months of 2021, the trade volume was more than 104 million US dollars. As of October 2021, Cambodia has invested more than $ 138 million in Laos and Laos has invested about $ 3.6 million in Cambodia.
Please note that Laos is also a country that has signed agreements to supply electricity to many countries. In 2017, Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) and Laos signed a memorandum of understanding (MoU) to purchase 115 kV electricity and connect the power supply network to Preah Vihear and Stung Treng provinces.
In 2018, Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) and Laos signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on the purchase and sale of 230 and 500 kV high voltage power from Banhat Station of Laos to Stung Treng Station.
