(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mao Havanal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, confirmed that after the Royal Government of Cambodia waived the provocation for Cambodian tourists who have been fully vaccinated, the number of tourists entering Cambodia has increased. Gradually ascending.
He said that in December 2021, eight airlines, six of which had applied for re-flight and two had applied for additional flights, increasing the number of flights to 43 a week. From December onwards.
Minister Mao Havnal made the remarks at the second meeting of the Royal Government-Private Working Group to Promote Tourism in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis, chaired by Minister of Tourism Thong Khon on the morning of the 29th. This November via video. This was confirmed by Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for Civil Aviation, confirmed to Fresh News.
According to the spokesman, Minister Mao Havanal said in the meeting that after the announcement of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the reopening of the country from November 15, 2021 for travelers to Cambodia in accordance. Measures and conditions of demand have led to a gradual increase in the number of tourists entering Cambodia.
The State Secretariat of Civil Aviation also focuses on the next priority, the resumption of regular flights between Cambodia and China, whenever the Chinese government eases anti-Kovid-19 measures. In this case, the growth of air passengers and flights will not be attractive to the aviation and tourism markets if the air traffic between the two countries is still limited.
