The Senate will convene a meeting of the Standing Committee on December 1 to set the date and agenda of the 4th Extraordinary Session (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Senate will convene a meeting of the Standing Committee on December 1, 2021 Upcoming to determine the date and agenda of the Extraordinary Session of the 4th Legislature. This is according to the announcement of the General Secretariat of the Senate, which was received by Fresh New Network this morning, November 29, 2021.
The meeting of the Standing Committee of the Senate will be chaired by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, with the following agenda:
First, review and decide on the request of the Second Committee of the Senate to put the draft law on finance for management in 2022 on the agenda of the Senate as the fourth extraordinary term.
Second, to review and decide on the request of the Second Committee of the Senate to include the draft law on the payment of the general state budget for the administration of 2020 in the agenda of the Senate meeting for the fourth extraordinary term.
Third, to review and decide on the request of the Ninth Committee of the Senate to submit the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN Protocol on the Strengthening of Dispute Resolution Mechanisms into the agenda of the Senate for the fourth extraordinary session.
Fourth: Determining the agenda and date of the extraordinary Senate session of the fourth legislature.
