(Phnom Penh): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, held an emergency meeting on the evening of November 28, 2021 with Deputy Commanders and relevant provincial commanders around Tonle Lake. After the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to crack down on the crime of deforestation around the Tonle Sap Lake, especially in Kampong Chhnang province.
The meeting was held immediately via Video Conference with the participation of the Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie, the Commander of the National Gendarmerie in Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Battambang, Pursat, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Kandal and Kampong Cham provinces.
On November 28, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued a strict order to relevant ministries and institutions and provincial governors along the Tonle Sap Lake to immediately prevent and crack down on illegal logging and flooding. Take land along the Tonle Sap Lake, especially in Kampong Chhnang province.
For General Sao Sokha, Samdech Techo ordered the use of infantry, both naval and helicopter control immediately, fearing that the water level may be cultivated on the Tonle Sap Lake encroachment and let out first.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed General Sao Sokha that "General Sao Sokha must take immediate action to lead the force to solve this problem by using both infantry and navy and helicopters to immediately monitor Operation to preserve this flooded forest area ... "
At the same time, Samdech asked Mr. Om Yentieng, Chief of the Anti-Corruption Unit to lead the force to search for any officials involved in the encroachment on the Tonle Sap Lake to prepare a case to be sent to court for trial. .
