Residents arrest a group of people in Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, claiming to be law enforcement forces to crack down on drugs
(Kampong Speu): Several villagers surrounded a group of people claiming to be police forces and confiscated a firearm as they cracked down on drugs in front of Ang Ta Lek pagoda in Sambo commune, Samrong Tong district. Kampong Speu province, night of November 26, 2021.
According to a report from Fresh News, at the time of the incident, a group of plainclothes men claimed to be police and came down to crack down on drug cases. When the villagers went out for questioning, the group said they had guns in their hands and that they were from the Ministry of Interior's drug crackdown unit.
Seeing the uncomfortable situation, they called the villagers to stop the car and prevent the local force from intervening and stopped them and brought them to the Samrong Tong District Police Inspectorate.
In this case, Major General Sam Samoun, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu, said that Colonel Tri Mon Cheat is a police officer, but he is in the sports unit, not in the drug department, as the people say. Today, the Special Forces will summon the two sides to meet and continue questioning.
Colonel Sam Sak, director of the Bureau of Serious Crimes, also said that they were police officers but not in the Drug Enforcement Unit, and that they had come to clarify the matter at 2 pm today. Girls in Chhlong district, Kratie province
(Kratie): Police in Chhlong district, Kratie province, arrested a man in connection with the rape of an 8-year-old girl. The arrest took place on November 26, 2021 at Krouch village, Damrey Phong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province.
The local police confirmed that on November 26, 2021, at about 8:30 AM, the police received a complaint from the victim's mother that there were 5 cases of rape between October and November 2021. Located in the commune where the incident occurred.
The victim was an 8-year-old Cambodian girl named BN, residing in Krouch village, Damrey Phong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province. The suspect, Soeun Krouch, a 49-year-old Cambodian man, lived in the commune with the victim girl.
Police said that according to the complaint from the victim's mother, there was a case of rape in Krouch village, Damrey Phong commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province. Raped her five times and threatened not to tell anyone if told and killed, the last rape on November 19, 2021, then on November 26, 2021 Just came to complain to the authorities.
After receiving the complaint, the police arrested the suspect and took him to the Chhlong District Police Inspectorate for questioning. After questioning, the suspect confessed that he had raped the girl five times.
The suspect is currently being held in custody at the Chhlong District Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to the provincial office to continue legal proceedings.
