(Kampong Chhnang): On the morning of November 27, 2021, Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Mission, invited 158 teachers and trainees to participate in a 15-day training course on "Division of Inheritance. In Islam ”at Anneak Mae School in Tuol Village, Chhouk Sor Commune, Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that knowledge of how to divide the inheritance is very important because in Islam, after the death of a family member, it is absolutely necessary to distribute the inheritance to the surviving relatives according to the rules. Religious law avoids scratching problems in the future.
He urged all participants after gaining knowledge from this training course to continue teaching to others. This is a good thing and also a merit for those who have given knowledge to others, as stated in Islam that after a person dies, everything is cut off except for three things that will Help them in the hereafter, which is to provide good knowledge to others.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan emphasized to the whole ceremony, "We must all express our gratitude to the Prime Minister for incorporating 1,500 Khmer-Islamic teachers into the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports." The salary that all Khmer Muslim teachers receive is up to nearly 6 million dollars per year.
He added that this did not happen spontaneously, because Samdech Techo saw the difficulties of the Khmer Muslim community, which always raises money to support teachers, and because Khmer Islam has actively supported the Royal Government. Decided to give this gift as well as other offerings and facilitation to the Khmer Muslim community. Therefore, we must thank and reciprocate the gratitude by continuing to support the Royal Government forever.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan also donated 2 million Riels to participate in this training.
