Hun Many was the first young politician to have an "electronic office" or "online office" to facilitate direct public communication.
Mr. Som Ratana, Member of the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and Chairman of the Public Relations and Public Relations Working Group, said that through the introduction of this electronic office or online office to provide more convenience to the public to find information and connect. Contact Mr. Hun Many on all frameworks quickly via electronic system.
According to Som Ratana, Hun Many is a young politician and the first in Cambodia to have an electronic office or online office. The creation of this online office is like keeping up with the latest developments in the world, especially in the use of technology.
Mr. Som Ratana further emphasized that Mr. Hun Many's electronic office has four main goals and functions, including:
* First: a source of official information about Mr. Hun Many in the form of mass, including articles, news, video clips or promotional materials that the public can access and download
* Second: Provide a platform to increase the efficiency of public relations work by introducing the concept, message or message of Mr. Hun Many to the public, both inside and outside the country, in addition to the existing media through various social media.
* Third: It is a mechanism to show the mission and performance of Mr. Hun Many in all frameworks, including: political work, work in the legislature, basic work, social work and youth work, etc.
* Fourth: Reflect the new generation of leaders needed to adapt to social evolution, especially in the context of the Industrial Revolution. Fourth, by taking advantage of the use of technology to expand the scope and effectiveness of communication with the public.
Mr. Som Ratana added that the establishment of the e-office also reflects and responds to the new trends of the law on access to information, and now the website hunmany.kh is constantly updated to meet the needs of users. . He added that all citizens can meet directly with Hun Many when there is a real need.
On the other hand, what is easier for journalists is to make an appointment for an interview without having to submit an official administrative letter to Mr. Hun Many's cabinet, just go through this website and follow the instructions stating your name and phone number. Institutional roles and objectives are achievable.
Please be informed that in addition to the multi-functionality as mentioned above, this e-office will allow the public to access Mr. Hun Many's information on all frameworks, including:
* First: Chairman of the Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism of the National Assembly * Second: President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia * Third: Secretary-General of the Mass Movement Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party * Fourth: Chairman of the Board Many Foundation * 5th: Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency * 6th: Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Center 4.0.
