The draft law on the organization and functioning of the National Committee for Human Rights of Cambodia is expected to be submitted to the Council of Ministers in the middle of next year
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CHRC) said that the draft law on the organization and functioning of the National Human Rights Committee of Cambodia (NHRC) is being expedited and is scheduled to be submitted to the Council of Ministers. In the middle of 2022.
The Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CHRC) on 26 November 2021, in collaboration with the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia (OHCHR), organized a consultative workshop with civil society on the draft law on The functioning of the National Committee for Human Rights of Cambodia (NHRC) aims to find more input.
"We are working hard to expedite the draft law and expect to submit it to the cabinet in the middle of next year." This was confirmed by Mr. Chet Chealy, Vice Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee during an interview with reporters.
Mr. Chet Chealy said that during the Khmer Rouge era, the right to life, a large part of human rights, was abolished by the organization, and whenever the organization wanted to take human life, it did so immediately. But today, human rights are heavily protected by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Mr. Chet Chealy added, "In order for the respect for human rights to be more effective and for Samdech Techo Hun Sen to pay attention to human rights, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee was allowed to draft this draft to promote and protect The rights of Cambodian citizens.
Meanwhile, Mr. Kata Un presented the background and the draft law that in the past, the draft law was submitted to civil society organizations (NGOs) as a draft, but did not work. Only now, in order for this draft law to take shape, the Prime Minister has decided to hand it over to the Cambodian Human Rights Committee.
Please be informed that the National Committee for Human Rights of Cambodia is an independent, neutral national body working in the field of human rights. This law has 8 chapters and 32 articles.
