(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, continued to appeal to owners of right-hand drive and left-hand drive vehicles who have not yet paid their taxes to pay their taxes in full. Before December 31, 2021 to get a 10% discount, if before, the tax will not be exempt.
Mr. Kun Nhem made this statement at a press conference on the progress of the implementation of the collection of import duties on existing duty-free vehicles this morning, November 26, 2021, via video.
Minister Kun Nhim stated, "I would like to call on car owners, both right-hand drive and left-hand drive, to hurry up and pay their taxes. Fulfilling the tax obligations is an obligation stipulated by the customs law. Obligations as stated in the law In order to receive a preferential tax of 10% on the total tax, please hurry to declare the tax on your car, left-hand drive car is before December 31, 2021.
Mr. Kun Nhim further stated that from the beginning of 2022 until June 30, 2022, left-hand drive vehicles will not receive 10% preference, they will have to pay 100% full tax. Once. For right-hand drive cars, car owners also have to rush to the car to show the post to deposit the same 10% tax deduction, and the tax rate will be reduced the same for both left-hand drive and right-hand drive vehicles.
Minister Kun Nhim also stated that the payment of taxes to the national budget is a contribution to help the nation to develop and serve the needs of the state in managing both social and economic work.
