Samdech Techo Hun Sen Begins to Lead the 13th Asia-Europe Summit on the Second Day
(Phnom Penh): At around 3 pm on Friday, November 26, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the 13th Asia-Europe Summit, presided over the summit at the Palace. Peace
Agenda: The second Asia-Europe Summit will discuss issues related to Kovid 19, socio-economic rehabilitation and development, the Asia-Europe Meeting, as well as international and regional issues, and the adoption of a working document. 13th Asia-Europe Summit, Closing Ceremony and Joint Press Conference
The closing ceremony of the Asia-Europe Summit and the press conference will also be broadcast live.
It should be noted that the 13th Asia-Europe Summit, which is hosted by Cambodia, officially opened on Thursday, November 25, with the participation of leaders from Asia-Europe countries, including the President, Prime Minister and About 51 senior leaders, including leaders of the European Union and the Secretary-General of ASEAN.
Yesterday's meeting was opened by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the European Council and Representative of the EU Coordinating Countries, President of the European Commission and Representative of the EU Coordinating Countries, Prime Minister of Russia The Middle East and South Asian Coordinating Countries, the Slovenian Prime Minister, the rotating chair of the Council of the European Union, and the EU Coordinating States and the Thai Prime Minister.
Yesterday's meeting also included a statement from representatives of the relevant meetings following the Asia-Europe Summit. The meeting then opened the discussion on the role of Asia-Europe in promoting multilateralism, a common theme, with the leaders of the Asia-Europe countries addressing a series of interventions in a series of about 30 letters.
For the first day of yesterday's meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the chairperson of the meeting, expressed his optimism that the results of the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) hosted by Cambodia are indeed an input. Valuable and intelligent for contributing to the promotion of multilateralism and the ASEM process.
Samdech Techo also highlighted that the meeting expressed full support for multilateralism, which is the foundation of peace, stability and global prosperity. He added that, of course, mutual respect, mutual understanding and trust are the principles on the path for multilateralism.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the meeting was committed to further enhance ASEM's role in promoting multilateralism and global governance, which the two regions need more to address common challenges.
Samdech Techo also highlighted the meeting's statement on the challenges of 19 Kovid disease, which has a serious impact on public health and the unprecedented socio-economic crisis.
He stressed that to address these challenges, the two sides agreed that solidarity, international cooperation and the promotion of multilateral vaccines are key. Therefore, protecting the health and security of the people as well as promoting unity between states should be our priority.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, continued to emphasize that economic recovery after Kovid-19 is a common priority of Asia and Europe. In this regard, the Meeting expressed support for strengthening the trading system based on the rule of law and commitment to protect the supply chain smoothly and unhindered, as well as promote the digitalization and explore the possibility of reopening safe tourism. And responsibilities.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Asia-Europe Summit on the 1st yesterday, most Asian-European leaders also committed to green and low-carbon development to keep global warming at bay. Not to exceed 1.5 degrees Celsius in accordance with the Paris Agreement on Climate.
To address this issue, Samdech Techo drew attention to the meeting that providing technical and financial assistance to developing countries must be a priority.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that the meeting also agreed that the past 25 years have provided a solid foundation for the Asia-Europe Partnership to move forward towards a brighter future. More environmentally friendly and durable. CPP Team Visits Pong Teuk Commune, Svay Rieng Province, Calls on People to Take Care of Their Health in Cold Weather
