(Kep): The Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia and the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism of Vietnam have agreed to launch a joint action plan to promote safe vaccination for tourists.
At the meeting, the two countries agreed to promote safe vaccination tourism, focusing on:
1: Encourage the resumption of tourism between the two countries by all means of transportation (land, sea, air), including
* Continue to promote self-driving tourism with the facilitation of safe travel
* Prepare to connect the two countries' tourist ports, urging the private sector of the two countries to study the connection quickly and efficiently.
2: Promote and study the market together under the theme "Two countries, one goal" at international events.
5. Encourage the organization of tourism promotion events in 2022 to celebrate the 55th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Vietnam.
The two sides shared information and experiences on the situation of Kovid 19, the response of the tourism sector to the spread of Kovid-19 and their respective international tourism plans. The two sides also reviewed each other's tourism promotion action plans as well as evaluated the results of past bilateral cooperation.
The Vietnamese side commended the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for effectively controlling the spread of Kovid-19 and implementing a successful vaccination campaign, especially in opening up the host country. International travelers and tourists have been fully vaccinated.
