The Information Office of the State Council of China publishes a white paper entitled "China-Africa Cooperation in a New Era"
On November 26, 2021, the Information Office of the State Council of China released a white paper entitled "China-Africa Cooperation in the New Era".
The White Paper includes four chapters: Building a Common Destiny Community between China and Africa, Closer Pioneering Cooperation in All Fields of China and Africa in the New Era, Strengthening Mutual Support and Establishing New design of China-Africa relations
The White Paper states that China and Africa have been a community of common destiny since the beginning. After entering the new era, Chinese President Xi Jinping outlined his views and policies with Africa in a pragmatic and honest manner, as well as the right interests, pointing the way forward for cooperation with Africa in New Age.
51 Royal Turtles Released in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): The European Union, Cambodian Wildlife Conservation Organization and the Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on November 26, 2021 released 51 turtles or turtles into the natural habitat through the Prek Sre system. Salt is located in Chamkar Luong commune, Kampong Seila district, Preah Sihanouk province.
Mr. Pum Sotha, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Fisheries Administration, said: "We are very grateful for the participation of local authorities, local communities, people and especially WCS, which has been rehabilitating the affected species. "This disaster to be present in this natural water again."
He also asked the relevant parties to continue the work of restoring this species of turtle and reminded some perpetrators who continue to trade this species will be punished before the law.
The EU has been funding wildlife conservation projects to combat illegal wildlife trade and to protect turtle and turtle nests, with WCS implementing projects in collaboration with the Fisheries Administration and local communities. The EU is also a key development partner in supporting Cambodia's sustainable management of key fisheries resources.
It is one of the 25 endangered species of freshwater and terrestrial turtles in the world. This species is listed on the IUCN Red List as the most endangered species and is considered a reptile species representing Cambodia, as defined in the 2005 Royal Decree.
Since then, WCS and the Fisheries Administration have worked together to protect the species from extinction. These turtle conservation activities include protection of turtle nests, rearing after hatching, prevention of illegal trade, enforcement of law enforcement, monitoring, promotion and support of community livelihoods under the financial support of the owners. Many donors include: EU and Mandai Nature.
The release of the royal turtle is the result of nearly two decades of efforts to protect turtle nests, care for all baby turtles at the Koh Kong Reptile Conservation Center, and protect turtles in communities along the canals. Donor-supported salt fields are listed above. This is the sixth release of royal turtles into the Prek Sre Ambel system since 2015, for a total of 147 cases.
Pursuant to the Law on the Administration of Medicines and the Law on the Amendment of the Law on the Administration of Medicines, all the circulation of pharmaceutical products or quality products for the prevention or treatment of all kinds of diseases in the Kingdom of Cambodia must have a visa number or an order from the Ministry of Health. .
Therefore, people, before buying any kind of medicine or health supplement product, please check the packaging on the packaging and the correct label is in two parts:
1: The upper part has the name of the Import Export Pharmaceutical Company 2: The lower part has the visa number or the list as attached.
The Ministry of Health would like to inform all citizens to stop believing in the promotion of unregistered drugs through the above Facebook social network account and to stop using these products.
The above Facebook account holders and other stakeholders must immediately stop importing, distributing or promoting "Hemorrhoid" products without the above registration number.
The Ministry of Health will take strict legal action against the above account holders and any related persons who import, distribute or advertise the products without the above registration number in accordance with the Law Amending the Law on Drug Administration in force.
