The new strain of the virus was found in a person who returned to Israel from Malawi, Africa. The other two cases of people who have just returned from abroad are also suspected of being infected with the new strain of virus B.1.1529. Both samples were tested to determine the genetic data of the virus and are awaiting results.
In addition to South Africa and Israel, Hong Kong and several other African countries have also been infected with the new strain of the virus. Israel on Thursday announced a ban on travelers from seven African countries in response to the discovery of a new strain of the virus in South Africa. On the same day, the United Kingdom issued a ban on travelers from six African countries for the same reason.
(Siem Reap): Banteay Srei district has been designated by the Angkor Center for Biodiversity Conservation (ACCB) as the world's first "whispering" breeding ground, located in the Kbal Spean resort area of Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province. Construction has been completed.
According to Banteay Srei District Governor Khim Finang's Facebook page, the endangered bird breeding site is the first in the world to breed endangered species that will provide a safe environment for endangered species. Recover to rehabilitate and make it easier for squirrels to lay eggs and raise their young.
Whistle eggs collected from the wild will also be artificially hatched here, and the young will be cared for until they reach adulthood before being put into breeding programs with hope. That all the offspring will be released back into the wild in the future.
The new mutated COVID-19 virus B.1.1.529 was first detected in South Africa this week and has spread to neighboring Africa and Hong Kong. Countries such as Britain and Israel have decided to temporarily suspend flights with six African countries over concerns about the new virus.
