China has signed more than 30 bilateral agricultural cooperation agreements with ASEAN member countries and implemented more than 200 agricultural technology exchange projects. By 2020, bilateral trade in agricultural products will reach 43 billion US dollars, accounting for 17.2 percent of China's total foreign agricultural trade, official data show.
ASEAN member countries are among China's top 10 import sources.
