Mr. Keo Remy said that for the two-year period of July 2021, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee has begun compiling those recommendations to become a mid-term report.
Regarding the draft law on the establishment of the National Human Rights Institution, Mr. Keo Remy said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has assigned the task of civil society organizations to draft this law since 2006, but so far No draft law has been approved by civil society organizations yet, so Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to hand over this task to the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to expedite the drafting of this law.
Regarding this case, Mr. Keo Remy pointed out that the draft law was submitted by the Cambodian Human Rights Committee for a series of discussions from the international level, internal consultations between civil society organizations, and on the 26th. Tomorrow, November, the draft law will be debated with 10 civil society organizations working in the field of human rights at the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
