As planned, after a year-long delay, at 3 pm on Thursday, November 25, 2021, the 13th Asia-Europe Summit kicked off with the participation of the Prime Minister. And 51 senior officials from Asia and Europe, accompanied by senior EU officials and the ASEAN Secretary-General.
As the host of the Asia-Europe Summit, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen was invited to open the meeting with the President of the European Council, the President of the European Commission, the Prime Minister of Russia and the Prime Minister of Thailand.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the theme "Strengthening Multilateralism for Joint Growth" for the 13th Asia-Europe Summit, which Cambodia has chosen, is an appropriate topic for discussion.
In this speech, Samdech Techo highlighted and highlighted the strengths of ASEM, which are based on its core principles: informality, flexibility, mutual respect in the spirit of consensus and equal partnership.
In a world of crisis, geopolitical competition and trade wars, he reminded Asian-European leaders that the two regions needed to work harder on the principle and required a response and response. Together.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that Asia-Europe leaders have a shared responsibility to ensure that ASEM continues to be an important and strong inter-regional forum that can bring great benefits to its people. Both can contribute more broadly to ensuring and maintaining world peace, stability, prosperity and development.
In addition to highlighting the importance of joint cooperation between Asia and Europe to respond to current global issues, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted some of the essential objectives of the Asia-Europe Summit. The 13th as well. For Samdech Techo, the purpose of this meeting is 6, including:
