CMH President: Measures to raise tobacco taxes as a win-win strategy to reduce smoking deaths
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mom Kong, Executive Director of the Cambodian Movement for Health (CMH), stated that raising taxes on tobacco products is a win-win strategy to reduce deaths and infections due to consumption. Tobacco products.
Dr. Mom Kong said this on the morning of November 25, 2021 in the final public speaking program after the topic: Tobacco tax measures and Kovid 19 "with the participation of representatives. Ministry of Education, Ministry of Health and Ministry of Economy, organized in the Cambodia-Korea Cooperation Center of the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
Dr. Mom Kong added that when the tobacco tax is raised, the state will get more tax revenue, and the experience of countries around the world as well as ASEAN countries also made it clear that when the tax on tobacco products is increased. The state tax revenue, such as Thailand, Singapore and the Philippines, in particular, will receive large sums of money into the state to pay for the health care of citizens to prevent Kovid 19.
The doctor added that smoking was not only a factor in the transmission of Kovid 19, but that smokers could also become seriously infected with Kovid 19 because they already had lung damage. As a result, smokers face a greater risk of death if they are infected with Kovid 19. In addition, smoking also increases the chances of contracting Kovid-19 because direct contact between the hands, mouth and cigarettes increases the risk of infection.
It should be noted that the use of tobacco products is a burden for the government to solve because the use of tobacco products causes people to get sick and die, of which about 15,000 Cambodians died due to smoking. In addition, tobacco use costs about $ 649 million, or 3 percent of Cambodia's gross domestic product.
