Rev. Sar Son, sister of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, dies
(Phnom Penh): Rev. Sar Son, the sister of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, passed away at 9:45 pm on Wednesday, November 24, 2021 at the age of 74.
The body of Rev. Sar Son was laid to rest in a traditional Buddhist ceremony at 368, Concrete Road, Factory 1 Village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, behind the Sen Sok District Hall.
The death of Disciple Sar Son has brought great sorrow and grief to all his family and relatives.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak committed to 7 points to the Cambodian Red Cross and the people of Kampong Thom
(Kampong Thom): With strong determination, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, during his appointment as the new Chairman of the Kampong Thom Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, made seven commitments to the Cambodian Red Cross and the people of Kampong Thom.
The seven commitments include:
1. He will adhere to the seven fundamental principles of the International Red Cross and Red Crescent Movement: humanity, impartiality, neutrality, independence, voluntary service, unity and universality.
2. He will strive to follow the guidelines of the Cambodian Red Cross in order to successfully fulfill his humanitarian duties.
3. He will maintain unity within the Branch Committee and accept consultation with the Branch Honors Committee and agree to work together to solve challenges with a high sense of responsibility.
4: He will strive to lead the branch executive team to perform well in accordance with the strategy of the Cambodian Red Cross.
5. He will work hard to continue the work of expanding the Cambodian Red Cross volunteers at the local level and strengthen community health education activities.
6. He will strive to expand and strengthen the activities of the Cambodian Red Cross youth in educational institutions as a model in humanitarian work, educational institutions and society.
7. He will continue to strive for good cooperation with authorities at all levels, departments, institutions, national and international organizations in the cause of humanitarian mobilization to contribute to reducing the suffering of vulnerable people.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak has been appointed as the Chairman of the Kampong Thom Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, replacing Mr. Sok Lou, who has been assigned a new task in Battambang Province.
At the same time, Ms. Pum Chantyny instructed Mr. Nguon Rattanak to continue to lead humanitarian work, disaster management, to find philanthropists, to check the composition of branch staff, to strengthen the capacity to perform humanitarian work, to adhere to the seven basic principles of the International Red Cross Movement. The Red Crescent is humane, impartial, neutral, independent, voluntary, united and universal.
