The 13th Asia-Europe Summit will be chaired by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the host of the meeting. As the host of an important meeting for Asia-Europe, representing more than 5 billion people, Cambodia has decided to discuss the theme "Strengthening Multilateralism for Joint Growth". Two days today (November 25-26).
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Asia-Europe Summit, which Cambodia is hosting, will adopt three key outcome documents, including: (1) the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting Chair Statement (2) Phnom Penh on Socio-Economic Rehabilitation after the Kovid-19 Outbreak and (3) Future Action Papers on Asia-Europe Connections.
The Asia-Europe Summit is an intergovernmental forum established in 1996 to promote dialogue and cooperation between Asia and Europe. The Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) is considered the only informal forum for dialogue and cooperation between Asia and Europe, focusing on strengthening partnerships, promoting peace and security, and promoting economic development. A sustainable society.
The Asia-Europe Meeting covers political and security aspects, economic cooperation and socio-cultural aspects, and this mechanism is also an excellent forum for leaders to address global challenges.
Since its first summit in March 1996 in Bangkok, which has only 26 founding members, the forum has expanded its membership to 53 countries and partners, including 30 in Europe and 21 in Asia. EU and ASEAN Secretariat. Taken together, the ASEM represents about 65 percent of the global economy, 60 percent of the population, 55 percent of trade and 75 percent of world tourism.
Over the past 25 years, ASEM has made significant institutional changes and contributed to solving complex regional and global issues that required close cooperation between the two continents. .
The hosting of the ASEM13 Summit reflects Cambodia's highest commitment to promoting multilateralism, as well as its active participation in the international community to address challenges. Global today and emerging recently.
