Ministry of Social Affairs Holds Training Course on Minimum Policies and Standards on Protection of Victims of Human Trafficking
(Kampong Cham): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on November 25, 2021, opened a training course on "Policies and Minimum Standards on the Protection of the Rights of Victims of Human Trafficking" in Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province.
The opening ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, with the participation of Mr. Pok Chantho, Deputy Governor of Koh Sotin District, Mr. Kong Sophonara, Advisor to the Ministry of Social Affairs, Ms. Prum Sokhon, Director of the Opposition Department Human Trafficking and Victim Integration, Mr. Un Vuthy, Project Manager for the Australian Anti-Trafficking Program in Cambodia.
Mr. Nhek Vannara said that human trafficking has been occurring everywhere in the form of transnational and organized crime, and that it has had a negative impact on individuals, families and communities, especially at the national level. Region and world.
At the same time, he said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been making efforts to formulate, disseminate and implement policies, strategies, plans, bilateral and multilateral agreements and mechanisms aimed at combating and minimizing trafficking. People and business on people in the national, sub-regional, regional and global.
He said that the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, which has been mandated by the Royal Government to protect and provide support services to victims, the Ministry has actively worked and achieved many achievements in protecting victims of crime. Human trafficking, policy-making, prevention of human trafficking, strengthening cooperation and enhancing partnerships.
Despite the Ministry's many achievements, the protection of victims of trafficking has not yet been fully addressed, especially the provision of support services for victims.
The "Minimum Policy and Standards on the Protection of the Rights of Victims of Human Trafficking" training course was organized in two sessions in Kang Meas and Koh Sotin districts, Kampong Cham province, with the aim of providing new knowledge and experience to service providers. The local level, which is the authority, has the authority to help the victims in time in their villages.
