(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 25, 2021, the National Assembly resumed its 6th session of the 6th legislature to elect the First Vice President and other members, as well as to discuss and approve two more draft laws. Related to finance.
The session was chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, with the participation of members of the National Assembly.
The resumption of the National Assembly session has the following six agendas: First, the decision on the validity of the mandate of Mr. Un Bunhan, a Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom constituency, replacing the late Dr. Nguon Nhel, who passed away.
Second: Election of Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cheam Yeap as the First Vice President of the National Assembly.
Third: Election of Mr. Chheang Vun as a member of the Economic, Financial, Banking and Auditing Committee of the National Assembly and Mr. Cheap Sivan as a member of the Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information Committee of the National Assembly.
Fourth: Discussion and approval of the draft law on the approval of the ASEAN Protocol on Strengthening Dispute Resolution Mechanisms.
Fifth: Discussion and approval of the draft law on finance for management in 2022.
