Governor of the State Bank of Vietnam praises Cambodia's success in speeding up vaccinations, protecting people's health and boosting economic activity
(Phnom Penh): On November 24, 2021, the National Bank of Cambodia held an online bilateral meeting with the State Bank of Vietnam. The bilateral meeting is held annually to strengthen and expand cooperation and friendly relations between the two central banks.
The two sides praised the progress of bilateral cooperation between the two central banks in the past, which has contributed to the development of the banking sector. Good cooperation between the banking sector has contributed to the growth of trade, investment and tourism in both countries.
The two sides exchanged views on the progress of the Cambodian macroeconomic situation, the development of the banking sector, the central bank's response to the negative effects of Kovid-19, the promotion of non-bank payments and the review of progress. With the determination of the direction of bilateral cooperation.
She praised the measures taken by the National Bank of Cambodia during the period of Kovid-19, which achieved good results in maintaining the progress and stability of the banking system and stabilizing the exchange rate and lowering inflation.
The State Bank of Vietnam also welcomed the introduction of modern payment systems, especially the Bakong system, which is a payment system that helps solve cross-institutional payment problems and connectivity with both local and regional payment systems.
Mr. Chea Chanto also thanked the State Bank of Vietnam, especially Governor Nguyen Thi Hong and the management of the State Bank of Vietnam for their excellent cooperation under the Memorandum of Understanding between the two central banks on general cooperation. Bank oversight and on money laundering and terrorist financing.
He also thanked the State Bank of Vietnam and the Government of Vietnam for supporting human resource development by continuing to provide scholarships to National Bank of Cambodia officials for undergraduate and doctoral studies in Vietnam.
The meeting was successful and fruitful in the spirit of friendship, brotherhood and good cooperation. The meeting also set priority work priorities for bilateral cooperation, including:
* Sharing knowledge on developing database systems for exchange rates, * Promoting the use of the national currency, * Strengthening risk-based controls and developing payment systems.
