Senior Minister Kun Kim urges continued attention to veterans' lives
(Kampong Chhnang): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, urged all relevant authorities to continue to pay attention to their livelihood. And the lives of veterans.
Senior Minister Kun Kim's urging came as he was inaugurated as the Honorary President and President of the Veterans Association in Kampong Chhnang province on Wednesday morning, November 24, 2021. In that, Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, was appointed as the Honorary President of the Association and Mr. Ou Sophea, Military Commander of Kampong Chhnang Province was the President of the Association.
At the ceremony, the Senior Minister reminded of the struggles and sacrifices of veterans in the cause of the motherland during the national crisis. For Senior Minister Kun Kim, all veterans have been associated with Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the search for peace and to prevent the return of the Pol Pot genocidal regime.
The Senior Minister also said that as Samdech Techo's staff on the work of veterans, he has always been warned and reminded by Samdech Techo to pay attention to the well-being and lives of veterans. In particular, efforts must be made to address the challenges of veterans and to improve their livelihoods through the provision of social land concessions, housing and the promotion of cultivation.
In response to this urging, Mr. Sun Sovannarith, who was elected as the Honorary President of the Kampong Chhnang Veterans Association, is determined to work hard to sustain all the shortcomings of the needy veterans in the lack of shelter. Stay, enjoy the land and so on.
Separately, Mr. Ou Sophea, President of the Association, is committed to improving the living standards and well-being of veterans. In particular, assign teams at all levels down to the grassroots to find out about the well-being, shelter and accommodation and solve some other practical problems.
