Surprised by the authorities to intervene immediately, it is suspected that there are illegal detainees in Boeung Keng Kang district, but the landlord is locked from outside because he does not pay rent
(Phnom Penh): The Boeung Keng Kang District Police Inspectorate has launched an operation to rescue two couples after a suspicion of illegal detention, but the landlord locked the door from the outside because the landlord This is not expensive for the landlord.
This incident caused a surprise at noon on November 24, 2021 at Jesse Airlines along Mao Tse Toung Street, Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
According to the report from the scene, before the incident, two men and women were seen riding a black 2015 Honda Dream 125 with a cleaning device, stopped the motorcycle and walked in. At Jesse Airlines to clean the company premises, a woman with two chains locked the door in front of the company.
Later, two men and a woman came down and cleaned up. Immediately, he saw that the door was locked from the outside, so he reported to the specialized police force at the post-district to come down to the company's location.
After receiving the information that the door was locked, the Boeung Keng Kang District Police Inspectorate arrived at the scene and asked for information about the two men and women, and then the police contacted the owner of Jesse Airlines for further questioning. .
The police contacted the landlord and the landlord said that because the owner of Jesse Airlines had not paid his rent for many months, he arrived at the company's location today. Suddenly there is no company equipment below.
He immediately went to buy a chain key to lock the door, but did not know that two men and women were cleaning at the company above. At that time, the police let the landlord rent a hat and open the door for the two men and women to come out. Authorities called two people, a couple and a representative of the landlord, to the Tuol Svay Prey I Administrative Police Station for further questioning.
According to the authorities, the owner of the house is Sok Huot, 53 years old, living in house No. 6, Street 328, Village 3, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey 1, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh Separately, 2 sanitation staff include:
