China joins CPTPP to boost global economic recovery and develop global trade
BEIJING, Sept. 16 (Xinhua) - China applied for accession to the Comprehensive Trans-Pacific Partnership and Progress Agreement (CPTPP) on September 16, which has drawn the attention of the international community.
The answer to this question can be obtained at a press conference held by the Chinese Ministry of Commerce on October 19.
At the press conference, Gao Feng, spokesman for the Chinese Ministry of Commerce, said that China welcomes all multilateral trade agreements in line with WTO principles. The world promotes economic globalization and regional economic integration under the principles of openness, environment and transparency.
China believes that China's accession to the CPTPP on the basis of reaching the RCEP will play a positive role in promoting economic integration in the Asia-Pacific region and promoting global economic recovery, trade development and investment growth. In particular, it will provide better quality goods and services to the people of the CPTPP Member States in order to bring tangible benefits to the people.
According to the website of the Chinese Ministry of Commerce, the free trade agreement between the People's Republic of China and the Royal Government of Cambodia will enter into force on January 1, 2022. The free trade agreement between China and Cambodia is a new symbol in the development of bilateral economic and trade relations, which will be conducive to bringing greater happiness to enterprises and people of the two countries.
