Mr. Zack Pele's assessment and appreciation was made during his courtesy call and discussion with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Peace Palace on Wednesday morning, November 24, 2021.
Eang Sophalleng, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, told reporters after the meeting that during the meeting, the French Ambassador expressed his pleasure to be appointed Ambassador to Cambodia.
In addition to expressing appreciation for his diplomatic mission in Cambodia, Jacques Perle also praised and admired the development and progress of Cambodia, a country devastated by the fires of war in the past. The government representative also expressed his congratulations and appreciation for the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who overcame the epidemic of Kovid 19 and achieved the Kovid 19 vaccine at the rate of High.
According to the French ambassador, the success of Cambodia's vaccination has also made about 400 French companies investing in Cambodia very happy. This success has led to improved economic and trade activity.
During the meeting, Mr. Jacques Pele informed Samdech Techo that French President Manuel Macron will attend the Asia-Europe Summit, which Cambodia is hosting tomorrow.
The meeting also highlighted the cooperation between ASEAN and Europe. He said he would push for stronger ASEAN-EU cooperation to make the cooperation between the two regions a risk-free and environmentally friendly one.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed and congratulated Mr. Zack Pele on his appointment as Ambassador to Cambodia. Samdech Techo also thanked the French Ambassador for his assessment of Cambodia's vaccination policy.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, also agreed with Mr. Jacques Perle on strengthening cooperation between Cambodia and France, as well as strengthening cooperation in various international frameworks.
For bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and France, Samdech Techo suggested that Cambodia and France should further deepen cooperation in all possible fields, including cooperation under the international umbrella. .
