Mr. Seng E reminded, "Our people need to cross from Stung Trang to Kroch Chhmar or from Kroch Chhmar to Stung Trang, it is difficult to travel across the river."
The hardships of the past have faded away and only traces remain for the people of Stung Trang and Krouch Chhmar districts after the Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar bridge has been put through since the Khmer New Year. Not only enjoying the trip, every evening, the people of this area always come up to visit the bridge, count on the water, seem to miss the hardships of the past.
Both Emon and Seng Ey rejoiced at the achievements of the new bridge over this tragic past. They saw that the bridge had provided the necessary services for the people to travel and transport agricultural products without the fear and anxiety as before.
The elders in both villages also saw that the presence of a bridge, which is a link of Cambodia-China friendship, will contribute to boosting the family economy of the people in this area even better.
It should be noted that the Cambodia-China Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar Friendship Bridge was officially inaugurated this morning, Tuesday, November 23, 2021 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
"Cambodia-China Stung Trang-Kroch Chhmar Friendship Bridge" began construction under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on February 9, 2018. The bridge starts at km 58 + 200 on the west bank on Provincial Road No. 2714 at Boeung Deng village, Prek Kak commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province, connecting to the east bank of the Mekong River at Kdol Kandal village, Trea commune, Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province.
The bridge body is 1,131 meters long, 13.5 meters wide, paved with 5 cm thick rubber concrete, there are 2 lanes for cars, 2 lanes for motorbikes, 2 lanes for pedestrians. The main road on both sides of the bridge connecting to National Road 71C is 8,323 meters long. The total length of the bridge and connecting road is 9,454 meters.
The bridge and connecting road took 42 months to build by Shanghai Construction Company (SCG) and technical inspection by Guangzhou Van An Technical Consulting Company at a cost of nearly 57 million US dollars.
In addition, the project also shows the connection of hope of the people living in this area. In particular, the religious harmony between Buddhists and the Cambodian Muslim community will be closer and stronger through joint communication and business relations.
He added that this new achievement is an invaluable commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia to the people of Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum, as well as people across the country for general and long-term use under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the General Guide and a win-win political operator who brought peace to the motherland of Cambodia.
