Rubber prices rise in Vietnam as industry firms enjoy profit
Vietnam's natural rubber industry has recovered significantly as the Kovid-19 outbreak has negatively affected production and business in all sectors of the economy.
Vietnam's Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development reported that rubber production increased by 13.9% in volume and 46.5% in value in the first 10 months of this year compared to the same period last year. Previous
The average export price of rubber products in the first 10 months reached $ 1,680 per tonne, up 4.1 percent from the same period last year.
According to a report released by the Association of Natural Rubber Producers (ANRPC), total global demand for natural rubber this year is projected to increase 9.3 percent year-on-year to 14.1 billion tonnes. Meanwhile, supply is estimated to increase by only 2 percent to 13.86 billion tons.
The global economic recovery will boost transport activity in both civil and industrial sectors, creating a growing demand for rubber, a key factor in demand.
High rubber prices have had a very positive impact on the profits of the rubber industry since the beginning of the year.
