Woman stabbed several times by suspects in Kambol district
(Phnom Penh): A woman was stabbed by another suspect with a knife and robbed her house, causing serious injuries, but the robber did not get the property, and later the suspect was arrested by the police and taken for questioning And take legal action.
The incident happened at 5:20 AM on November 20, 2021 in Prey Tapok Village, Sangkat Ovulok, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh.
The victim, 48-year-old Vit Sokhon, who lived in the village, was injured in several places. As for the suspect, his name is Chamroeun Udom, 31 years old, he used to live in Trapeang Arak village, Sangkat Ovulok, and now he lives in Pong village, Sangkat Ovulok, Khan Kambol.
Police said that in the early hours of the morning, the victim woke up and boiled water to make tea, while the suspect moved into his altar. When the victim heard the sound of the body moving, she went out to look, but saw nothing, then went to the bedroom and suddenly saw the suspect was moving his wallet and jewelry.
He immediately ran into the altar room and was chased by the suspect, who stabbed him several times, causing him to bleed profusely. Only then did he have the opportunity to run outside, shouting for help.
The police officer said that at that time, his children ran to help their mother, but when they arrived, the suspect ran over the fence and escaped, but the victim knew the suspect and told him that his name was Udom. Trapeang Arak village robbed him. After that, the children complained to the Ouk Lok Police Station and the Kambol District Criminal Police to inspect the scene and arrest the suspect, bring him for questioning and take legal action.
