(Phnom Penh): Disinfection machines, air purifiers, disinfectants - Bottles have been handed over to WKL Echo Indochina by the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to take measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 while the disease is not Still fading out of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Nuon Pharath considered that the above-mentioned humanitarian and virtuous gestures really contributed significantly to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration and the Royal Government in accordance with the call of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to take action to prevent The spread of Kovid-19 virus in Phnom Penh as well as across the country was timely.
He said, "This noble generosity shows the consideration and compassion for our compatriots, based on the cause of national unity as a whole in the spirit of helping each other in the circumstances that the nation has been facing the danger of Prevention of Kovid 19 virus. This wonderful sympathy will be remembered by the Royal Government, the Phnom Penh administration and all Cambodians. ”
The Ambassador made this statement in front of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, at the handover ceremony of 19 Kovid disease prevention equipment donated by the Chinese military to the Cambodian side on November 23, 2021. At Phnom Penh International Airport.
Wang Wentian said that the global Kovid 19 situation continues to be tense, world peace and regional stability have many challenges, but the Cambodian and Chinese armies continue to support each other, overcome all obstacles together, and push forward Strong practical cooperation between the two militaries continues to enhance the level of capacity to defend national security, protect sovereignty and serve the people.
"The Chinese People's Liberation Army will continue to work with the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) to strictly implement the consensus strategy set by the leaders to promote practical cooperation between the two militaries and enhance the two countries' comprehensive strategic partnership," he said. "Deepen and make a greater contribution to promoting the interests of the people of China and Cambodia more."
According to the Chinese ambassador, the two armies are steel brothers, know each other and have a hand-to-foot relationship. In recent years, under the direct leadership and full encouragement of Chinese President Xi Jinping and Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the two armies have taken a new step in a series of areas of cooperation. Military, military training and military alliances.
After the outbreak of Kovid 19, both countries and the military have helped each other and donated materials to prevent the disease several times. The cooperation of the two militaries in preventing the disease not only sets an example of international military cooperation, but also actively contributes to building a common destiny community between China and Cambodia.
Mr. Wang Wentian recalled that Prince Tea Banh had visited the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia to hand over a gift of 19 Kovid vaccines to the Chinese Ministry of National Defense, which made the Chinese side very excited. The Chinese military has not only sent medical and medical experts to Cambodia to facilitate the prevention of Kovid 19, but has also provided Cambodia with vaccines and equipment.
