The bonds, launched by the National League for Democracy (NUG), an alliance between pro-democracy groups, ethnic armed groups, and former members of Aung San Suu Kyi's government, said the bonds went on sale Monday. Most of them are to Myanmar nationals living abroad for $ 100, $ 500, $ 1,000, and $ 5,000 with a two-year tenure.
