The Yellow Sea is the sea between China and the Korean Peninsula. The reason for its name is probably due to the yellow-brown water flowing in from the Yellow River, while its water is loaded with soil and sand from the lowlands.
The White Sea is located in northwestern Russia and is completely under Russian jurisdiction. Because it is near the Arctic of the North Pole, the sea is covered with ice for between six and seven months every year. One theory is that it is called the White Sea because of this.
