Ministry of Posts Releases Results of Minister Chea Van Det's Official Visit to Korea to Strengthen Cambodia-Korea Digital Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Ms. Lim Hyesook, Minister of Science, Information and Communication Technology of the Republic of Korea, Mr. Chea Van Det, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, led an official visit to the Republic of Korea from November 15 to 2021 to further strengthen digital cooperation between the two countries.
During the visit, Minister Chea Van Det discussed with Ms. Lim Hay Suk on the development of digital technology, 5th generation telecommunications technology (5G), artificial intelligence cloud technology and data analysis to promote the digital transformation. Effective and fast.
In addition, the delegation met with Moon Yong-sik, Director of the Korea National News Agency, to discuss digital government cooperation between the two institutions, such as sharing experiences of implementing digital government policy. Cooperation Digital Government Cooperation Center, Human Resource Training on Cloud Technology Development and Digital Technology Development.
The delegation learned about data integration between individual ministries and state institutions, which were isolated 15 years ago, leading to high costs and limited security. The delegation also discussed with Naver and Samsung SDS data storage, data analysis technology, data security, protection and human resource development.
