Cambodia plans to build a large international university hospital at Kob Srov Road under $ 80 million project
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia plans to build a large international university hospital at Kob Srov Road in Phnom Penh under a $ 80 million project, a loan from a Korean bank and a contribution from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
A delegation of Korean companies who came to Cambodia to study the construction of this large university hospital was allowed by Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, to meet and discuss work at the Ministry of Health on the evening of the 22nd. This November 2021.
After the meeting, Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, confirmed to the media that the construction project has been approved by the Head of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Economy and Finance, located on Kob Srov Road, Phnom Penh, on a land size of more than 2 The planned $ 80 million hectare includes $ 66 million in Korean bank loans and $ 14 million in government contributions.
She said that including the study and inspection of the location, the hospital can be built in 2 to 4 years.
She stated that the University Hospital is the largest university in Cambodia and is under the auspices of the Ministry of Health by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to empower the Ministry of Health while Cambodia is fighting Kovid. 19 and have successfully treated people as well as provided services.
She added that the university hospital can provide a place for students who have graduated from colleges and universities to practice their studies, and there will be professional doctors and professors who have just graduated abroad, as well as parties in ASEAN. Also participate.
