(Battambang): Vendors selling food items such as porridge, noodles said that the gathering of this group of traders began on the afternoon of November 22, 2021 in order to ask Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Battambang to intervene for them. Selling food, vegetables, fruits, fish, meat around the same Boeung Chhouk market without moving to a new location next to the Boeung Chhouk parking lot at a distance of 200-300 meters.
Other prahok sellers also confirmed that the owner of Boeung Chhouk Market recently told everyone that the owner of the market asked to remove the place where the vendors are selling in order to maintain order, so it is necessary for all sellers. On sale at the new location from November 25 onwards. More than 600 traders insisted that Mr. Sok Lou, the provincial governor, help the people.
In this regard, Battambang provincial administration officials assigned five business representatives to meet with the deputy governor in charge, but the traders refused to meet because they wanted to meet with Mr. Sok Lou orally because the governor was busy. They agreed to dissolve and wait to meet with Mr. Sok Lou in person on November 23, 2021 tomorrow.
