Elections are scheduled under a law issued by Libyan Parliament Speaker Aguila Saleh in September 2021. According to the law, the first round of presidential elections is scheduled for December 24, while parliamentary elections will be held in January or February next year.
Last year, a UN-led political dialogue forum reached a master plan to end the civil war in Libya after an eastern group's campaign to seize the western capital, Tripoli, failed. The plan led to the formation of Dbeibah's current interim government and demanded democratic parliamentary and presidential elections.
