Speaking to Fresh News by telephone on November 22, Mr. Sok Kim Choeun, Director of the Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, Kampot Province, said that currently there are 10,000 tons of salt in storage, which can supply a month. More.
He said that although the amount of salt in the warehouse is small, but there will be no shortage of salt to supply domestic demand from this period until the beginning of 2022, because the salt on the market is high because In October, some traders bought stocks.
"At the end of October, the removal of salt from the market was so severe that only a few tons of salt remained in the cascade," he said. There is little stock left, but it is in the depot because the merchants sometimes he is smart, he sees that the salt is good for him, he buys the stock, they buy the stock for the fishing season, so there is no shortage of salt for this year, maybe enough for the year. 2022 In the early months of the salt production season.
The salt production season in Kampot and Kep for 2022 has arrived, from November 2021 to May 2022. But until now, salt production has not started yet, as it rains almost every day.
Kim Choeun said that if the weather is not conducive to salt production next year, there may be salt imports from China and India to meet domestic demand.
In particular, the production of salt for export by local enterprises does not seem to be a problem, but exports are small due to shipping costs.
"Production is normal, we hope we can produce more in 2022, and now we have started to prepare the fields for harvest in January 2022," she said. "If we have more funds, we can expand our production capacity to the first 50,000 tonnes for next year and increase next year to supply both domestically and abroad."
According to the salt production report of the Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation of Kampot Province, in 2021, the salt production area is 2,857.23 hectares, with 139 production groups, producing 68,682 tons.
The Foreign Ministry said in a statement that Xi Jinping's five proposals include:
* First, to build a peaceful home together as China prepares to deepen cooperation in the field of defense, transnational crime and to sign a protocol to the Treaty on the Armsless Southeast Asia. Nuclear (SEANWFZ).
* Second, build a secure home together with China's commitment to support ASEAN health protection barriers and strengthen effective cooperation on disaster management.
* Third: Build a prosperous home together as China will provide 1.5 billion US dollars in development investment projects for three years and is ready to work with ASEAN to reap the benefits. Full of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) and the revised ASEAN-China Free Trade Area and to increase support for human resource development.
* Fourth: Build a beautiful house together, focusing more cooperation on green development and blue economy, among other cooperation.
* Fifth: Build a peaceful home together by promoting tourism, people-to-people exchanges, especially among young people and young leaders. ASEAN, China Leaders Agree to Establish Comprehensive Strategic Partnership
(Phnom Penh): At the ASEAN-China Special Summit to Commemorate the 30th Anniversary of the ASEAN-China Dialogue Partnership, which was held on video on November 22, 2021, ASEAN-China Leaders Agreed to Establish As a strategic partner in all aspects. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News.
At the meeting, Xi Jinping made five proposals to strengthen ASEAN-China relations, including:
1. Build a peaceful home together as China prepares to deepen cooperation in the field of defense, transnational crime and in signing the Protocol to the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons in Southeast Asia. SEANWFZ)
2. Build a secure home together with China's commitment to support ASEAN health protection barriers and strengthen effective cooperation on disaster management
3. Build a prosperous home together as China will provide 1.5 billion US dollars in development investment projects for three years and is ready to work with ASEAN to take full advantage of Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) and the revised ASEAN-China Free Trade Area and to increase support for human resource development
4: Build a beautiful house together by focusing on wider cooperation on green development and blue economy among other cooperation and
5. Build a friendly home together by promoting tourism, people-to-people exchanges, especially among young people and young leaders.
In tackling the effects of Kovid-19, the leaders pledged to strengthen ASEAN-China post-Kovid-19 cooperation for long-term sustainable development, including by supporting the ASEAN Comprehensive Rehabilitation Framework. (ACRF) as well. The leaders shared the view that the rapid ratification and implementation of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) will accelerate economic recovery.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also attended the summit at the invitation of Xi Jinping, co-chair of the meeting. At the meeting, the Prime Minister congratulated China on achieving its national development goals in building a moderately prosperous society and steady progress towards its second century goals.
(Kampong Cham): The murderer who raped and killed a girl in Chamkar Leu District, Kampong Cham Province, on his way home from school, was arrested by Kampong Cham Provincial Police on the afternoon of November 22, 2021, after escaping After the action on November 20, 2021.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal told Fresh News that after identifying the perpetrators, he ordered the provincial criminal force, the technical police and the district criminal police to launch a search operation. Who escaped.
According to the General Commissioner, based on the research, the competent authorities determined that the suspect named Mab Komsat alias Alan, 16 years old, living in the same village / commune, acted while the victim was on his way home from school. At the scene in Prey Chamkar Pout.
The police continued to search for the suspect and arrested him at 2:15 pm on November 22, 2021, at Prey Chamkar, behind Mondul Vibassana Pagoda, Pang Village, Chounang Commune, Taing Kork District. Kampong Thom Province. According to the preliminary answer, the suspect confessed that he actually raped and killed and sold the victim's phone in Phnom Penh for 200,000 riel to buy clothes and drive back home.
The case was shared by Facebook users who sent condolences to the family of the deceased after the death of the victim and condemned the brutal actions of the perpetrator, who was just 16 years old. International Monetary Fund (IMF) urges China to address financial risks in a coordinated and clear manner
In a statement issued by the fund's officials, which recently concluded its consultation on Article IV 2021 with China, the IMF said: "China's economic recovery is strong. "Better but unbalanced and the momentum of growth is slowing while downside risks are rising."
The International Monetary Fund (IMF) has blamed China's slowdown in economic growth for the speedy withdrawal of policy support, which has hurt recurring consumption from the Kovid-19 epidemic and caused power shortages and slowdowns. Investment in real estate.
The IMF said: "Fiscal policy, which has been drastically withdrawn this year, should be temporarily shifted towards a neutral stance and focus on strengthening social protection and promoting green investment rather than spending. "On traditional infrastructure."
According to Reuters, the IMF also called for a "comprehensive banking restructuring approach" to strengthen China's banking system, as well as open market efforts and reform of state-owned enterprises.
Efforts are being made to address the use of high-level corporate debt, in line with the establishment of a "market-based debt settlement framework," the IMF said.
The IMF also recalled that Beijing's tougher regulations against technology have increased policy uncertainty.
China's real estate sector has shaken financial markets and left the world's second-largest economy uncertain about its growth prospects.
Japanese government considers releasing state oil reserves to curb rising prices after US request (Video inside) Rising energy prices. According to three sources from the Japanese government told Reuters.
Reuters reports that one of the three sources said the Japanese government was looking at releasing part of the fuel in excess of the legal minimum required. Japanese law allows the release of oil reserves in the event of shortages or natural disasters, but does not provide for the release of oil reserves to curb rising oil prices.
The sources declined to be named because the plan has not yet been made public.
Japan has never released state oil reserves, as oil companies did during the Persian Gulf War in 1991 and after the 2011 earthquake and tsunami.
Joe Biden's government has made an unusual request to some of the world's largest oil producers, including China and India, to consider releasing their strategic reserves after OPEC and its allies. They largely rejected US proposals to increase oil production.
The Japanese government has 145 days of usable oil reserves by the end of September, which is more than the legal 90-day period, while the private sector has 80 days of usable oil stocks, which is beyond the legal deadline. 70 days as required by law. According to Reuters.
In terms of export volume, in the first 10 months of this year, Cambodia exported 266,765 tons of rubber, an increase of 23,639 tons, equivalent to 10% compared to the same period last year. The export of rubber wood reached 5,128 cubic meters.
The average selling price of rubber from the beginning of the year until October 2021 was $ 1,664 per ton, an increase of $ 354 per ton, equivalent to 27% compared to the same period last year.
The trial export of tires is a celebration for the Cambodian rubber market, which can be sold locally, while the new investment law exempts value-added tax (VAT), which allows rubber plantations to supply factories.
In 2020, Cambodia exported more than 350,000 tons of rubber, earning more than $ 482 million. Cambodian rubber is exported to China, Vietnam, Singapore and Malaysia.
