Ministry of Justice Establishes Working Group on Foreign Language Translation, chaired by Mr. Chin Malin
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on November 22, 2021, decided to establish a working group in charge of foreign language translation of the Ministry of Justice.
In the decision of the Ministry of Justice, obtained by Fresh News, Mr. Keut Rith appointed Mr. Chin Malin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice, as the Chairman of the Working Group, accompanied by 14 Vice-Chairmen and members.
For the team in charge of foreign language translation work is also divided into sub-groups, including:
First: Sub-Working Group on English Translation Second: Sub-Working Group on French Translation Third: Sub-Working Group on Chinese Translation
The Foreign Language Translation Working Group of the Ministry of Justice has the following roles and responsibilities:
Responsible as a translator for the Minister and leaders of the Ministry of Justice in meetings and meetings with guests and international development partners * Interpret legal documents, legal documents and / or administrative letters and press releases as needed English, French, Chinese and other foreign languages to perform other duties as determined by the Minister of Justice.
The introduction of vaccination obligations has provoked mixed reactions from individual executives, with some saying they welcomed the new rules because they removed the company's responsibilities. It is a personal responsibility. Others say the vaccination obligation has pushed employers into major disputes with their employees.
Under the new Joe Biden law, employers with 100 or more employees must ensure that their employees are "fully" vaccinated or tested negative for COVID-19 at least weekly. And wear a mask at work. However, the implementation of the new law has been suspended by the Federal Court of Appeal in response to legal challenges.
