What are the fruitful achievements of 30 years of ASEAN-China relations for member countries as well as the world?
BEIJING, Nov. 22 (Xinhua) - ASEAN-China leaders held a special summit on Monday morning to celebrate the 30th anniversary of the ASEAN-China Dialogue Partnership. The meeting was videotaped by Chinese President Xi Jinping, as well as ASEAN leaders and the ASEAN Secretary-General.
Despite the context of the Kovid 19 outbreak, this important meeting went smoothly with the joy of the 30th ASEAN Leaders' Meeting.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, President of the People's Republic of China, President of the People's Republic of China (PRC) And China further.
For the past three decades, ASEAN member countries have been warmly welcomed by Chinese leaders, who value ASEAN-China cooperation, achievements and mutual benefits, and bring peace. Stability, prosperity and sustainable socio-economic development in the region and the world.
In fact, through the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China, which will enter into force in early 2022, about 300 goods will be duty-free to the Chinese market, which is one of the reasons why ASEAN member countries strive to Openness gives each other opportunities.
China is one of the largest countries in the world with a population of billions of people. Growth must also grow together, and China will surely become the largest trading partner of ASEAN and the European Union.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave four recommendations to the ASEAN-China Special Summit. Linking ASEAN-China, promoting ASEAN-China comprehensive strategic partnership and adhering to multilateralism.
Today, China has been buying a lot of ASEAN products, making the Southeast Asian region aware of strong economic growth, as the Chinese community is pulling ASEAN closer together. Although China-ASEAN relations have been improving year by year, from the very beginning, ASEAN leaders have always adhered to a clear principle of non-alignment.
To date, China has established diplomatic relations with 180 countries around the world and has continuously promoted China's influence, attraction and inspiration on the international stage.
It is noteworthy that China has always fulfilled its promises made in the Five Principles of Coexistence, and China has established peaceful and harmonious relations with its neighbors in ASEAN as well as in the world. Continue to resolve the remnants of much of history in a way that is appropriate with those countries, without war, either verbal or bloody, with a major diplomatic solution mechanism.
At the same time, in international affairs, China adheres to the five principles of peaceful co-existence, which strives to contribute to the peaceful settlement of international disputes, promote international affairs and safeguard regional and global peace.
China has also become an important pole for the world as China, the world's second largest economy, is a model for ASEAN and is an indispensable driving force of ASEAN and the world. China is gaining more and more influence in the international community and has become a good role model for ASEAN as well as the world.
