The Cambodia National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 aims to address those challenges. The plan prioritizes investment in public infrastructure, including water supply and sanitation, and sets national targets for all cities to have access to clean water by 2025 and strengthen solid waste management.
In Bavet and Poipet, the project will support the rehabilitation of existing canals and the construction of new wastewater treatment plants, sewerage systems and landfills. In Kampot, the project will expand the sewerage network and support plans for the provincial administration to strengthen the provision of adequate services.
The project will also create a roadmap to increase revenue collection by the municipal administration, which is relying heavily on subsidies from the national administration to provide services. The roadmap will include tariff reforms to cover city operations and maintenance costs, and a plan to ensure efficient delivery of services, including an assessment of opportunities for private sector participation.
