(Kampong Cham): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on November 22, 2021, opened a training course on "Policies and Minimum Standards on the Protection of the Rights of Victims of Human Trafficking" in Kang Meas District, Kampong Cham Province.
The opening ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, with the participation of Mr. Phok Savuth, District Governor of Kang Meas District, Mr. Kong Sopnara, Advisor to the Ministry of Social Affairs, Ms. Prum Sokhon, Director of the Opposition Department Human Trafficking and Victim Integration, Mr. Un Vuthy, Project Manager, Australian Program Against Human Trafficking in Cambodia
Mr. Nhek Vannara said that human trafficking has been occurring everywhere in the form of transnational and organized crime, and that it has had a negative impact on individuals, families and communities, especially at the national level. Region and world.
At the same time, he said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been making efforts to formulate, compile, disseminate and implement policies, strategies, plans, bilateral and multilateral agreements and mechanisms aimed at combating and minimizing acts. Human trafficking and human trafficking in the national, sub-regional, regional and global.
On the morning of Monday, November 22, 2021, ASEAN-China leaders held a special summit to celebrate the 30th anniversary of the ASEAN-China Dialogue Partnership. The meeting was videotaped by Chinese President Xi Jinping, ASEAN leaders and the ASEAN Secretary-General. But the Myanmar leader was not present.
In this important meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, President of China, and other ASEAN leaders delivered keynote speeches highlighting the achievements of ASEAN-China cooperation and setting out a vision. New to strengthen relations and cooperation between ASEAN and China.
In his keynote address to the top leaders of China and ASEAN member countries, Samdech Techo stressed that ASEAN-China has established a close, fruitful, united and fruitful relationship that is mutually beneficial and contributes significantly to Bringing peace, stability, security, prosperity and sustainable socio-economic development and environment in both regions.
In addition to highlighting the importance of ASEAN-China relations, the Cambodian Prime Minister also set out four recommendations as key to improving relations and cooperation between ASEAN and China. The four recommendations include:
He encouraged China to continue to provide assistance to ASEAN, especially in support of the ASEAN Comprehensive Rehabilitation Framework and Initiatives in Response to Kovid 19. Samdech Techo continued that in the near future, Cambodia encourages China to re-open the entry-exit travel between the two ASEAN-China regions to strengthen and promote tourism, air transport services, business activities, trade. Karma and investment.
Samdech Techo expressed the hope that the above initiative will complement and support the comprehensive strategic partnership of ASEAN-China to become more meaningful based on practical cooperation that benefits each other.
Fourth, Adhering to Multilateralism: Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that ASEAN-China should continue to adhere to the multilateral system in order to promote cooperation in all fields and to address common regional and global challenges. Peacefully and based on the spirit of mutual trust and confidence aimed at maintaining peace, stability and good and fruitful cooperation in the region.
In this spirit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced his support for the initiative to celebrate the 20th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration on the Conduct of Parties in the South China Sea in 2022. He also praised the progress of the negotiations towards the completion of the Code of Conduct in the South China Sea, which is full of content and high efficiency.
