The following is the full text of the announcement made by the University of Health Sciences: Falling rice prices this year make farmers in Svay Rieng less profitable
(Svay Rieng): The rainy season rice harvest of the people in Svay Rieng province is busy, while the price of rice is slightly lower, the payment and costs make farmers less profitable.
Residents of Svay Ta Phlor village, Bassac commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province, said that today they are engaged in farming and this year's rice yield is not as good as usual because there is a lot of grass growing in the field. And even the fall in rice prices makes them resilient and at a loss. Others make little profit compared to the cost of fertilizers, oils and medicines purchased from Vietnam.
"Vietnamese traders only come up to buy rice from Cambodians at the border, and the price of rice is based on Vietnamese traders because we have no local market," he said. Dry rice, as well as wet rice, is often used by Vietnamese traders to provide fertilizer, oil, and medicine. When it is time to harvest rice, they are reimbursed to Cambodian traders.
People said that the price of rain-fed rice this year is only 700 to 800 riel per kilogram, and the yield of rice per hectare is only 2 to 3 tons, so this year's rice production is less profitable due to the cost of fuel. Fertilizers, pesticides are too expensive.
The villagers have asked the local authorities as well as the relevant departments to help the canal in Svay Taphle village, Bassac commune, Svay Chrum district to use it, because today they have dug wells to grow dry rice and buy water from Vietnam to use. He also suggested buying rice from local people so that people do not spend too much and Vietnamese traders are too busy to improve people's lives.
It should be noted that Svay Rieng province has Prey Vally international port, which is located in Kampong Ror district, Svay Rieng province. Buy to Khmer territory.
