ASEAN countries have tried to step in to resolve the issue by establishing five principles in order to mobilize all parties to the conflict in Myanmar to resolve issues peacefully and to improve the overall situation, but this goal is seen. That was not decided, so Min Aung Leng was not invited to participate in the ASEAN Summit.
Although ASEAN has facilitated Myanmar's ability to send non-political representatives to previous summits, the military-backed government has not arranged for them to be sent and has blamed ASEAN for its unconstitutional role. That is not to interfere in the internal affairs of member countries and instead follow the pressure from the West.
At the ASEAN-China Summit on Video, which marks the 30th anniversary of the establishment of the Dialogue, Chinese President Xi Jinping said in front of the nine ASEAN leaders that Beijing will not Do not coerce or put any pressure on all ASEAN countries.
"China will not seek hegemony or take advantage of itself as a big country and threaten small countries," he said. China will work with ASEAN to eliminate interference. "China is a good neighbor, good friend and good partner of ASEAN."
(Siem Reap): Three military officers were arrested by the National Gendarmerie in cooperation with the police force in connection with the illegal storage and trafficking of weapons, which authorities found 33 hidden in Chamkar Mean in Phnom Proek district. Battambang Province. The three military officers were arrested on the night of November 19 and 20, 2021.
According to local media reports, at least one person was killed, but police said the exact number was unknown at this time, while 11 adults and 12 children were also evacuated. Go to 6 local hospitals as well.
Four main factors that make entrepreneurs in the cashew sector in Tbong Khmum province successful
As a result, the team found that cashew nuts have the greatest potential for export opportunities due to the increase in output, prices and high demand in overseas markets, especially China. However, Cambodian entrepreneurs are not yet interested in investing in processing, focusing only on selling fresh cashew nuts to neighboring markets, which can not provide much value for direct exports from Cambodia. .
"The mission aims to study the management standards and successful experience of cashew export products as a basis for developing other entrepreneurial capacity development programs in the cashew crop sector, which is a potential crop," he said. High out to contribute to expanding productivity, processing and increase revenue to the national economy.
With the aim of promoting local cashew products and exporting processed cashew products directly from Cambodia to international markets, he returned to the country and started a business by setting up a cashew processing factory. Has a production line similar to his factory in Vietnam, as well as additional skills training for local workers.
He stated that the four main factors that made him successful in the past were: building a business network, technical skills, selling waste products from processing and a clear knowledge of the production line.
As a talented entrepreneur and seeing the high potential of Cambodian cashew crops, he wants to expand his production chain and business network to be bigger and stronger.
He also plans to expand the production process to 200,000 tons of fresh cashew nuts per year and especially wants to get ISO certification in the near future.
This will help expand the production and processing of Cambodian cashew products to increase exports even more.
