North Korea's reaction comes four days after the Third Committee of the United Nations General Assembly (UN) adopted a resolution on a draft resolution criticizing alleged human rights abuses by North Korean authorities. That will be officially approved at the UN General Assembly in December.
However, the DPRK Foreign Ministry rejected the resolution in a statement released by state television KCNA on Sunday, calling it a double standard and anti-Korean intent. Legs. "We will not tolerate any attempt to infringe on our sovereignty and we will continue to resolutely oppose any hostile actions against us," the statement said.
This is not the first time North Korea has been criticized for its human rights abuses. In 2014, the UN Commission of Inquiry also accused North Korean authorities of taking full responsibility. For the proliferation of systemic human rights abuses. But Pyongyang has often dismissed such allegations as a US-led plot to overthrow Kim Jong Un.
