Interior Ministry Spokesman: 44 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): At least 44 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on November 21, 2021 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on November 22.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 44 suspects, 29 were arrested in 12 criminal cases and 15 were arrested in seven drug cases.
Australian Defense Minister Peter Dutton has joined the US and Australian ambassadors in signing the agreement on Australian soil so that the three countries can share key technologies related to the use of nuclear energy in Australia. In the Navy.
This is the first technology agreement that has been publicly signed between the three countries since the announcement of the AUKUS trilateral alliance, which has been facing strong criticism from China. The deal angered China, calling it a "completely irresponsible" threat to regional stability.
Under the AUKUS agreement, Australia will receive eight state-of-the-art nuclear-powered submarines capable of stealth and long-range missions. The agreement will also share intelligence, artificial intelligence (AI) and the benefits of underwater research.
