President of the Cambodian Muslim Youth League Association of Phnom Penh led a delegation to plant 460 trees at the Islamic Center of Cambodia, Russey Chroy, Kandal Province.
(Kandal): On the morning of November 21, 2021, Mr. Rofi Osman, Member of the National Assembly and Chairman of Soy came to Phnom Penh to lead a delegation to plant 460 trees at the Islamic Center of Cambodia, Russey Chroy, Kandal Province.
The program was attended by Mr. Sen Nasi, Under Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, representing Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Sen Nazi brought a message from Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Mrs. to the people, teachers, students with all the deepest memories and emotions.
During the ceremony, Mr. Rofi Osman reminded the people to participate in the conservation of trees and continue to help plant more trees, because these trees are a source of oxygen for our lives. That will give full benefits in the next 30 years, which can be extracted to use according to actual needs.
He also thanked Mr. Say Sam Al for providing the trees for planting, which reflects the attention of the head of the Royal Government to preserve the environment in Cambodia, as well as to participate in the care of the global ecosystem. Well.
