Samdech Sangkha and Royal Council of Cambodia Present the Royal Certificate of Honor "Buddhist Disciple" to Rev. Touch Son
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Sangkha and the Royal Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia under the initiative of Mr. Dy Pov, Personal Assistant of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Deputy Commander of the Bodyguard and Family Command on November 21. This year 2021, a ceremony was held to hand over the Royal Certificate of Honor "Grand Disciple of Buddhism" to Rev. Touch Son.
Samdech Preah Reachakorn, who was invited to the ceremony to hand over the Royal Certificate to Touch Son, a Buddhist devotee, including:
1: Samdech Preah Pothivong, Honorary Doctor Am Lim Heng, Samdech Preah President of the Theresa Assembly, Cambodian Buddhist Monks, Samdech Preah Sang, First Deputy Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Chief Priest of Wat Sovan Mony (Wat Champouk K'aek).
2: Samdech Preah Odom Chakriya, Dr. Chheng Bun Chhea, Vice President of the Permanent Assembly of Cambodian Buddhist Monks and Chief Bishop of Wat Vimean Tech.
3- Samdech Preah Puth Chey Mony Khim Sorn, Chairman of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Mayor of Phnom Penh, and right-wing teacher at Wat Botum Vatey.
4: Samdech Preah Moha Arey Vong, Dr. Ly Sovanratana, Deputy Director of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Chief Bishop of Wat Mongkul One (Wat Svay Dangkum).
5. Preah Khou Thom Lon Sokunthea, Royal Council of Minorities, Deputy Chairman of the Secretariat of the Council of Priests, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Svay Chrum.
6: Preah Serey Samdech Vong Tep Phan, King of the Trinity Committee, Member of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia and right-hand teacher Sovan Mony (crow's beak).
7: Buddha Vong Ho Chheav Neath, Royal Council of the Third Class, Preah Ballat, Phnom Penh Capital Council and Director of Preah Suramrit Buddhist High School.
8- Preah Nhean Vong Saor Mony, Royal Council of the Trinity, Member of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Preah Anukon, Khan Chbar Ampov and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Komsan.
9: Preah Serey Kosal Som Sokha, Royal Council of Honor, Member of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Preah Vinay Thor, Phnom Penh Capital Council, Preah Anukon, Khan Kambol, and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Phneat Simpaly.
10: Preah Mongkul Methea Nhem Sothy, Royal Council of Honor and the right teacher of Wat Komsan.
On that occasion, Mr. Dy Pov said that because Cambodia is completely peaceful under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he was encouraged to have the opportunity to celebrate this.
Mr. Dy Pov continued that although the ceremony was held in the context of the spread of Kovid 19, but the arrangement is to implement the health rules recommended by the Royal Government, in which the Prime Minister also tried to promote vaccination. 3 doses for people across the country and get progress every day, and people really get a warm protection.
He added that the development of Cambodia to this day can not be separated from the contribution of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, because both princes are very important in helping to build and Supporting Buddhism in Cambodia. He was very grateful to both princes.
He said that the above number is a decrease compared to the same time during the Water Festival in 2020, the reason is because this year the rain continues to fall, the road is difficult to travel and so on.
At the same time, 54 tourists visited the Oral Mountains, including four foreigners, he said.
Please be informed that on the occasion of the three-day holiday of the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon Ok Ambok on November 18-20, 2021, the total number of tourists visiting Kampong Speu province 37,465 people.
Mrs. Hun Mana Presents Two Deity Houses to the Poor, the Elderly and Homeless and Donates Relics to 4 Pagodas in Takeo Province
(Takeo): Mrs. Hun Mana, Director General of Bayon Radio and Television and Director of Tevta House Program, led the team to hand over 2 more Tevta houses to the poor, the elderly and the homeless in Takeo province on the morning of the 21st. This November 2021.
During the handover ceremony, Mrs. HUN Mana brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who both Samdech always think about the well-being of the people everywhere and at all times.
1: House size 8 x 11 meters, built for the family of Sean Srey Nich, a disabled sister living in Kraing Chheu Neang village, Angkanh commune, Traing district, Takeo province. She has congenital edema (elephant foot) and lives with six family members in poverty. This house is a legacy gift of Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana Bun Seangly.
2: House size 6 x 7 meters, built for the family of Mrs. Prak Saroeun, 62 years old, living in Kansom Ok village, Prey Khla commune, Koh Andet district, Takeo province. As a gift from the legacy of Duke Prit Moha Upasika Thommanhan Vivathana Bun Seangly.
In addition to the above house donations, they also received gifts from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, including household items, various groceries and some money.
With this very happy program, Ms. HUN Mana and her team also distributed the gifts of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the grandparents, grandchildren and students who participated in the celebration of the handing over of the angel house. : Study materials, cakes, clothes, hand gel, hand soap and some money.
After the handover ceremony on the morning of the same day, she also brought a large number of the relics of the Duke, Priest Moha, Disciple Vivathana Bun Seangly, as well as food, supplies and various items to be donated to 4 pagodas. In Traing and Koh Andet districts of Takeo province.
This ceremony was held together at the construction site of Wat Sangkabor called Wat Daun Pei in Khvav commune, Takeo province. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province. On that occasion, Lok Chumteav and her team handed over the relics to the monks of 4 pagodas according to the traditional customs.
She also had a talk and brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all the monks and all the people.
She said that both Samdech always thought about the hardships of all the monks in the temples in Cambodia, and bringing the relics to offer now can alleviate the hardships of all the monks. For a while, too.
BEIJING, Nov. 18 (Xinhua) - On November 18, 2021, the Lithuanian government ignored China's strong protests and repeated warnings and allowed the Taiwanese authorities to establish a so-called "Taiwan headquarters in Lithuania". .
Please note that there is only one China in the world and the government of the People's Republic of China is the only legitimate government that can represent the whole of China. One China principle is a common concept of the international community and a basic code of international relations that is widely recognized by the international community and also a political basis for China to develop bilateral relations with Lithuania.
Due to the political basis for establishing diplomatic relations, the ambassadorial level was destroyed by Lithuania, in order to protect its sovereignty and the Basic Code of International Relations, the Chinese government reduced the diplomatic relations between China and Lithuania to the Chargé d'Affaires. Not available. The Lithuanian side needs to suffer all the consequences caused by this.
(Battambang): The relics of Rev. Srey Ly, Preah Vinay Thor, Battambang Municipality and Chief Bishop of Wat Po in Battambang City were paraded around Battambang City on the afternoon of November 21, 2021 before being laid to rest at Preah Vihear in Wat Po Knong.
Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Battambang Province, told Fresh News that the funeral procession of Preah Srey Chou To Srey Ly was attended by senators, members of the National Assembly, chairmen of provincial councils, provincial leaders and relevant departments, as well as monks of the Buddhist pagoda committee. Many more.
Please be informed that Mr. Ta Srey Ly, Preah Vinay Thor, Sub-Municipality of Battambang City and the Chief Bishop of Wat Po in Battambang City, passed away at 3:52 AM on November 16, 2021 at the Russian Hospital.
Ms. Srey Ly suffered from severe paralysis (vomiting blood) while visiting relatives in Kampong Chhnang province and was rushed to Calmette Hospital on Thursday morning, November 4, 2021. Go to a Russian hospital.
According to the Battambang Municipal Sub-District Hall, Preah Akka Chou To Srey Ly was born on August 13, 1950 in Pring Kong village, Cheung Kreav commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, to a farming family. His father's name is Srey Leng, his mother's name is Ray Moeun, and he has six siblings (three brothers and three sisters), of whom he is the fourth child.
The 14-year-old was taken by his parents to the Chief Inspector Un at Wat Sambour Meas to study. He was ordained a monk in 1967 and a monk in 1971, and in 1976 he was forced to leave the seminary by Khmer Rouge soldiers.
He rebuilt the pagoda in 1987 by Pao Chhean at the boundary of Wat Maha Kiri, Phnom Thom, and completed his training as a monk at Wat Reach Nivesanaram, also known as Wat Preah Ponlea, in the presence of Nhean Samvaro. Loy Loeung in Banteay Meanchey province in 1988.
After being venerated for three years, he went to stay at Wat Po in the presence of Chief Inspector Ouk Muth to study. As for his studies, Preah Akka Chou To Srey Ly has completed all three levels of Dharma Discipline and Pali Primary School from the beginning.
After entering the monastery for the second time, the teacher completed the discipline of the three majors again under the guidance of Pastor Som Sovann and Pastor Yin Thoeut, and also graduated from the Buddhist High School (Bakdup Pali) at 2005. In addition, the teacher also passed the exam to receive the Patimok Blessing Degree and the Vipassana Dhurak Degree.
In terms of rank and position, he was appointed as the Chief Bishop of Wat Po in 2005, the Sathapana Medal in 2008 and finally was appointed as the Preah Vinay Thor, Battambang Municipality.
